# Правила работы ИИ-агентов: polytropos-alpha

Этот документ обязателен для любого ИИ-агента, который изменяет репозиторий. Он распространяется на корень и все вложенные каталоги. **`AGENTS.md` в корне — единственный источник инструкций агентам проекта.** Дублирующие файлы правил не создавать.

## Назначение и границы проекта

- Разрабатываем **VeriNeural**: архитектурно-нейтральную импортируемую Rust-библиотеку, в которой пользователь определяет математические операции и контракты, собирает вложенные модули и архитектуры, а единый Semantic Neural IR служит источником для NVIDIA GPU-кода, Lean 4-моделей и проверяемых артефактов.
- VeriNeural **не является готовой LLM**. Не создавать обязательные Transformer/Attention/MHA/GQA, KV Cache, MoE, tokenizer, serving/API, обучение, распределённую инфраструктуру или деплой. Исследовательские архитектуры принадлежат потребителям библиотеки, а не её ядру.
- **`docs/verineural/SPEC.md`** описывает конечные требования; **`docs/verineural/ROADMAP.md`** задаёт этапы и критерии приёмки. Фактически реализованные интерфейсы проверять по исходному коду и Taskfile. Не выдавать целевую спецификацию за уже работающую функцию.
- **Этот `AGENTS.md` содержит только постоянные правила для агентов, а не журнал разработки.** Запрещено добавлять сюда хронологию этапов, коммитов, результаты тестов, benchmark, SHA-256 манифесты, отчёты о проверках и текущие временные статусы. Изменять файл лишь при изменении самих правил.

## Конечная цель проекта: сильная рекуррентная LLM с дисковой латентной памятью

Это **постоянная архитектурная цель polytropos-alpha**, а не обещание достигнутого качества. Нельзя подменять её созданием энциклопедии внутри весов или преждевременной разработкой интеграций.

- **Первый приоритет — интеллектуально сильное ядро.** Создать компактную, крайне эффективную **рекуррентную LLM**, которая самостоятельно решает сложные математические, химические и другие задачи, требующие многошаговых рассуждений, обобщения и переноса навыков. Качество решения новых задач, способность строить и проверять выводы важнее механического запоминания фактов. Исследовательский ориентир по полезным интеллектуальным способностям — **Qwen3.8 27B**; сопоставимость не заявлять без отдельных воспроизводимых тестов.
- **Размер весов ядра — целевые 3–4 GB.** Это верхний целевой диапазон *хранимых параметров модели*, без дисковой латентной памяти. Основная аппаратная граница — **одна NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 с 8 GB VRAM**, на которой должно быть возможно **обучение**, а не только inference. Размер весов не равен полному расходу VRAM: отдельно учитывать пик активаций, градиентов, состояний оптимизатора, временных буферов и CUDA. Никаких фиктивных заявлений о выполнимости обучения без замеров.
- **Крайне высокая обучаемость.** Приоритетны sample efficiency, стабильность сложных рассуждений, скорость обучения, пропускная способность и время до заданного качества при реальном аппаратном бюджете. Сравнения проводить на одинаковых задачах и бюджетах данных/вычислений, а не только по скорости одного CUDA kernel.
- **Минимум универсального знания внутри ядра.** Ядро должно сохранять базовые понятия, математические/логические навыки, способы решения задач, обобщающие связи и способность адресовать нужные сведения. Большой объём частных фактов, деталей и специализированных знаний должен быть **вынесен во внешнюю латентную память**, а не обязательно закодирован в весах.
- **Обучаемое разделение знаний, а не ручная разметка.** **Во время обучения сама модель должна определять**, какие сведения критично оставить в весах, а какие сохранить или обновить во внешней памяти. Целевой ориентир — **около 20% базовых/связующих знаний в ядре и 80% расширяемых знаний во внешней памяти**. Это доли *полезного содержания/функций памяти*, а **не** строгая доля параметров, байтов, обучающих токенов или заранее доказанный коэффициент. Нужны измеримые критерии удержания навыков, качества извлечения, ошибок переноса и потери информации.
- **Связность важнее простого разбиения 20/80.** Оставшиеся в ядре общие знания должны быть достаточными для понимания задачи, выбора нужной области памяти, извлечения релевантных подробностей, объединения нескольких фрагментов и вывода ответа. Нельзя получить «умную» модель простым удалением 80% данных без механизма обучения извлечению и интеграции.
- **Внешняя латентная память — на диске, не в VRAM.** Хранить расширяемые иерархические представления и факты в дисковом хранилище без требования целиком загружать, копировать или постоянно кешировать эту базу на GPU. **В VRAM находится активная модель и необходимое для её вычислений ограниченное рабочее состояние**, но не вся внешняя база знаний. При запросе поднимать с диска **только адресованные регионы** в ограниченные CPU/передаточные буферы и предоставлять модели лишь необходимое содержимое/представление в рамках её входа и вычислений. Не маскировать массовую загрузку внешней базы «памятью модели».
- **Масштабируемая и обучаемая дисковая память.** Её ёмкость **не должна ограничиваться объёмом VRAM или размером весов**; она должна расширяться по мере накопления знаний и допускать эффективные добавление, обновление, организацию и поиск. «Неограниченная» здесь означает отсутствие *архитектурного фиксированного лимита*, но реальная ёмкость, I/O, скорость поиска и место на диске конечны и измеряются отдельно.
- **Иерархическая адресация и выбор глубины.** Кластеризовать знания по областям и уровням детализации. Рекуррентное ядро само выбирает регион, ветвь и нужную глубину, при необходимости уточняя запрос: например, «базы данных» (уровень 0) → «PostgreSQL» (1) → «SQL» → «как работает SELECT» (уровень *x*). Не загружать все кластеры в контекст и не закреплять постоянную глубину поиска.
- **Текущий этап без внешних адаптеров.** Не планировать и не реализовывать пока сетевые коннекторы, web-поиск, Wiki API и другие внешние сервисные адаптеры. Источник знаний на данном этапе — **собственная локальная дисковая латентная память**, с которой ядро учится работать непосредственно. К интеграциям возвращаться только после сильного базового reasoning и подтверждённого обучаемого распределения знаний.
- **Вращающиеся матрицы** исследуются как способ уменьшения памяти параметров ориентировочно **в 10–100 раз** с максимально возможным сохранением качества, устойчивости и скорости обучения. Это гипотеза, а не достигнутый результат: проверять число весов, размер checkpoint, цену вычислений и деградацию на серьёзных задачах.
- **Приёмка по этапам:** (1) способность ядра решать сложные задачи без внешней памяти; (2) обучаемое решение «оставить внутри / выгрузить на диск» и сохранение качества рассуждений; (3) адресное и иерархическое извлечение из дисковой памяти с измеренными задержками/ошибками; (4) обучение на RTX 5060 8 GB и проверка предела 3–4 GB весов; (5) сравнение с крупной эталонной моделью. Проверять отдельно качество **без памяти и с памятью**, а также вклад памяти, не приписывая внешние факты внутренним параметрам.

**Граница ответственности сохраняется:** `crates/verineural/` предоставляет архитектурно-нейтральные примитивы, состояние, контракты, Semantic IR, GPU lowering и Lean-верификацию. Конкретные рекуррентные блоки LLM, алгоритм обучаемой маршрутизации знаний, дисковая латентная память и обучение принадлежат **`labs/` как потребителям публичного API**. Если не хватает общего примитива, сначала расширять универсальную библиотеку, не встраивая в неё готовую предметную LLM.

## Rust workspace, Nix и Task

1. **Rust только через Cargo workspaces.** Корневой `Cargo.toml` задаёт workspace. Переиспользуемые библиотечные/инструментальные компоненты добавлять в `crates/`; конкретные исследовательские consumer-архитектуры допускаются в `labs/<architecture-name>-<version>/` и при появлении Rust package включаются в тот же workspace. Не переносить lab-specific нейросеть в `crates/verineural/`. Зависимости должны быть явными; не создавать циклов.
2. **В корне обязателен `flake.nix`.** Все необходимые инструменты разработки и генерации артефактов (Rust, LLVM/NVPTX, Lean 4, CUDA toolkit, Task и другие при расширении проекта) должны быть описаны в Nix. При добавлении обязательной зависимости актуализировать `flake.nix`. Драйвер NVIDIA остаётся системной предпосылкой, а не зависимостью, автоматически устанавливаемой в devShell.
3. **Команды определять и документировать в корневом `Taskfile.yml` (go-task).** Для сборки, форматирования, проверки, тестов, генерации кода и сертификатов использовать `task <имя>`; не вводить параллельный набор Makefile, shell-скриптов и разрозненных инструкций. `task check` обязан сначала выполнять `task prepare` (Rust autoformat), затем `cargo check`; при успешной проверке он может автоматически коммитить и отправлять **только новые изменения форматирования отслеживаемых Rust-файлов** в `dev`, если до запуска не было изменений `.rs` или staged-файлов и `HEAD` совпадает с `origin/dev`. Существующие пользовательские правки не отправлять автоматически.
4. **По умолчанию ИИ-агент НЕ запускает большинство команд**: `task build`, `task check`, `task test`, `task clippy`, `task doc`, тяжёлые `nix develop`/`nix flake check` и GPU-прогоны. Пользователь самостоятельно тестирует и собирает проект локально. Выполнять такие команды только по его **явному запросу**. Допустимы лёгкое чтение файлов и локальные статические проверки структуры; о непроверенном состоянии сообщать прямо.
5. Не устанавливать инструменты глобально, не обходить Nix непрозрачными установщиками, не изменять пользовательское окружение.
6. `Cargo.lock` и `flake.lock` при их появлении сохранять для воспроизводимости; не игнорировать. Не утверждать, что окружение зафиксировано, пока lock-файл отсутствует.

## Обязательное использование VeriNeural в лабораториях

- **При разработке нейросети или исследовательской архитектуры в `labs/` обязательно использовать публичный API библиотеки VeriNeural** для определения вычислительных примитивов, контрактов, модулей, связей, Semantic Neural IR, генерации NVIDIA GPU-кода и Lean-моделей/доказательств в пределах поддерживаемого профиля. Лаборатория должна быть потребителем библиотеки, а не параллельной реализацией её вычислительного и верификационного стека.
- **Если для лабораторной архитектуры не хватает возможностей VeriNeural, сначала расширить библиотеку универсальными, архитектурно-нейтральными строительными блоками в `crates/verineural/`**, а не реализацией требуемого конечного компонента. Разрабатывать минимально необходимые переиспользуемые примитивы, операции над тензорами и состоянием, интерфейсы композиции и контракты; при необходимости доводить их через Semantic Neural IR до поддерживаемых GPU/Lean backend-путей, тестов и явно ограниченных доказательств. Затем **собирать специализированный компонент из этих примитивов внутри `labs/`**. Не обходить ограничения библиотеки отдельными лабораторными CUDA kernels, генераторами Lean, скрытыми операциями или собственным несовместимым IR.
- **Граница абстракции обязательна:** VeriNeural предоставляет элементарные и составляемые механизмы, пригодные для разных архитектур, но **не содержит готовых предметно-специфичных компонентов**, даже если они нужны текущей лаборатории. Например, **KV-кэш реализуется только в лаборатории**; библиотека при необходимости расширяется общими примитивами хранения и обновления состояния, индексного чтения/записи, работы с формами и зависимостями, из которых потребитель может построить KV-кэш, другие виды памяти или совершенно иной алгоритм. Нельзя добавлять в ядро типы, API или семантику, жёстко завязанные на ключи/значения Attention, KV-кэш либо другую частную модель.
- В `labs/` оставлять специфичные для эксперимента определения архитектуры, специализированные составные компоненты, их композицию, конфигурацию, данные, сценарии запуска, независимые тестовые оракулы и исследовательские результаты. **Не переносить готовую конкретную нейросеть или её прикладные блоки в ядро VeriNeural**: расширять только универсальный набор операций и контрактов, достаточный, чтобы потребитель сам собрал нужный сложный компонент.
- При отсутствии доказанного lowering или математической гарантии расширять поддерживаемый профиль с отдельной проверкой либо **явно завершать неподдерживаемый этап ошибкой**. Не выдавать лабораторный обходной путь, численное совпадение или Lean-доказательство идеальной модели за сертификацию NVIDIA FP32/SASS.

## Git: разработка только в `dev`

- **Единственная рабочая ветка — `dev`.** Все изменения исходников, тестов и документации коммитить непосредственно в неё. **Не создавать** `agent/*`, `feature/*`, временные или отдельные ветки под исправления и этапы. Не спамить ветками.
- **Не коммитить напрямую в `main`.** `main` — ветка стабильной интеграции. Перенос изменений из `dev` в `main` возможен **только по явному запросу пользователя** и только fast-forward с проверкой предка; никакого автоматического продвижения.
- Перед записью в `dev` проверять её актуальный HEAD и ancestry нового коммита. При расхождении сначала синхронизироваться без merge-коммитов; не переписывать историю. При GitHub API обновлять `refs/heads/dev` исключительно с `force=false`, `expected_sha` и повторной проверкой HEAD.
- **Никаких pull request**, draft PR, PR merge, squash merge, rebase merge, merge-коммитов, force push и принудительных перемещений refs. Не удалять чужие или существующие ветки без явного разрешения пользователя.
- После изменения кратко сообщать SHA коммита в `dev`, сущность изменений и реальный статус проверок, не записывая эти сведения в `AGENTS.md`.

## Запрет на самовольную инфраструктуру

**Без предварительного явного разрешения пользователя ЗАПРЕЩЕНО добавлять или изменять:**
- CI/CD, GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/`), другие пайплайны;
- автоматические pre-commit hooks, git hooks, ботов, cron/scheduled tasks;
- контейнеризацию, удалённые среды, деплой, release automation, новые внешние сервисы;
- вспомогательную инфраструктуру проверки, мониторинга и публикации ради самой инфраструктуры.

Не подменять этот запрет аргументом «так принято в индустрии». Если инфраструктура действительно понадобится, сначала объяснить её цель и попросить разрешение.

## Принципы разработки (обязательны)

- **KISS**: самая простая реализация, которая даёт требуемую функциональность. Никаких фреймворков и слоёв абстракции «на вырост».
- **DRY**: один источник правды для контрактов, семантики и конфигурации; не дублировать одну и ту же математическую логику между backend'ами.
- **Pragmatic Engineering**: оптимизировать полезный результат, понятность и время реализации; конкретный работающий вертикальный срез ценнее теоретически идеального, но незавершённого дизайна.
- **Risk-based Verification**: усилия на доказательства направлять туда, где ошибка наиболее опасна: формы, границы индексов, память, численная семантика, корректность трансформаций и отчёт о гарантии.
- **Modular Verification**: небольшие проверяемые примитивы, локальные контракты, повторно используемые леммы и композиция доказательств. Не начинать с монолитного доказательства всей нейросети; затем реализовать численно осведомлённую композицию контрактов.

## Темп работы и масштаб изменений

- Проект **любительский**. Планировать **крупные содержательные этапы** с чётким работающим артефактом и критерием завершения. Не дробить одну фичу на десятки мелких коммитов/«рефакторингов ради рефакторинга» и не расходовать три дня на косметику.
- Предпочитать end-to-end вертикальные срезы: пользовательский Rust API → IR → GPU либо Lean → явный отчёт. Не создавать неподключённые заготовки.
- При выборе между широтой поддержки и глубиной гарантий сужать поддерживаемое подмножество, а не преувеличивать корректность.
- Новые зависимости, функции и модули добавлять по мере фактической необходимости. Не опережать этапы дорожной карты без конкретного запроса.

## Обязательная модель CUDA-исполнения: CUDA Graph + Kernel Fusion

- **Строго запрещены CUDA Legacy Streams**: `CU_STREAM_LEGACY`, NULL/default stream (`stream = 0`) в CUDA runtime/Driver API, а также неявный fallback на legacy/per-thread default streams. Не передавать `nullptr` / `ptr::null_mut()` вместо потока при запуске kernels, копировании или синхронизации.
- **Все вычислительные kernels исполнять через CUDA Graph**, построенный из зависимостей Semantic Neural IR: захват на явно созданном `CU_STREAM_NON_BLOCKING` либо явное построение kernel-узлов графа. Сборка графа, его инстанцирование и `cuGraphLaunch` должны использовать реальные CUDA Graph API. Запуск отдельного kernel через `cuLaunchKernel` вне построения CUDA Graph запрещён.
- **Kernel Fusion является основным механизмом GPU-оптимизации**: объединять совместимые операции, не нарушая потребителей IR, зависимостей, контрактов, порядка вычислений и FP32-политики. Нельзя навязывать fusion любому произвольному подграфу без проверки предпосылок.
- Передача данных и синхронизация выполняются на **явном non-blocking stream**, без legacy/default-stream-семантики. Для async transfer использовать корректно живущую до завершения операции закреплённую host-memory (pinned memory).
- Если требуемые CUDA Graph API / `CU_STREAM_NON_BLOCKING` недоступны, **fail-closed**, без старого пути прямых запусков и без запуска на legacy stream. Зависимости CUDA Graph должны определяться IR и профилем исполнения, а не готовой архитектурой Transformer.
- Lean-доказательство математической fusion-леммы не означает доказательства CUDA Graph, FP32, PTX, JIT или исполнения аппаратурой. Статус этих гарантий всегда отражается отдельно.

## Формальная верификация и честность отчётов

- Источник математических требований — явный Rust-контракт или семантика доверенного примитива; генератор не придумывает корректность новой математики.
- В certified-режиме запрещены `sorry`, `admit`, непроверенные аксиомы и неподтверждённые допущения. Недоказанная цель означает провал нужного уровня сертификации.
- Точно различать: **формально доказано в Lean**, **численно проверено запуском**, **принято как доверенное предположение (TCB)**, **не поддерживается/не доказано**.
- Нельзя утверждать, что доказано исполнение машинного кода, если не доказана связь GPU IR → LLVM IR → PTX → SASS/железо; явно описывать доверенную границу.
- Strict FP32 требует явной обработки rounding, FMA, FTZ/денормалов, NaN/Infinity, signed zero и порядка редукции. Fast-math не включать неявно.
- Экспериментальные GPU-оптимизации отделять от доказанно эквивалентных преобразований. Лемма Lean об идеальной `Int`-семантике не доказывает эквивалентность LLVM/PTX/FP32 и не разрешает выдавать фьюжн за сертифицированную численную оптимизацию.
- Изменения оптимизирующих проходов в certified-режиме допустимы только с правилом сохранения семантики или сертифицированной оценкой ошибки.
- Нейросетевые свойства обучения, сходимости и качества не следует автоматически из корректности forward pass.
- **Теорема о локальном блоке не равна теореме о всей архитектуре.** Глобальное свойство требует формальной постановки, проверенных условий применения локальных лемм и отдельной композиционной проверки. Формирование Lean-файла и численная валидация GPU не доказывают произвольный алгоритм, IEEE-754 или машинный код.

## Порядок работы агента

1. Читать корневой `AGENTS.md`, `docs/verineural/SPEC.md` и `docs/verineural/ROADMAP.md` перед изменениями VeriNeural.
2. Сначала проверять текущую структуру и этап. Делать только нужный для задачи вертикальный срез; не трогать архитектуру раньше времени.
3. Обновлять документацию и Taskfile только при реальном изменении API/команд.
4. По завершении кратко перечислять изменённые файлы, реализованные и **нереализованные** возможности и факт запуска/незапуска тестов.
5. Не добавлять CI или инфраструктуру, не запускать массовые проверки без прямой санкции пользователя.

FILE	Cargo.toml
[workspace]
members = [
    "crates/verineural",
    "labs/coupled-field-0.1.0",
    "labs/xor-0.1.0",
    "labs/consumer-acceptance-0.1.0",
    "labs/rotating-matrices-0.1.0",
    "labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0",
]
resolver = "3"

[workspace.package]
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2024"
rust-version = "1.85"

FILE	README.md
# polytropos-alpha

Исследовательский Rust-проект для разработки **интеллектуально сильной, компактной рекуррентной LLM**. Сначала ядро должно научиться самостоятельно решать сложные **математические, химические и логические задачи**. Затем во время обучения оно должно научиться решать, какие базовые знания и навыки оставить в параметрах, а какие сохранять во **внешней иерархической латентной памяти на диске**.

**Целевые ограничения (пока не достигнуты):** уровень полезных интеллектуальных возможностей выбранного ориентира Qwen3.8 27B, **3–4 GB весов ядра**, реальное обучение на **одной RTX 5060 с 8 GB VRAM**, высокая скорость и эффективность обучения. Вращающиеся матрицы исследуются как способ сжатия параметров в **10–100 раз** при контролируемой потере качества. Целевые характеристики должны быть подтверждены экспериментами.

**Принцип разделения знаний:** ориентир **20% базовых и связующих знаний в ядре / 80% расширяемых сведений во внешней памяти**. Это не жёсткое соотношение байтов или параметров: ядро учится сохранять способности рассуждать и извлекать нужные знания. Дисковая память может расти независимо от VRAM, должна поддерживать эффективное обучение/обновление и **не загружаться в GPU целиком**. Модель запрашивает только нужные иерархические регионы и выбирает глубину погружения, например «базы данных → PostgreSQL → SQL → SELECT». В VRAM помещаются веса, обязательные вычислительные состояния и лишь ограниченное представление запрошенных данных. **Сетевые и Wiki-адаптеры пока исключены из текущего этапа.**

## Два уровня проекта

**VeriNeural** (`crates/verineural/`) — независимый от архитектуры конструктор вычислений. Пользователь определяет Rust-примитивы, операции и контракты, объединяет их в Semantic Neural IR и получает:

- LLVM NVPTX/PTX и исполнение через **CUDA Graph** на явном non-blocking stream;
- Lean 4-модели и проверку поддерживаемых математических свойств;
- артефакты перевода, проверки ограничений памяти, композиции и доверенных предположений.

VeriNeural **не поставляет готовые LLM, Transformer/Attention, KV cache или обучающий стек конкретной модели**. Они принадлежат потребительским архитектурам в `labs/` и должны собираться из публичного API. Дисковая латентная память и её обучаемая маршрутизация также относятся к конкретной LLM, а не к готовым компонентам библиотеки. Lean-доказательства математической модели не являются доказательствами CUDA JIT/SASS или успешности обучения.

## Структура

| Каталог | Назначение |
| --- | --- |
| `crates/verineural/` | Компонуемые Rust API, Semantic IR, autodiff, компиляция GPU, Lean, проверки |
| `lean/VeriNeural/` | Исходники проверяемых Lean-теорем |
| `labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/` | Исследование рекуррентной языковой модели EMA4/Torus16/Role-Delta; экспериментальная v0.2 |
| `labs/rotating-matrices-0.1.0/` | Исследование вращающихся матриц, маршрутизации, сохранённые результаты |
| `labs/xor-0.1.0/`, `labs/coupled-field-0.1.0/` | Отдельные проверяемые потребители библиотеки |
| `labs/consumer-acceptance-0.1.0/` | Приёмочные сценарии публичного API |
| `docs/verineural/` | Полная спецификация, дорожная карта, границы доказательств |

Основные документы: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) (обязательные правила и конечные критерии), [SPEC.md](docs/verineural/SPEC.md) (целевая библиотека), [ROADMAP.md](docs/verineural/ROADMAP.md) (реализованное и планы), [AUTO_BUILD.md](docs/verineural/AUTO_BUILD.md) (сертифицируемая сборка), [Torus16 v0.2 transition](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/V0.2_TRANSITION.md) и [журнал экспериментов](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/EXPERIMENT_RESULTS.md).

## Среда и основные команды

Инструменты Rust, LLVM NVPTX, CUDA toolkit, Lean 4 и Task определены в `flake.nix`. NVIDIA Driver/GPU требуются на хосте для аппаратных проверок.

```sh
nix develop
task prepare           # cargo fmt и проверка форматирования
task check             # Rust workspace (см. правило auto-format в AGENTS.md)
task test              # CPU/обычные Rust-тесты
task clippy
```

`repospool` доступен в закреплённом Nix devShell. Команда `task prepare` сначала выполняет `repospool generate .`, создавая локальный `.repospool` со снимком **закоммиченного `HEAD`** (незакоммиченные изменения не входят), затем форматирует Rust. Все основные лабораторные команды Taskfile проходят эту подготовку; `task build`, `task clippy` и `task doc` также обновляют снимок без запуска автоформатирования. Если RepoSpool завершится ошибкой, последующая лабораторная команда не запустится. Снимок является генерируемым файлом и игнорируется Git; ручной запуск: `task repospool-generate`.

Специализированные команды из единого [Taskfile.yml](Taskfile.yml):

```sh
task proof-stage3
task verify-certified-build
task lab-xor && task verify-lab-xor
task lab-stage9 && task verify-lab-stage9
task verify-gpu-temporal-bptt
task verify-gpu-batch-transfers
task test-lab-torus16-ema4-checkpoint
```

Задачи `lab-xor` и `lab-stage9` **создают проверяемые файлы в своих лабораториях** (DOT/PNG, Lean, LLVM/PTX, manifests, output bits). Эти файлы считаются **генерируемыми выходами**, в Git не хранятся. Оффлайн `verify-lab-xor` / `verify-lab-stage9` запускают **после** генерации актуального набора. Исходники и обязательства доказательств сохраняются в Rust и Lean.

Для Torus16 сначала изучить [README лаборатории](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/README.md) и [план перехода v0.2](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/V0.2_TRANSITION.md). **Полный BPTT16 GPU JIT намеренно заблокирован по умолчанию:** большой граф с 63 707 CUDA kernels зависал на загрузке драйверного модуля без нагрузки GPU. `task benchmark-torus16-v02-bptt16` исторически называется benchmark, но сейчас выполняет только безопасный **CPU preflight** без LLVM/CUDA JIT и обучения. Не считать его показателем качества модели.

## Лёгкий CI (без GPU)

GitHub Actions при push в `dev` и `main` генерирует и проверяет `.repospool`,
загружает резервный snapshot в Actions Artifacts на 7 дней, затем запускает
только `cargo test --locked -p verineural --lib --tests`. Тесты с `#[ignore]`
(требующие GPU/Lean/LLVM/Graphviz) не запускаются. **Лабораторные crates
и их задачи через CI не запускаются.** Полная GPU/Lean-приёмка остаётся локальной.

После успешных тестов workflow **коммитит `.repospool` в `dev`** отдельным
fast-forward коммитом от `github-actions[bot]` без force-push; `main` остаётся
только для чтения и тестов. Снимок содержит исходное состояние предыдущего
коммита: сам `.repospool` исключён из индекса RepoSpool, а его запись в Git
создаёт новый SHA, поэтому он не может ссылаться на собственный Git-коммит.
Следующие `task repospool-generate` / `task prepare` учитывают этот случай и
не изменяют содержимое снимка на уже опубликованном artifact-only HEAD.
Публикация выполняется только при успешной генерации, верификации и CPU-тестах;
при конкурентном push обычный fast-forward `git push` отклонит устаревший снимок.

## Правила результатов и верификации

- **Не путать** математические Lean-теоремы, структурный PTX audit, численную CUDA-проверку и неподтверждённую корректность аппаратного исполнения.
- Сообщать размер весов **отдельно** от объёма дисковой латентной памяти; измерять пик VRAM (включая состояния оптимизатора), задержки адресного чтения с диска, время компиляции/JIT, training throughput и время до качества.
- В лабораториях отделять train, validation и test; не выбирать архитектуру по зарезервированному test, сравнивать одинаковый объём обучения и учитывать различия числа optimizer updates.
- Не запускать тяжёлые GPU/Lean/Cargo задачи агентом без явного указания. Пользователь выполняет их на своей RTX 5060 и предоставляет логи.
- Рабочая ветка — только `dev`. `main` не обновляется без прямого поручения. Запрещены самовольные CI/CD и инфраструктурные сервисы.

Текущий репозиторий содержит **исследовательские реализации и проверяемые подмножества**, а не завершённую рекуррентную LLM с 3–4 GB весов и обучаемой дисковой памятью. Историю измерений хранить в профильных документах лабораторий, не раздувать корневой README очередными журналами запуска.

FILE	Taskfile.yml
version: '3'

# Local developer commands. AI agents must not execute build/test commands
# by default; see AGENTS.md. GitHub Actions checks CPU tests and publishes RepoSpool in dev.
tasks:
  default:
    desc: Show available tasks
    cmds:
      - task --list

  fmt:
    desc: Format the entire Rust workspace (developer-run)
    cmds:
      - cargo fmt --all

  repospool-generate:
    desc: Refresh the source snapshot, using its source parent after a CI artifact-only commit
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source_rev=HEAD
        if [ "$(git diff-tree --no-commit-id --name-only -r HEAD)" = ".repospool" ]; then
          source_rev=HEAD^
        fi
        repospool generate . --rev "$source_rev"

  # Safe local preflight: refresh RepoSpool, then format workspace sources.
  # Every lab generation/replay and workspace/lab test task depends on this.
  prepare:
    desc: Refresh committed-source snapshot and format Rust before laboratory runs and tests
    cmds:
      - task: repospool-generate
      - task: fmt
      - cargo fmt --all -- --check

  check:
    desc: Autoformat Rust, type-check the workspace, and publish rustfmt-only changes safely on dev
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        # Snapshot dirty source/index state before running rustfmt. Existing
        # developer edits must never become an automatic formatting commit.
        prior_rust="$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- '*.rs')"
        prior_index="$(git diff --cached --name-only)"
        task prepare
        cargo check --workspace --all-targets
        if git diff --quiet HEAD -- '*.rs'; then
          echo "check: no tracked Rust changes to publish."
          exit 0
        fi
        if [ -n "$prior_rust" ] || [ -n "$prior_index" ]; then
          echo "check: existing Rust edits or staged changes; formatted and checked, but not auto-pushing user work." >&2
          exit 0
        fi
        branch="$(git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD)" || {
          echo "check: detached HEAD; skipping automatic push." >&2
          exit 0
        }
        if [ "$branch" != "dev" ]; then
          echo "check: only dev allows automatic formatting commits (current: $branch)." >&2
          exit 0
        fi
        git diff --check
        git remote get-url origin >/dev/null
        git fetch --quiet origin dev
        remote_head="$(git rev-parse --verify refs/remotes/origin/dev)"
        if [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" != "$remote_head" ]; then
          echo "check: dev differs from origin/dev; refusing to auto-push." >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        # Tracked .rs files only. Untracked sources and existing staged work
        # are never silently added to a formatting commit.
        git add -u -- '*.rs'
        if git diff --cached --quiet; then
          echo "check: no tracked Rust changes to commit."
          exit 0
        fi
        git commit -m "style(verineural): apply cargo fmt"
        git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/dev

  build:
    desc: Build the Rust workspace (developer-run)
    deps: [repospool-generate]
    cmds:
      - cargo build --workspace

  test:
    desc: Run workspace tests (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test --workspace

  clippy:
    desc: Lint the workspace (developer-run)
    deps: [repospool-generate]
    cmds:
      - cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings

  doc:
    desc: Build Rust documentation locally (developer-run)
    deps: [repospool-generate]
    cmds:
      - cargo doc --workspace --no-deps

  example-stage2:
    desc: Run the stage-2 Semantic Neural IR example (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage2_graph

  proof-stage3:
    desc: Generate and check the stage-3 Lean 4 proof (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage3_proof

  proof-scan-invariant:
    desc: Check consumer-owned ideal-Int step claims and the bounded recurrent invariant with Lean
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example scan_invariant

  verify-inductive-invariant:
    desc: Check P1 arbitrary-horizon ideal-Int state invariant from one reusable consumer transition
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test inductive_invariant
      - cargo test -p verineural --test inductive_invariant -- --ignored

  verify-reusable-module-proof:
    desc: Check single/multi-output reusable definitions, per-instance obligations and global composition in Lean
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test reusable_module_definition
      - cargo test -p verineural --test reusable_module_definition -- --ignored

  auto-architecture:
    desc: Generate and audit all ideal-Int architecture/goal proofs and lower each supported output to NVPTX
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example auto_architecture

  verify-auto-architecture:
    desc: Offline replay of current auto-build Semantic IR, SHA-256 manifest, Lean kernel/axioms and LLVM/PTX translation
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example auto_architecture -- --verify

  proof-gated-select:
    desc: Check generic positive mask and conditional select with bounded Lean state invariant (GPU fail-closed)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example gated_select

  symbolic-shapes:
    desc: Verify two consumer symbolic-shape specializations with Lean and LLVM NVPTX (no GPU execution)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example symbolic_shapes

  verify-storage-semantics:
    desc: Check P1/P10 contiguous strides, reshape aliases and canonical storage identity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test storage_semantics
      - cargo test -p verineural --test tensor_indexing

  gpu-multi-output:
    desc: Check one Lean model and capture/replay a shared four-output NVIDIA CUDA Graph
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example multi_output_gpu

  verify-gpu-capabilities:
    desc: Check P1/P12 kernel-memory-translation coverage, fusion preconditions and audited Lean memory obligations
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_capability
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_capability -- --ignored
      - cargo test -p verineural --test auto_build

  gpu-state-replay:
    desc: GPU acceptance for named stateful ModelExecution, five D2D feedback steps and exact FP32 results
    deps:
      - prepare
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stateful_model_gpu

  verify-gpu-feedback-runtime:
    desc: NVIDIA regressions for raw state feedback readiness, alias snapshots and named stateful replay
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_feedback -- --ignored --nocapture
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stateful_model_gpu

  gpu-stage4:
    desc: Lower IR to PTX and run the CUDA stage-4 example (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage4_gpu

  cert-stage5:
    desc: Run Lean, CUDA and the Stage 5 evidence bundle (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage5_cert

  verify-stage5:
    desc: Recheck Stage 5 SHA-256 manifest and Lean source (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage5_verify

  neural-stage6:
    desc: Execute Stage 6 residual FFN via Lean + CUDA and produce an evidence bundle (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage6_ffn

  gpu-stage7:
    desc: Validate fusion and benchmark reusable CUDA Graph replay with CUDA events (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage7_fusion

  verify-gpu-stage7:
    desc: Replay Stage 7 SHA-256 manifests and Lean proof checks without GPU execution (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage7_fusion -- --verify

  gpu-stage7-bench:
    desc: Benchmark four CUDA Graph workload sizes, input rebinding, and FP32 bitwise checks (developer-run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage7_benchmark --release

  numeric-stage8:
    desc: Check Stage 8 Lean/RNE and per-kernel Numeric Translation Validation before CUDA Graph execution
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage8_exact

  verify-numeric-stage8:
    desc: Offline verify Stage 8 Lean, all per-kernel LLVM/PTX translation reports, FP32 bits and SHA-256
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --example stage8_exact -- --verify

  verify-numeric-branch:
    desc: Check P1 stable PositiveMask/SelectPositive RNE branch inheritance and fail-closed zero crossing
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test numeric_branch
      - cargo test -p verineural --test numeric_branch -- --ignored

  verify-numeric-state:
    desc: Check P1 fixed-horizon recurrent RNE contract carry and invariant state q scale
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test numeric_state
      - cargo test -p verineural --test numeric_state -- --ignored

  lab-stage9:
    desc: Build Stage 9 independent coupled-field research lab, Lean, CUDA Graph and DOT/PNG evidence
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p coupled-field-lab --example stage9_architecture

  verify-lab-stage9:
    desc: Offline reconstruct Stage 9 Semantic IR/DOT and check Lean, LLVM/PTX and SHA-256
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p coupled-field-lab --example stage9_architecture -- --verify

  lab-xor:
    desc: Check XOR MLP truth table via VeriNeural, Lean, NVPTX and CUDA Graph; write lab evidence
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p xor-lab --example xor_lab -- {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  verify-lab-xor:
    desc: Recheck XOR lab artifacts, Lean, translation and hashes without GPU
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p xor-lab --example xor_lab -- --verify {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  certified-build:
    desc: Stage 10 certified build dispatcher for --manifest-path selected consumer (no GPU launch)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --bin cargo-verineural -- build --certified {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  verify-certified-build:
    desc: Stage 10 offline certified replay using --manifest-path and optional external pin
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p verineural --bin cargo-verineural -- verify --certified {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  verify-certified-stage10:
    desc: Tool-dependent Stage 10 acceptance for true/false Lean goals, identity and tamper
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test certified_build -- --ignored

  certified-xor:
    desc: Stage 10 proof-gated certified model build for XOR (CPU tools only, no GPU run)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p xor-lab --example xor_certified -- {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  verify-certified-xor:
    desc: Offline Stage 10 replay for XOR (optional --pinned-sha256 <digest>)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p xor-lab --example xor_certified -- --verify {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  certified-coupled:
    desc: Stage 10 proof-gated certified model build for CoupledField (no GPU execution)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p coupled-field-lab --example coupled_field_certified -- {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  verify-certified-coupled:
    desc: Offline Stage 10 replay for CoupledField (optional --pinned-sha256 <digest>)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p coupled-field-lab --example coupled_field_certified -- --verify {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  test-lab-xor:
    desc: Run CPU-only XOR consumer tests including one global proof and GPU compilation planning
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p xor-lab --all-targets

  verify-relational-predicates:
    desc: Lean kernel and axiom audit acceptance for true and deliberately false consumer relational claims
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test relational_predicates -- --ignored

  verify-pointwise-primitive:
    desc: Kernel-check independent user-defined atomic pointwise semantics and contracts
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test pointwise_primitive -- --ignored

  p0-acceptance:
    desc: Verify VN-P01..P06 supported-scope contracts, external primitive, composition and certified Lean trust boundary
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test relational_predicates
      - cargo test -p verineural --test pointwise_primitive
      - cargo test -p verineural --test auto_build
      - cargo test -p verineural --test relational_predicates -- --ignored
      - cargo test -p verineural --test pointwise_primitive -- --ignored
      - cargo run -p verineural --example auto_architecture
      - cargo run -p verineural --example auto_architecture -- --verify
      - cargo test -p verineural --test certified_build -- --ignored

  verify-tensor-reductions:
    desc: Lean-check axis-sum ideal semantics, nonnegative fold, and consumer contracts
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test tensor_reductions -- --ignored

  verify-tensor-slice:
    desc: Check P1 static axis slice host/IR semantics, Lean preservation and explicit GPU fail-closed
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test tensor_slice
      - cargo test -p verineural --test tensor_slice -- --ignored

  p2-consumers:
    desc: Exercise three independent P2 consumer architectures, positive/negative contracts and honest GPU profiles
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural-consumer-acceptance --all-targets

  verify-p2-consumers:
    desc: Kernel-check P2 nested, bounded recurrent, custom primitive, tensor-heavy and deliberately false goals
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural-consumer-acceptance --all-targets -- --ignored

  verify-stage10-proof-boundary:
    desc: Stage 10 publication rollback, Lean relational composition, and GPU translation/memory fail-closed checks
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --lib interrupted_legacy_migration
      - cargo test -p verineural --lib interrupted_fresh_publication
      - cargo test -p verineural --test relational_predicates
      - cargo test -p verineural --test relational_predicates -- --ignored
      - task verify-gpu-capabilities
      - task verify-certified-stage10

  verify-all-acceptance:
    desc: Developer-run combined Stage 1-4 regression, Lean, certified bundle and NVIDIA rotating acceptance
    cmds:
      - task check
      - task test
      - task clippy
      - task verify-api-acceptance
      - task verify-stage10-proof-boundary
      - task gpu-state-replay
      - task verify-lab-rotating-gpu
      - task lab-rotating

  verify-api-acceptance:
    desc: Developer-run P0/P1/P2 API contracts, real Lean checks, and independent consumer cases
    cmds:
      - task p0-acceptance
      - task verify-reusable-module-proof
      - task p2-consumers
      - task verify-p2-consumers

  verify-lab-rotating-gpu:
    desc: NVIDIA acceptance for typed ArgMax output and independent rotating-matrices CUDA Graph parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test tensor_indexing -- --ignored
      - cargo test -p rotating-matrices-lab --test gpu_parity
      - cargo test -p rotating-matrices-lab --test gpu_parity -- --ignored

  lab-rotating:
    desc: Inspect and train rotating-matrices; deterministic routing uses the unified structural/index CUDA Graph
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p rotating-matrices-lab --example rotating_matrices -- --inspect
      - cargo run -p rotating-matrices-lab --example rotating_matrices -- --train 128

  inspect-lab-rotating:
    desc: Inspect rotating cores and export diagnostic Semantic IR without GPU or Lean
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p rotating-matrices-lab --example rotating_matrices -- --inspect

  test-lab-rotating:
    desc: Developer-run CPU tests for 40 operations, byte dictionary, rotation and IR shapes
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p rotating-matrices-lab --all-targets

  train-lab-rotating:
    desc: Train rotating cores and eight-way router with CUDA Graph and report held-out accuracy
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p rotating-matrices-lab --example rotating_matrices -- --train {{.CLI_ARGS}}

  certify-lab-rotating:
    desc: Build rotating-matrices structural/index evidence with Lean and NVPTX (no GPU launch)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p rotating-matrices-lab --example rotating_matrices -- --certify-architecture

  lab-torus16-mix:
    desc: Inspect the VeriNeural Torus16-Mix operator and execute the Tensor host reference
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example torus16_mix -- --inspect

  inspect-ir-torus16-mix:
    desc: Print the complete canonical Torus16-Mix operator Semantic IR
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example torus16_mix -- --ir

  test-lab-torus16-mix:
    desc: Run Torus16-Mix plus reusable one-row structural GPU contract tests (no PyTorch)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test structural_last_row
      - cargo test -p verineural --test pointwise_gpu
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab

  verify-gpu-structural-last-row:
    desc: Run ignored NVIDIA acceptance for generic SliceAxis/BroadcastTo/Concat(1) in one CUDA Graph
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test structural_last_row -- --ignored --nocapture

  lab-torus16-mix-gpu:
    desc: Run all eight Torus16-Mix roles in one CUDA Graph with explicit approximate exp and compare Tensor oracle
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example torus16_mix -- --gpu

  verify-gpu-torus16-mix:
    desc: NVIDIA GPU acceptance for Torus16-Mix full multi-output forward (no PyTorch)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test gpu_forward -- --ignored --nocapture

  pointwise-binary-chain-fusion:
    desc: Structural checks for generic two-operation Add/Mul CUDA fusion
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test binary_pointwise_fusion

  verify-gpu-binary-chain-fusion:
    desc: NVIDIA bitwise parity for opt-in two-operation Add/Mul fusion
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test binary_pointwise_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  pointwise-three-op-fusion:
    desc: Structural contracts for three-op strict FP32 pointwise CUDA fusion
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_mul_fusion

  verify-gpu-three-op-fusion:
    desc: NVIDIA bitwise equivalence for twelve Mul-Add-Mul operand layouts
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_mul_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  pointwise-mul-add-fusion:
    desc: Validate checked opt-in Mul+Add CUDA fusion and its reverse-mode boundaries
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_fusion

  verify-gpu-mul-add-fusion:
    desc: NVIDIA bitwise fused vs unfused Mul-then-Add parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  temporal-bptt-stage:
    desc: Test generic recurrent IR unroll, through-time dependency and full EMA4 parameter inventory
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test temporal
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4

  verify-gpu-temporal-bptt:
    desc: Verify a two-step recurrent gradient with a hand-derived NVIDIA CUDA oracle
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test temporal -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-batch-transfers:
    desc: NVIDIA acceptance for partial H2D updates, selective batched D2H and old API parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_batch_transfers -- --ignored --nocapture

  test-lab-torus16-ema4-checkpoint:
    desc: CPU round-trip, corruption rejection and AdamW restart continuity for EMA4 snapshots
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --lib ema4_checkpoint -- --nocapture

  train-lab-torus16-ema4-bptt:
    desc: Release-optimized BPTT with batched transfers and per-stage wall-clock profiling
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt

  verify-gpu-p2-equivalence:
    desc: NVIDIA P2 acceptance - D2D/host feedback, fused/unfused FP32, EMA4 uninterrupted vs checkpoint resume
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_feedback -- --ignored --nocapture
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_add_mul_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture
      - cargo test -p verineural --test binary_pointwise_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture
      - |
        set -eu
        # Never read, overwrite or resume the user's normal training file.
        parity_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/verineural-ema4-p2.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$parity_dir"; else printf "P2 logs/checkpoints retained at %s\n" "$parity_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=2
        echo "P2 (1/3): full EMA4 fused/unfused parity, then two training windows"
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/first.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/first.log"; exit 1; }
        grep -q '^fusion_parity=PASS .*scope=EMA4_logits_gradients_terminal_states$' "$parity_dir/first.log"
        grep -q '^train_window=1 .*optimizer_step=2 ' "$parity_dir/first.log"
        echo "P2 (2/3): resume the two-window checkpoint to four windows"
        TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/resume.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/resume.log"; exit 1; }
        grep -q '^checkpoint_resumed=.*completed_windows=2$' "$parity_dir/resume.log"
        grep -q '^train_window=3 .*optimizer_step=4 ' "$parity_dir/resume.log"
        echo "P2 (3/3): continuous four-window training from a fresh initialization"
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/continuous.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/continuous.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/continuous.log"; exit 1; }
        grep -q '^train_window=3 .*optimizer_step=4 ' "$parity_dir/continuous.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/first.log" >"$parity_dir/observed.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/resume.log" >>"$parity_dir/observed.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/continuous.log" >"$parity_dir/expected.log"
        if ! cmp -s "$parity_dir/observed.log" "$parity_dir/expected.log"; then
          echo "FAIL: per-window EMA4 CE/BPC or optimizer step differs" >&2
          diff -u "$parity_dir/expected.log" "$parity_dir/observed.log" || true
          exit 1
        fi
        if ! cmp -s "$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" "$parity_dir/continuous.ckpt"; then
          echo "FAIL: checkpoint differs (parameters, recurrent states, AdamW, cursor)" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        echo "PASS: EMA4 fused/unfused logits, gradients and terminal states match at FP32 bit level"
        echo "PASS: uninterrupted and checkpoint-resumed training match per-window CE/BPC and optimizer steps"
        echo "PASS: final EMA4 checkpoints are bit-identical, including 271 parameter tensors, recurrent states and AdamW"

  verify-gpu-kernel-reuse:
    desc: Validate NVPTX specialization interning, translation evidence, and NVIDIA CUDA Graph parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test kernel_specialization_reuse
      - cargo test -p verineural --test kernel_specialization_reuse -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-dual-pointwise-outputs:
    desc: Check observable dual-output RNE fusion with structural tests and NVIDIA CUDA Graph parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test dual_pointwise_outputs
      - cargo test -p verineural --test dual_pointwise_outputs -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-diamond-fusion:
    desc: Structural and NVIDIA bitwise acceptance for four-op rounded diamond fusion with selected output
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_diamond_add_fusion
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_diamond_add_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-four-op-fusion:
    desc: Structural and NVIDIA bitwise acceptance for generic rounded four-operation pointwise fusion
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_mul_add_div_fusion
      - cargo test -p verineural --test mul_mul_add_div_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-sqrt-add-div-fusion:
    desc: Structural and NVIDIA bitwise acceptance for generic 3-operation rounded Sqrt/Add/Div fusion
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test sqrt_add_div_fusion
      - cargo test -p verineural --test sqrt_add_div_fusion -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-independent-batch:
    desc: NVIDIA accept independent CUDA Graph session preparation, pending IO guard, and bitwise serial/parallel equivalence
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_independent_batch independent_replay_matches_serial_and_rejects_pending_access -- --ignored --nocapture

  benchmark-gpu-independent-batch:
    desc: Measure four independent CUDA Graphs serial vs queued on separate non-blocking streams
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_independent_batch independent_streams_report_serial_vs_queued_wall_time -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-gpu-adamw:
    desc: Experimental generic CUDA Graph AdamW, host numeric oracle, GPU restart and EMA4 checkpoint parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_adamw
      - cargo test -p verineural --test gpu_adamw -- --ignored --nocapture
      - |
        set -eu
        parity_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/verineural-gpu-adamw.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$parity_dir"; else printf "GPU AdamW logs and checkpoint retained at %s\n" "$parity_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=2
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/first.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/first.log"; exit 1; }
        TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/resume.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/resume.log"; exit 1; }
        grep -q '^checkpoint_resumed=.*completed_windows=2$' "$parity_dir/resume.log"
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$parity_dir/continuous.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$parity_dir/continuous.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$parity_dir/continuous.log"; exit 1; }
        grep -q 'optimizer_backend=GPU_IR$' "$parity_dir/continuous.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/first.log" >"$parity_dir/observed.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/resume.log" >>"$parity_dir/observed.log"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$parity_dir/continuous.log" >"$parity_dir/expected.log"
        diff -u "$parity_dir/expected.log" "$parity_dir/observed.log"
        cmp "$parity_dir/resumed.ckpt" "$parity_dir/continuous.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: GPU AdamW 4-step checkpoint/resume matches uninterrupted training bit-for-bit"
        echo "PASS: GPU AdamW original parameters and optimizer moments survive checkpoint/resume"

  benchmark-torus16-holdout-reuse:
    desc: Compare fresh and reused holdout GPU sessions, requiring exact validation, test and checkpoint parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        bench_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/torus16-holdout.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$bench_dir"; else printf "Holdout logs and checkpoints retained at %s\n" "$bench_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_BPTT TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE TORUS16_ROLE_INIT TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=64 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=64 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=32
        for mode in fresh reused; do
          printf '\nholdout_mode=%s\n' "$mode"
          if [ "$mode" = reused ]; then export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1; else unset TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT; fi
          TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$bench_dir/$mode.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$bench_dir/$mode.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$bench_dir/$mode.log"; exit 1; }
          grep '^holdout_session_mode=' "$bench_dir/$mode.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$bench_dir/$mode.log"
          grep '^validation_window=' "$bench_dir/$mode.log"
        done
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p; /^validation_window=/s/ elapsed_s=.*$//p; /^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=/s/ eval_score_seconds=.*$//p; /^test_reset_streaming_bpc=/s/ checkpoint=.*$//p' "$bench_dir/fresh.log" >"$bench_dir/fresh.metrics"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p; /^validation_window=/s/ elapsed_s=.*$//p; /^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=/s/ eval_score_seconds=.*$//p; /^test_reset_streaming_bpc=/s/ checkpoint=.*$//p' "$bench_dir/reused.log" >"$bench_dir/reused.metrics"
        diff -u "$bench_dir/fresh.metrics" "$bench_dir/reused.metrics"
        cmp "$bench_dir/fresh.ckpt" "$bench_dir/reused.ckpt"
        cmp "$bench_dir/fresh.best.ckpt" "$bench_dir/reused.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: fresh and reused holdout BPC/checkpoints match bit-for-bit"
        echo "NOTE: holdout_session_prepare_s is one-time setup outside training clock"

  benchmark-torus16-codegen:
    desc: Compare strict-FP32 NVPTX llc O0/O2 on GPU AdamW, fail closed on PTX translation and checkpoint mismatch
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        bench_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/torus16-codegen.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$bench_dir"; else printf "Codegen logs and checkpoints retained at %s\n" "$bench_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_BPTT TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE TORUS16_ROLE_INIT TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=32
        for opt in 0 2; do
          printf '\nllc_codegen_optimization=-O%s\n' "$opt"
          TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT="$opt" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$bench_dir/opt$opt.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$bench_dir/opt$opt.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$bench_dir/opt$opt.log"; exit 1; }
          grep '^llc_codegen_optimization=' "$bench_dir/opt$opt.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$bench_dir/opt$opt.log"
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$bench_dir/opt$opt.log"
        done
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$bench_dir/opt0.log" >"$bench_dir/opt0.curve"
        sed -n '/^train_window=/s/ end_to_end_step_ms=.*$//p' "$bench_dir/opt2.log" >"$bench_dir/opt2.curve"
        diff -u "$bench_dir/opt0.curve" "$bench_dir/opt2.curve"
        cmp "$bench_dir/opt0.ckpt" "$bench_dir/opt2.ckpt"
        cmp "$bench_dir/opt0.best.ckpt" "$bench_dir/opt2.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: O2 matches O0 sample-by-sample and preserves final and best checkpoints bit-for-bit"
        echo "NOTE: O2 remains experimental; rerun benchmarks to confirm speed and use a separate resume regression"

  benchmark-torus16-throughput:
    desc: GPU AdamW throughput tuning; compare optional sparse loss readback and CUDA block size, require bitwise checkpoint parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        bench_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/torus16-throughput.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$bench_dir"; else printf "Benchmark logs retained at %s\n" "$bench_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_BPTT TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE TORUS16_ROLE_INIT TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        for choice in "256 1" "256 32" "64 32" "128 32" "512 32"; do
          set -- $choice
          threads="$1"; metric_every="$2"
          label="${threads}_${metric_every}"
          printf '\nthreads=%s metric_every=%s\n' "$threads" "$metric_every"
          TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK="$threads" TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY="$metric_every" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$bench_dir/$label.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$bench_dir/$label.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$bench_dir/$label.log"; exit 1; }
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$bench_dir/$label.log"
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$bench_dir/$label.log"
          grep '^cuda_graph_before=' "$bench_dir/$label.log"
        done
        cmp "$bench_dir/256_1.ckpt" "$bench_dir/256_32.ckpt"
        cmp "$bench_dir/256_1.best.ckpt" "$bench_dir/256_32.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: metric sampling preserves parameters, optimizer moments, states and validation selection bit-for-bit"
        echo "NOTE: compare tokens/s, not nvidia-smi utilisation; different block sizes require their own NVIDIA parity check"

  benchmark-gpu-adamw:
    desc: Compare sustained host/GPU AdamW throughput on the same EMA4 four-layer BPTT graph (256 windows)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        bench_dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/verineural-adamw-bench.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$bench_dir"; else printf "Benchmark logs retained at %s\n" "$bench_dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE TORUS16_ROLE_INIT TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_BPTT=2 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=128 TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED=1
        echo "Benchmark: host AdamW (256 windows)"
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$bench_dir/host.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$bench_dir/host.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$bench_dir/host.log"; exit 1; }
        echo "Benchmark: GPU IR AdamW (256 windows; finite-domain D2H validation)"
        TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$bench_dir/device.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$bench_dir/gpu.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$bench_dir/gpu.log"; exit 1; }
        echo "Host result:"
        grep '^training_total_s=' "$bench_dir/host.log"
        grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$bench_dir/host.log"
        grep '^fused_cuda_graph_event_average_ms=' "$bench_dir/host.log"
        grep '^cuda_graph_before=' "$bench_dir/host.log"
        echo "GPU result:"
        grep '^training_total_s=' "$bench_dir/gpu.log"
        grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$bench_dir/gpu.log"
        grep '^fused_cuda_graph_event_average_ms=' "$bench_dir/gpu.log"
        grep '^cuda_graph_before=' "$bench_dir/gpu.log"
        if ! grep -Eq '^cuda_graph_before=.* diamond_fusions=[1-9][0-9]* ' "$bench_dir/gpu.log"; then
          echo "FAIL: GPU AdamW did not activate the required observable-output diamond fusion" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        echo "NOTE: end-to-end throughput is authoritative; GPU optimizer adds IR kernels and may be slower."

  verify-torus16-matrix-initial:
    desc: NVIDIA bitwise parity between independently initialized W and Torus16-Mix tied W, before training (Rust only)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4 torus_matrix_modes_initial_gpu_logits_and_state_match_bits -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-torus16-matrix-gradients:
    desc: "NVIDIA numerical VJP check: shared W gradient equals sum of eight independent role gradients"
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4 torus_role_matrix_gradients_sum_to_shared_gradient -- --ignored --nocapture

  verify-torus16-matrix-training:
    desc: Full 2-step BPTT, fused/unfused GPU gradient parity, AdamW, and exact independent/shared checkpoint-resume
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/vn-matrix-train-test.XXXXXX")"
        trap 'status=$?; if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then rm -rf "$dir"; else echo "GPU training test logs at $dir" >&2; fi' EXIT
        unset TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK TORUS16_LLC_OPT TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION=1 TORUS16_BPTT=2
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=2 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=2
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched
        for mode in torus_shared independent; do
          export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="$mode"
          TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH="$dir/$mode.initial-probe" \
            TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/$mode-resumed.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/$mode-start.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 80 "$dir/$mode-start.log"; exit 1;
            }
          grep -q '^fusion_parity=PASS ' "$dir/$mode-start.log"
          TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/$mode-resumed.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/$mode-resume.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 80 "$dir/$mode-resume.log"; exit 1;
            }
          TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/$mode-continuous.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/$mode-continuous.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 80 "$dir/$mode-continuous.log"; exit 1;
            }
          cmp "$dir/$mode-resumed.ckpt" "$dir/$mode-continuous.ckpt"
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$dir/$mode-resume.log"
          grep '^test_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$dir/$mode-resume.log"
          echo "PASS: $mode two-step BPTT/GPU AdamW parity and bitwise resume"
        done
        cmp "$dir/torus_shared.initial-probe" "$dir/independent.initial-probe"
        echo "PASS: initial training BPTT logits and terminal states bitwise-equal across architectures"

  finetune-torus16-best-lr5:
    desc: Paired seed-0 best-checkpoint continuation with 5x reduced AdamW LR and preserved moments
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        # Match checkpoint fingerprints: BPTT, validation frequency and
        # training budget are set as one consistent preset, not independent
        # inherited environment variables. BPTT=2 remains the default.
        bptt="${TORUS16_FINETUNE_BPTT:-2}"
        case "$bptt" in
          2)
            source_default=target/torus16-pilot
            out_default=target/torus16-finetune-lr5-seed0
            eval_every=2048
            checkpoint_every=1024
            default_windows=98304
            ;;
          4)
            source_default=target/torus16-bptt4-seed0
            out_default=target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0
            eval_every=1024
            checkpoint_every=512
            default_windows=65536
            ;;
          *) echo "TORUS16_FINETUNE_BPTT must be 2 or 4" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        esac
        source_dir="${TORUS16_FINETUNE_SOURCE_DIR:-$source_default}"
        out="${TORUS16_FINETUNE_DIR:-$out_default}"
        if [ "$source_dir" = "$out" ]; then echo "Source and finetune directories must differ" >&2; exit 1; fi
        mkdir -p "$out"
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X=1 TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_BPTT="$bptt"
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=512 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=512 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY="$eval_every" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY="$checkpoint_every"
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=32 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256
        export TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS="${TORUS16_FINETUNE_WINDOWS:-$default_windows}"
        for mode in torus_shared independent; do
          tag="$mode-matched-seed0"
          source_best="$source_dir/$tag.best.ckpt"
          destination="$out/$tag.ckpt"
          best="$out/$tag.best.ckpt"
          log="$out/$tag.log"
          if [ ! -f "$source_best" ]; then echo "Missing source best checkpoint: $source_best" >&2; exit 1; fi
          if [ ! -e "$destination" ] && [ ! -e "$best" ]; then
            cp "$source_best" "$destination"
            cp "$source_best" "$best"
          elif [ ! -f "$destination" ] || [ ! -f "$best" ]; then
            echo "Incomplete finetune checkpoint pair: $destination / $best" >&2
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "Fine-tune: $tag bptt=$TORUS16_BPTT target_windows=$TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS AdamW_LR=0.0004 (best-checkpoint source)"
          TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="$mode" TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0 \
            TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$destination" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >>"$log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$log"
              echo "FAIL: $tag; full log at $log" >&2
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^checkpoint_resumed=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_adamw_lr=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^test_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^validation_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.validation_curve.log"
          grep '^train_curve_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.train_curve.log"
        done
        echo "PASS: paired seed-0 finetune completed, logs/checkpoints: $out"

  compare-torus16-matrix-tying:
    desc: Resumable seeded Rust/VeriNeural Torus16-Mix LM ablation with train/validation curves
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        unset TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        out="${TORUS16_MATRIX_ABLATION_DIR:-target/torus16-matrix-ablation}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_BPTT="${TORUS16_BPTT:-2}"
        export TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS="${TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS:-65536}"
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT="${TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT:-4096}"
        export TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT="${TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT:-4096}"
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY="${TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY:-8192}"
        export TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY="${TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY:-4096}"
        export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1
        # Default is one paired matched-W seed. Set MATRIX_SEEDS="1 2 3"
        # for replicate trials, INCLUDE_DIVERSE=1 for the independent-W
        # baseline, and MATRIX_ABLATION_FRESH=1 for an explicit fresh run.
        if [ "${TORUS16_MATRIX_ABLATION_FRESH:-0}" = 1 ]; then
          export TORUS16_FRESH=1
        else
          unset TORUS16_FRESH
        fi
        for seed in ${TORUS16_MATRIX_SEEDS:-0}; do
          case "$seed" in ''|*[!0-9]*) echo "Invalid uint64 seed: $seed" >&2; exit 1;; esac
          variants="torus_shared:matched independent:matched"
          if [ "${TORUS16_INCLUDE_DIVERSE:-0}" = 1 ]; then
            variants="$variants independent:diverse"
          fi
          for variant in $variants; do
            mode="${variant%%:*}"
            init="${variant#*:}"
            tag="$mode-$init-seed$seed"
            log="$out/$tag.log"
            echo "Torus16-Mix training: $tag (windows=$TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS, BPTT=$TORUS16_BPTT, validation=$TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT)"
            if [ -n "${TORUS16_FRESH:-}" ] || [ ! -f "$out/$tag.ckpt" ]; then
              : >"$log"
            fi
            TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="$mode" TORUS16_ROLE_INIT="$init" TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED="$seed" \
              TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$tag.ckpt" \
              cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >>"$log" 2>&1 || {
                tail -n 100 "$log"
                echo "FAIL: $tag; full log in $log" >&2
                exit 1
              }
            grep '^experiment_matrix_mode=' "$log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^training_total_s=' "$log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^test_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^train_curve_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.train_curve.log"
            grep '^validation_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.validation_curve.log"
          done
        done
        echo "PASS: matched-seed Torus16-Mix pair evaluated; results at $out"
        echo "best checkpoints: $out/*.best.ckpt"

  autodiff-stage:
    desc: Validate architecture-neutral reverse-mode IR rules, finite difference checks and atomic AdamW
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test autodiff

  verify-gpu-autodiff:
    desc: Validate reverse-mode MatMul/fanout gradients through CUDA Graph against independent oracle
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test autodiff -- --ignored --nocapture

  train-lab-torus16-ema4:
    desc: GPU CE to reverse-IR VJP to host AdamW, one-token truncated gradient for final-beta only
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_train

  lab-torus16-ema4:
    desc: Inspect the 4-layer streaming EMA4-LM architecture built from VeriNeural primitives
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4 -- --inspect

  test-lab-torus16-ema4:
    desc: Validate research-sized parameter count, all named states and causal CPU reference
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p verineural --test pointwise_gpu
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4

  lab-torus16-ema4-gpu:
    desc: Execute three EMA4-LM autoregressive steps through one persistent CUDA Graph
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4 -- --gpu

  verify-gpu-torus16-ema4:
    desc: NVIDIA acceptance for streaming EMA4-LM logits and on-device EMA feedback
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4 -- --ignored --nocapture

  certify-lab-torus16-mix:
    desc: Fail closed on unsupported certified numerical semantics of pointwise Exp/Div
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p torus16-mix-lab --example torus16_mix -- --certify


  verify-torus16-role-delta:
    desc: Validate Role-Delta inventory, scalar gradients, initial EMA4 parity and projection GPU VJP
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4 role_delta_parameter_inventory_and_zero_adapter_initialization
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --lib role_delta_scalar_vjp_matches_finite_differences
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --lib role_delta_parameter_only_hoisting_reduces_real_bptt_ir -- --nocapture
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --lib role_delta_warm_start_accepts_shared_and_rejects_incompatible_sources
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --test ema4 role_delta_initial_gpu_logits_and_state_match -- --ignored --nocapture
      - cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --lib role_delta_gpu_vjp_matches_scalar_oracle -- --ignored --nocapture

  compare-torus16-role-delta-ranks:
    desc: Paired rank-4/rank-8 validation-only Role-Delta experiments (resumable, no test peeking)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing TorusShared source checkpoint: $source (set TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE)" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        backend="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_BACKEND:-cpu}"
        case "$backend" in
          cpu)
            default_out=target/torus16-role-delta-rank-ablation
            unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT
            export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1
            ;;
          gpu)
            default_out=target/torus16-role-delta-rank-ablation-gpu
            export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=32 TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1
            ;;
          *) echo "TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_BACKEND must be cpu or gpu" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        esac
        out="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_DIR:-$default_out}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1
        export TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_WINDOWS:-8192}"
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=512 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=512
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=1024 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=512
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SEED:-0}"
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256
        unset TORUS16_FRESH TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        unset TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED
        unset TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH
        unset TORUS16_CORPUS
        for mode in role_delta_4 role_delta_8; do
          tag="$mode-seed$TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED"
          log="$out/$tag.log"
          if [ ! -f "$out/$tag.ckpt" ]; then : >"$log"; fi
          echo "Role-Delta validation-only ablation: $tag backend=$backend, windows=$TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS, source=$source"
          TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="$mode" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$tag.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >>"$log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$log"
              echo "FAIL: $tag; see $log" >&2
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^experiment_matrix_mode=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^validation_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.validation_curve.log" || true
          grep '^train_curve_window=' "$log" >"$out/$tag.train_curve.log" || true
        done
        echo "Compare best_validation_bpc from both ranks; the test suffix has not been evaluated."
        echo "Checkpoints, logs and curves: $out"

  verify-torus16-role-delta-resume:
    desc: Bitwise checkpoint/resume versus continuous Role-Delta training, with test held out
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing TorusShared source checkpoint: $source (set TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE)" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        mode="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_VERIFY_MODE:-role_delta_4}"
        case "$mode" in
          role_delta_2|role_delta_4|role_delta_8) ;;
          *) echo "Unsupported Role-Delta mode: $mode" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        esac
        mkdir -p target
        dir="$(mktemp -d target/torus16-role-delta-resume.XXXXXX)"
        echo "Resume evidence directory: $dir"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="$mode" TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=2 TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256
        unset TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_FRESH
        TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/start.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$dir/start.log"; exit 1;
          }
        TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/resumed.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/resume.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$dir/resume.log"; exit 1;
          }
        TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=4 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/continuous.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/continuous.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$dir/continuous.log"; exit 1;
          }
        grep -q '^checkpoint_resumed=' "$dir/resume.log"
        for log in "$dir/start.log" "$dir/resume.log" "$dir/continuous.log"; do
          grep -q '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$log"
        done
        cmp "$dir/resumed.ckpt" "$dir/continuous.ckpt"
        cmp "$dir/resumed.best.ckpt" "$dir/continuous.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: $mode bitwise checkpoint/resume and validation-best checkpoint"
        echo "Evidence: $dir"

  benchmark-torus16-role-delta-backends:
    desc: Compare CPU/GPU optimizer throughput for warm-start rank4 BPTT4
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then echo "Missing warm-start source: $source" >&2; exit 1; fi
        out="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_BENCH_DIR:-target/torus16-role-delta-backend-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256
        # A benchmark must not accidentally resume a previous trial.
        export TORUS16_FRESH=1
        unset TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED
        unset TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        for backend in cpu gpu; do
          if [ "$backend" = gpu ]; then
            export TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW=1 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=32 TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1
          else
            unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT
            export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1
          fi
          echo "Role-Delta BPTT4 throughput backend=$backend windows=256"
          TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$backend.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$backend.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/$backend.log"
              echo "FAIL: backend=$backend log=$out/$backend.log" >&2
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^cuda_graph_' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$out/$backend.log" | tail -n 1
        done
        echo "Compare training_tokens_per_second, profile and compilation costs; utilization alone is insufficient."
        echo "CPU/GPU checkpoints are separate; numerical parity between optimizers is not assumed."
        echo "Evidence: $out"

  verify-torus16-role-delta-fast-setup:
    desc: Bitwise CPU Role-Delta checkpoint parity with and without redundant unfused compilation
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then echo "Missing warm-start source: $source" >&2; exit 1; fi
        mkdir -p target
        dir="$(mktemp -d target/torus16-role-delta-fast-setup.XXXXXX)"
        echo "Fast-setup evidence directory: $dir"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=2
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=2 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=2 TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256
        export TORUS16_FRESH=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        unset TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED
        unset TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=0 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/baseline.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/baseline.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$dir/baseline.log"; exit 1;
          }
        TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$dir/fast.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$dir/fast.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$dir/fast.log"; exit 1;
          }
        grep -q '^cuda_graph_before=' "$dir/baseline.log"
        grep -q '^cuda_graph_baseline=SKIPPED ' "$dir/fast.log"
        grep -q '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$dir/fast.log"
        cmp "$dir/baseline.ckpt" "$dir/fast.ckpt"
        cmp "$dir/baseline.best.ckpt" "$dir/fast.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: fast setup and full diagnostic setup produce bitwise-identical checkpoints"
        echo "Original preparation:"
        grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$dir/baseline.log"
        echo "Fast preparation:"
        grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$dir/fast.log"
        echo "Evidence: $dir"

  profile-torus16-bptt16-interning:
    desc: CPU BPTT16 preflight; opt-in NVIDIA BPTT8/BPTT16 JIT and synchronized CUDA Graph probes (no training)
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        gpu="${TORUS16_PROFILE_RUN_GPU:-0}"
        case "$gpu" in 0|1) ;; *) echo "TORUS16_PROFILE_RUN_GPU must be 0 or 1" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
        out="${TORUS16_PROFILE_BPTT_DIR:-target/torus16-bptt16-interning}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        cargo test -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt bptt16_budget_tests -- --nocapture
        # No warm-start, training, validation, test, or checkpoint mutation.
        unset TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW
        unset TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED
        unset TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_FRESH=1 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=1 TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=1 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=1
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_MAX_TENSOR_MIB=512
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_MAX_UNIQUE_KERNELS=4096
        export VERINEURAL_GPU_PREPARE_PROFILE=1
        export TORUS16_BPTT=16 TORUS16_BPTT16_PREFLIGHT_ONLY=1
        unset TORUS16_BPTT16_ENABLE_SLOW_JIT
        # Preflight never calls LLVM llc or CUDA, even when the budget fails.
        TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/never-written-bptt16.ckpt" \
          cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/bptt16-preflight.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 80 "$out/bptt16-preflight.log"; exit 1;
          }
        grep '^gpu_compilation_inventory bptt=16 ' "$out/bptt16-preflight.log"
        grep '^bptt16_resource_preflight ' "$out/bptt16-preflight.log"
        grep -F 'bptt16_preflight_only=PASS cuda_jit=SKIPPED gpu_graph=NOT_CREATED training=SKIPPED validation=SKIPPED test=SKIPPED' "$out/bptt16-preflight.log"
        if grep -Eq '^(gpu_nvptx_stage=|gpu_prepare_phase=|setup_probe=|training_total_s=)' "$out/bptt16-preflight.log"; then
          echo "FAIL: preflight entered GPU work or training" >&2; exit 1
        fi
        if [ "$gpu" = 0 ]; then
          echo "PASS: BPTT16 CPU-only inventory. NVIDIA probes withheld."
          echo "Explicit opt-in: TORUS16_PROFILE_RUN_GPU=1 task profile-torus16-bptt16-interning"
          echo "Logs: $out"
          exit 0
        fi
        timeout_s="${TORUS16_PROFILE_TIMEOUT_S:-240}"
        case "$timeout_s" in ''|*[!0-9]*) echo "TORUS16_PROFILE_TIMEOUT_S must be integer seconds" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
        if [ "$timeout_s" -lt 30 ] || [ "$timeout_s" -gt 900 ]; then
          echo "TORUS16_PROFILE_TIMEOUT_S must be in 30..900" >&2; exit 1
        fi
        export TORUS16_SETUP_PROBE_ONLY=1 TORUS16_BPTT16_PREFLIGHT_ONLY=0
        # Raise the separate graph-node cap only for this explicitly opted-in
        # diagnostic. PTX entrypoint and graph-tensor caps remain independent.
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_MAX_KERNELS=80000
        for bptt in 8 16; do
          export TORUS16_BPTT="$bptt"
          if [ "$bptt" -eq 16 ]; then
            export TORUS16_BPTT16_ENABLE_SLOW_JIT=1
          else
            unset TORUS16_BPTT16_ENABLE_SLOW_JIT
          fi
          label="bptt$bptt-probe"
          echo "NVIDIA setup/replay probe $label (timeout=${timeout_s}s, no AdamW/checkpoint/validation)"
          TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/never-written-$label.ckpt" \
            timeout -k 10s "${timeout_s}s" cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$label.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/$label.log"
              echo "FAIL: $label; JIT may be too large; artifacts: $out" >&2
              exit 1
            }
          grep "^setup_probe=PASS bptt=$bptt " "$out/$label.log"
          grep '^gpu_nvptx_stage=' "$out/$label.log"
          grep '^gpu_prepare_phase=' "$out/$label.log"
          if [ -e "$out/never-written-$label.ckpt" ]; then
            echo "FAIL: setup probe modified checkpoint" >&2; exit 1
          fi
        done
        echo "PASS: two GPU setup probes completed. CUDA event replay and JIT timings are diagnostic, not throughput/BPC results."
        echo "Graph tensor bytes are NOT peak VRAM. Evidence: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-v02-bptt16:
    desc: SAFE BPTT16 graph preflight only; never start blocking driver PTX JIT or a CUDA Graph
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        # Compatibility with the old task name. The previous task generated
        # 63,707 CUDA kernels and hung in CUDA module loading with no GPU load.
        # This task now does CPU graph analysis ONLY, not GPU benchmarking.
        base="${TORUS16_V02_BPTT16_DIR:-target/torus16-v02-bptt16-preflight}"
        mkdir -p "$base"
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_PREFLIGHT_ONLY=1
        export TORUS16_V02_RANKS=4 TORUS16_V02_BPTTS=16
        export TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS=64 TORUS16_V02_VALIDATION_CHARS=64
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_MAX_KERNELS=40000
        export TORUS16_BPTT16_MAX_TENSOR_MIB=512
        unset TORUS16_BPTT16_ENABLE_SLOW_JIT
        echo "BPTT16 safety: CPU-only resource preflight, no CUDA driver JIT, no training or evaluation."
        TORUS16_V02_DIR="$base" task benchmark-torus16-v02-horizon >"$base/summary.log" 2>&1 || {
          tail -n 120 "$base/summary.log"
          echo "FAIL: BPTT16 preflight; logs under $base" >&2
          exit 1
        }
        raw="$base/rank4-bptt16.log"
        grep '^bptt16_resource_preflight ' "$raw"
        grep -Fx 'bptt16_preflight_only=PASS cuda_jit=SKIPPED gpu_graph=NOT_CREATED training=SKIPPED validation=SKIPPED test=SKIPPED' "$raw"
        if grep -Eq '^(gpu_nvptx_stage=|gpu_prepare_phase=|training_total_s=)' "$raw"; then
          echo "FAIL: BPTT16 preflight unexpectedly entered LLVM/CUDA or training" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        echo "PASS: CPU-only BPTT16 preflight completed without launching CUDA JIT."
        echo "GPU replay NOT RUN: use TORUS16_PROFILE_RUN_GPU=1 task profile-torus16-bptt16-interning for an explicitly bounded diagnostic."
        echo "Logs: $base/summary.log $raw"

  benchmark-torus16-v02-allocation-slab:
    desc: Compare separate CUDA tensor allocations against a single bounded slab and require bitwise checkpoint parity
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        base="${TORUS16_V02_SLAB_DIR:-target/torus16-v02-allocation-slab}"
        mkdir -p "$base"
        export VERINEURAL_GPU_PREPARE_PROFILE=1
        export TORUS16_V02_RANKS=4 TORUS16_V02_BPTTS=8
        export TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS=64 TORUS16_V02_VALIDATION_CHARS=64
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ALLOCATION_SLAB
        for mode in separate slab; do
          if [ "$mode" = slab ]; then
            export TORUS16_GPU_ALLOCATION_SLAB=1
          else
            unset TORUS16_GPU_ALLOCATION_SLAB
          fi
          echo "v0.2 memory layout=$mode role_delta_4 BPTT8 (64-char setup smoke)"
          TORUS16_V02_DIR="$base/$mode" task benchmark-torus16-v02-horizon >"$base/$mode.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$base/$mode.log"
            exit 1
          }
          # The nested task prints only a summary. Allocation details
          # exist in the raw training log, not in the nested task stdout.
          raw="$base/$mode/rank4-bptt8.log"
          if [ ! -s "$raw" ]; then
            echo "Missing raw training log: $raw" >&2
            exit 1
          fi
          grep -Fx "gpu_allocation_mode=$mode" "$raw" || {
            echo "Unexpected GPU allocation mode in $raw" >&2
            tail -n 100 "$raw"
            exit 1
          }
          grep "^gpu_prepare_allocations mode=$mode .*artifact_dir=.*vn_ema4_bptt_" "$raw"
          grep '^gpu_prepare_phase=.*artifact_dir=.*vn_ema4_bptt_' "$raw"
          grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$raw"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$raw"
          grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$raw"
        done
        cmp "$base/separate/rank4-bptt8.ckpt" "$base/slab/rank4-bptt8.ckpt"
        cmp "$base/separate/rank4-bptt8.best.ckpt" "$base/slab/rank4-bptt8.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: slab and separate CUDA allocations preserve final/best checkpoint bits."
        echo "DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: 64-char validation must not be used to rank architecture quality."
        echo "Summary logs: $base/separate.log $base/slab.log"
        echo "Raw GPU logs: $base/separate/rank4-bptt8.log $base/slab/rank4-bptt8.log"

  benchmark-torus16-v02-setup-stability:
    desc: Repeat BPTT8 CUDA setup across fresh processes, report phase spread and verify deterministic checkpoint bytes
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        base="${TORUS16_V02_SETUP_DIR:-target/torus16-v02-setup-stability}"
        mkdir -p "$base"
        export VERINEURAL_GPU_PREPARE_PROFILE=1
        export TORUS16_V02_RANKS=4 TORUS16_V02_BPTTS=8
        export TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS=64 TORUS16_V02_VALIDATION_CHARS=64
        for trial in 1 2 3; do
          echo "CUDA setup reproducibility trial=$trial/3, role_delta_4 BPTT8, separate process"
          TORUS16_V02_DIR="$base/trial$trial" task benchmark-torus16-v02-horizon >"$base/trial$trial.log" 2>&1 || {
            tail -n 100 "$base/trial$trial.log"
            exit 1
          }
          # Distinguish the training graph from the much smaller reused
          # holdout graph. Report stages without collapsing them into one timer.
          grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$base/trial$trial.log"
          grep '^gpu_nvptx_stage=.*artifact_dir=.*vn_ema4_bptt_' "$base/trial$trial.log"
          grep '^gpu_prepare_phase=.*artifact_dir=.*vn_ema4_bptt_' "$base/trial$trial.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$base/trial$trial.log"
          grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$base/trial$trial.log"
          if [ "$trial" != 1 ]; then
            cmp "$base/trial1/rank4-bptt8.ckpt" "$base/trial$trial/rank4-bptt8.ckpt"
            cmp "$base/trial1/rank4-bptt8.best.ckpt" "$base/trial$trial/rank4-bptt8.best.ckpt"
          fi
        done
        echo "PASS: checkpoint bits identical across three independent setup runs."
        echo "DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: 64-char validation is not an architecture quality gate."
        echo "Compare llc, cuda_module_load, kernel_resolution and graph_instantiate across trials."
        echo "Logs: $base/trial1.log $base/trial2.log $base/trial3.log"

  benchmark-torus16-v02-horizon:
    desc: v0.2 transition gate - Role-Delta rank 4/8 x BPTT 4/8 with packed I/O and long validation
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing TorusShared warm-start checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        # Equal training characters, NOT equal optimizer updates.
        train_tokens="${TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS:-4096}"
        case "$train_tokens" in
          ''|*[!0-9]*) echo "TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS must be an integer" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        esac
        if [ "$train_tokens" -lt 8 ] || [ "$train_tokens" -gt 32768 ] || [ "$((train_tokens % 8))" -ne 0 ]; then
          echo "TORUS16_V02_TRAIN_TOKENS must be 8..32768 and divisible by 8" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        # Long-validation acceptance remains the default. A 64-character
        # diagnostic mode is useful only for compiler/setup profiling.
        validation_chars="${TORUS16_V02_VALIDATION_CHARS:-8192}"
        case "$validation_chars" in
          64|8192) ;;
          *) echo "TORUS16_V02_VALIDATION_CHARS must be 64 (setup smoke) or 8192 (acceptance)" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        esac
        out="${TORUS16_V02_DIR:-target/torus16-v02-horizon}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0 TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT="$validation_chars" TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=8192
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=16
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        export TORUS16_PACKED_D2H=1 TORUS16_PACKED_H2D=1 TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY=1
        export TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=1024
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        # Default is the full matrix. Filter specific configurations when
        # investigating expensive CUDA setup, without touching other runs.
        ranks="${TORUS16_V02_RANKS:-4 8}"
        bptts="${TORUS16_V02_BPTTS:-4 8}"
        for rank in $ranks; do
          case "$rank" in 4|8) ;; *) echo "Invalid v0.2 rank: $rank" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
          for bptt in $bptts; do
            case "$bptt" in 4|8|16) ;; *) echo "Invalid v0.2 BPTT: $bptt" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
            if [ "$((train_tokens % bptt))" -ne 0 ]; then
              echo "Training tokens ($train_tokens) must be divisible by BPTT=$bptt" >&2
              exit 1
            fi
            windows="$((train_tokens / bptt))"
            export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE="role_delta_$rank"
            export TORUS16_BPTT="$bptt" TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS="$windows"
            # Evaluate only after the same number of trained characters.
            export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY="$windows"
            label="rank$rank-bptt$bptt"
            echo "v0.2 gate $label training_characters=$train_tokens windows=$windows validation_characters=$validation_chars"
            TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$label.ckpt" \
              cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$label.log" 2>&1 || {
                tail -n 100 "$out/$label.log"
                echo "FAIL: v0.2 gate $label ($out/$label.log)" >&2
                exit 1
              }
            # A BPTT16 CPU-only inspection returns successfully before
            # llc and cuModuleLoadData. Do not require training metrics or
            # final/best checkpoints from a preflight-only execution.
            if [ "$bptt" -eq 16 ] && [ "${TORUS16_BPTT16_PREFLIGHT_ONLY:-0}" = 1 ]; then
              grep '^bptt16_resource_preflight ' "$out/$label.log"
              grep '^bptt16_preflight_only=PASS ' "$out/$label.log"
              echo "BPTT16 training=SKIPPED because this is CPU-only JIT preflight."
              continue
            fi
            grep '^temporal_parameter_only_hoisting=enabled ' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^cuda_graph_baseline=SKIPPED ' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            if [ -n "${VERINEURAL_GPU_PREPARE_PROFILE:-}" ]; then
              grep '^gpu_nvptx_stage=' "$out/$label.log"
              grep '^gpu_prepare_phase=' "$out/$label.log"
            fi
            grep '^training_parameter_upload_mode=packed_true' "$out/$label.log"
            grep '^training_d2h_profile_avg_ms .*packed=true' "$out/$label.log"
            grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            grep "^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=.*scored_characters=$validation_chars " "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$out/$label.log" | tail -n 1
          done
        done
        if [ "${TORUS16_BPTT16_PREFLIGHT_ONLY:-0}" = "1" ]; then
          echo "PASS: BPTT16 CPU-only graph inspection finished; training/validation/test and CUDA JIT were NOT run."
        else
          echo "PASS: selected runs completed, validation_characters=$validation_chars, test withheld."
        fi
        if [ "$validation_chars" != 8192 ]; then
          echo "DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: validation is too short to rank architectures."
        fi
        echo "Important: BPTT changes optimizer update count; different ranks/BPTT have different checkpoint identities."
        echo "Evidence and checkpoints: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-packed-hoisting:
    desc: Paired and reversed-order BPTT hoisting benchmark with both packed CUDA Graph transfers enabled
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing trained TorusShared source checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        out="${TORUS16_PACKED_HOIST_BENCH_DIR:-target/torus16-packed-hoist-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        export TORUS16_PACKED_D2H=1 TORUS16_PACKED_H2D=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        for trial in 1 2; do
          # Reverse order to expose first-run/warm-cache and driver variation.
          if [ "$trial" = 1 ]; then modes="baseline hoisted"; else modes="hoisted baseline"; fi
          for mode in $modes; do
            if [ "$mode" = hoisted ]; then hoist=1; else hoist=0; fi
            echo "packed BPTT4 trial=$trial mode=$mode, 256 windows"
            TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY="$hoist" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$trial-$mode.ckpt" \
              cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$trial-$mode.log" 2>&1 || {
                tail -n 100 "$out/$trial-$mode.log"
                exit 1
              }
            grep '^temporal_parameter_only_hoisting=' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^cuda_graph_baseline=SKIPPED ' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^setup_stage=' "$out/$trial-$mode.log"
            grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^training_parameter_upload_mode=packed_true' "$out/$trial-$mode.log"
            grep '^training_d2h_profile_avg_ms .*packed=true' "$out/$trial-$mode.log"
            grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
            grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/$trial-$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          done
        done
        for mode in baseline hoisted; do
          cmp "$out/1-$mode.ckpt" "$out/2-$mode.ckpt"
          cmp "$out/1-$mode.best.ckpt" "$out/2-$mode.best.ckpt"
        done
        echo "PASS: each IR mode is deterministic across both trials; compare modes by replay/throughput/BPC."
        echo "Different IR fingerprints and FP32 reduction order: do NOT compare hoisted vs baseline checkpoint bytes."
        echo "Measurements: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-packed-h2d:
    desc: Compare packed parameter H2D versus standard CPU AdamW upload and check checkpoint bits
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing trained TorusShared source checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        out="${TORUS16_PACKED_H2D_BENCH_DIR:-target/torus16-packed-h2d-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY=0
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        export TORUS16_PACKED_D2H=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_PACKED_H2D
        for mode in baseline packed; do
          if [ "$mode" = packed ]; then export TORUS16_PACKED_H2D=1; else unset TORUS16_PACKED_H2D; fi
          echo "CPU AdamW upload=$mode, rank4 BPTT4, 256 windows, packed D2H"
          TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$mode.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$mode.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/$mode.log"
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^training_parameter_upload_mode=' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/$mode.log"
        done
        cmp "$out/baseline.ckpt" "$out/packed.ckpt"
        cmp "$out/baseline.best.ckpt" "$out/packed.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: packed H2D preserves exact CPU AdamW checkpoint bits"
        echo "Logs and checkpoints: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-packed-d2h:
    desc: Compare standard CPU AdamW D2H against CUDA Graph packed gradient readback and verify checkpoint bits
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing trained TorusShared source checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        out="${TORUS16_PACKED_D2H_BENCH_DIR:-target/torus16-packed-d2h-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY=0
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS TORUS16_PACKED_D2H TORUS16_PACKED_H2D
        for mode in baseline packed; do
          if [ "$mode" = packed ]; then export TORUS16_PACKED_D2H=1; else unset TORUS16_PACKED_D2H; fi
          echo "CPU AdamW readback=$mode, rank4 BPTT4, 256 windows"
          TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$mode.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$mode.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/$mode.log"
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^training_d2h_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/$mode.log"
        done
        cmp "$out/baseline.ckpt" "$out/packed.ckpt"
        cmp "$out/baseline.best.ckpt" "$out/packed.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: packed CUDA Graph readback preserves exact CPU AdamW checkpoint bits"
        echo "Logs and checkpoints: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-cpu-metric-sampling:
    desc: Verify CPU AdamW metric sampling preserves rank-4 BPTT-4 checkpoints bit-for-bit and profile D2H
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing trained TorusShared source checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        out="${TORUS16_CPU_METRIC_BENCH_DIR:-target/torus16-cpu-metric-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1 TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY=0
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        for every in 1 16; do
          echo "CPU AdamW metric sample=$every, rank4 BPTT4, 256 windows"
          TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY="$every" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/metric$every.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/metric$every.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/metric$every.log"
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^training_d2h_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/metric$every.log"
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/metric$every.log"
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/metric$every.log"
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/metric$every.log"
        done
        cmp "$out/metric1.ckpt" "$out/metric16.ckpt"
        cmp "$out/metric1.best.ckpt" "$out/metric16.best.ckpt"
        echo "PASS: sampled CPU logits preserve full optimizer/state/checkpoint bits"
        echo "Compare repeated throughput and separate D2H enqueue/sync/host-copy timings, not one noisy run."
        echo "Logs and checkpoints: $out"

  benchmark-torus16-role-delta-hoisting:
    desc: Compare same rank-4 BPTT-4 training with and without parameter-only temporal IR reuse
    deps: [prepare]
    cmds:
      - |
        set -eu
        source="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_SOURCE:-target/torus16-bptt4-finetune-lr5-seed0/torus_shared-matched-seed0.best.ckpt}"
        if [ ! -f "$source" ]; then
          echo "Missing trained TorusShared source checkpoint: $source" >&2
          exit 1
        fi
        out="${TORUS16_ROLE_DELTA_HOIST_DIR:-target/torus16-role-delta-hoist-benchmark}"
        mkdir -p "$out"
        export TORUS16_WARM_START_SHARED="$source"
        export TORUS16_MATRIX_MODE=role_delta_4 TORUS16_ROLE_INIT=matched TORUS16_MATRIX_SEED=0
        export TORUS16_DELTA_SCALE=1 TORUS16_BPTT=4 TORUS16_TRAIN_WINDOWS=256
        export TORUS16_VAL_LIMIT=64 TORUS16_TEST_LIMIT=64
        export TORUS16_EVAL_EVERY=256 TORUS16_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=256
        export TORUS16_SKIP_TEST=1 TORUS16_SKIP_FUSION_BASELINE=1
        export TORUS16_METRIC_EVERY=1 TORUS16_REUSE_HOLDOUT=1
        export TORUS16_LLC_OPT=0 TORUS16_THREADS_PER_BLOCK=256 TORUS16_FRESH=1
        unset TORUS16_GPU_ADAMW TORUS16_LR_DECAY_5X TORUS16_VERIFY_FUSION
        unset TORUS16_BENCH_COMPARE TORUS16_BENCH_FUSED TORUS16_GPU_FEEDBACK_EVENTS
        unset TORUS16_INITIAL_PROBE_PATH TORUS16_CORPUS
        for mode in baseline hoisted; do
          if [ "$mode" = hoisted ]; then hoist=1; else hoist=0; fi
          echo "Temporal parameter-only reuse: $mode, rank4 BPTT4, 256 windows"
          TORUS16_HOIST_PARAMETER_ONLY="$hoist" TORUS16_CHECKPOINT="$out/$mode.ckpt" \
            cargo run --release -p torus16-mix-lab --example ema4_bptt >"$out/$mode.log" 2>&1 || {
              tail -n 100 "$out/$mode.log"
              echo "FAIL: $mode, log=$out/$mode.log" >&2
              exit 1
            }
          grep '^temporal_parameter_only_hoisting=' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^cuda_graph_baseline=SKIPPED ' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^setup_stage=' "$out/$mode.log"
          grep '^setup_compile_and_cuda_prepare_ms=' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_profile_avg_ms ' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^training_total_s=' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^holdout_reset_streaming_bpc=' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
          grep '^test_evaluation=SKIPPED ' "$out/$mode.log" | tail -n 1
        done
        echo "Assess kernel count, replay time, wall-clock throughput and validation BPC."
        echo "Different IR fingerprints/FP32 gradient reduction order: do not require bitwise checkpoint equality."
        echo "Logs and checkpoints: $out"

FILE	crates/verineural/Cargo.toml
[package]
name = "verineural"
version.workspace = true
edition.workspace = true
rust-version.workspace = true
description = "Importable Rust library for neural computation and formal verification (Semantic IR, Lean proof, and experimental LLVM NVPTX/CUDA stage)"
publish = false

[lib]
name = "verineural"
path = "src/lib.rs"

# Stage 4 still has no Rust dependencies; NVIDIA driver is loaded dynamically.
# llc is supplied by flake.nix, and GPU execution requires a system NVIDIA driver.

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/auto_architecture.rs
//! Independent architecture consumer: define reusable local modules, wire a
//! fork/fan-in graph, then verify all selected outputs and a global goal and
//! emit NVPTX without manually invoking either backend for each component.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    ArchitectureAutoCompiler, ArchitectureProofTask, ContractClaim, Domain, GpuRequirement,
    MathContract, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NeuralModule, NodeId, PortContract, ProofGoal,
    ProofGoalKind, Shape,
};

struct Activated {
    contract: MathContract,
}
impl NeuralModule for Activated {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "consumer_activation"
    }
    fn semantic_version(&self) -> &'static str {
        "1.0"
    }
    fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract {
        &self.contract
    }
    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        graph.relu(inputs[0])
    }
}

struct Merge {
    contract: MathContract,
}
impl NeuralModule for Merge {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "consumer_merge"
    }
    fn semantic_version(&self) -> &'static str {
        "1.0"
    }
    fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract {
        &self.contract
    }
    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        graph.add(inputs[0], inputs[1])
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let args = std::env::args().skip(1).collect::<Vec<_>>();
    let pinned = match args.as_slice() {
        [] => None,
        [command] if command == "--verify" => None,
        [command, option, digest] if command == "--verify" && option == "--pinned-sha256" => {
            Some(digest.as_str())
        }
        _ => {
            return Err(
                "usage: auto_architecture [--verify [--pinned-sha256 <64-hex-digest>]]".into(),
            );
        }
    };
    let verify = !args.is_empty();
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![4])?;
    let finite = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let nonnegative = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let any = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::Any);
    let activated = Activated {
        contract: MathContract::new(vec![finite], nonnegative.clone())
            .with_claim(ContractClaim::Nonnegative),
    };
    let merge = Merge {
        contract: MathContract::new(vec![nonnegative.clone(), nonnegative], any)
            .with_claim(ContractClaim::Nonnegative),
    };

    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let signal = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let parameter = graph.input(shape, Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let left = graph.apply_module(&activated, &[signal])?;
    let right = graph.apply_module(&activated, &[parameter])?;
    let output = graph.apply_module(&merge, &[left, right])?;

    let tasks = vec![
        ArchitectureProofTask::Goal(ProofGoal {
            name: "merged_nonnegative".to_owned(),
            output,
            kind: ProofGoalKind::Nonnegative {
                assumptions: Vec::new(),
            },
        }),
        ArchitectureProofTask::Goal(ProofGoal {
            name: "left_nonnegative".to_owned(),
            output: left,
            kind: ProofGoalKind::Nonnegative {
                assumptions: Vec::new(),
            },
        }),
    ];
    let compiler = ArchitectureAutoCompiler::default();
    let root = Path::new("target/verineural/auto-architecture");
    let outputs = [left, right, output];
    let report = if verify {
        compiler.verify_bundle(
            &graph,
            &outputs,
            &tasks,
            GpuRequirement::AllOutputs,
            root,
            pinned,
        )?
    } else {
        compiler.build(&graph, &outputs, &tasks, GpuRequirement::AllOutputs, root)?
    };
    println!(
        "Wiring: {} edges, {} bound module ports, {} instances; \
         checked {} architecture theorems and {} independent goal(s)",
        report.connectivity.data_edges,
        report.connectivity.module_ports,
        report.connectivity.module_instances,
        report.architecture_theorems,
        report.goal_theorems.len(),
    );
    for artifact in &report.output_evidence {
        println!("GPU output {}: {:?}", artifact.node, artifact.ptx);
    }
    println!("Report: {}", report.directory.join("report.txt").display());
    println!(
        "SHA256SUMS digest (pin externally): {}",
        report.manifest_sha256
    );
    if verify && pinned.is_none() {
        println!(
            "Provenance: unpinned replay checks current Rust IR and all bundle contents, not external authenticity"
        );
    }
    println!(
        "Assurance: Lean ideal-Int and structural PTX translation only; GPU machine semantics not proven"
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/gated_select.rs
//! Consumer-defined gated state update over generic mask and selection IR.
//! Produces a Lean-checked fixed-horizon ideal-Int invariant, while binary32
//! RNE and NVPTX lowering remain explicitly unsupported for these new ops.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    ContractClaim, Domain, GpuEngine, GpuError, LeanProofEngine, MultiOutputContract,
    MultiOutputModule, NamedPortContract, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NodeId, PortContract, Shape,
    Tensor,
};

struct GatedUpdate {
    interface: MultiOutputContract,
}

impl MultiOutputModule for GatedUpdate {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "consumer_gated_update"
    }
    fn contract(&self) -> &MultiOutputContract {
        &self.interface
    }
    fn semantic_version(&self) -> &'static str {
        "1.0"
    }

    fn build(
        &self,
        graph: &mut NeuralGraph,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError> {
        let mask = graph.positive_mask(inputs[1])?;
        let next_state = graph.select_positive(mask, inputs[1], inputs[0])?;
        let readout = graph.relu(next_state)?;
        Ok(vec![next_state, readout])
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![3])?;
    let positive = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let named = |name| NamedPortContract::new(name, positive.clone());
    let module = GatedUpdate {
        interface: MultiOutputContract {
            inputs: vec![named("state"), named("input")],
            outputs: vec![
                NamedPortContract {
                    name: "next_state",
                    port: positive.clone(),
                    claims: vec![ContractClaim::Nonnegative],
                },
                named("output"),
            ],
        },
    };

    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let initial = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let first = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let second = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let scan = graph.scan_fixed(&module, initial, &[first, second])?;
    let checker = LeanProofEngine::default();
    let lean = checker.generate_fixed_scan_nonnegative(&graph, &scan, "gated")?;
    let file = Path::new("target/verineural/verification/gated_select.lean");
    let (checked, audit) = checker.verify_certified(&lean, file)?;

    // An independent concrete host-reference fixture, not an FP32 theorem.
    let mask = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![-1.0f32, 0.0, f32::NAN])?;
    let yes = Tensor::new(shape.clone(), vec![1.0, 2.0, 3.0])?;
    let no = Tensor::new(shape, vec![4.0, 5.0, 6.0])?;
    assert_eq!(mask.positive_mask().values(), &[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]);
    assert_eq!(mask.select_positive(&yes, &no)?.values(), &[4.0, 5.0, 6.0]);

    for output in &scan.outputs {
        assert!(matches!(
            GpuEngine::default().compile(&graph, *output),
            Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation { .. })
        ));
    }
    println!(
        "Lean checked {} theorems (H=2); assumptions={}; axioms={:?}",
        checked.theorem_names.len(),
        checked.assumptions.len(),
        audit
            .axiom_dependencies
            .values()
            .flatten()
            .collect::<std::collections::BTreeSet<_>>()
    );
    println!(
        "Assurance: ideal-Int bounded invariant; f32 mask reference checked; RNE/GPU lowering unsupported"
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/multi_output_gpu.rs
//! One CUDA Graph computes four declared outputs with one shared producer.
//! Lean certifies only the ideal-Int model, not NVIDIA FP32 machine behavior.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{Domain, GpuEngine, LeanProofEngine, NeuralGraph, Shape, Tensor};

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![4])?;
    let x = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let y = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    let common = graph.add(x, y)?;
    let activated = graph.relu(common)?;
    let weighted = graph.mul(common, y)?;
    let output = graph.add(activated, weighted)?;
    let outputs = [common, activated, weighted, output];
    let gpu = GpuEngine::default();
    let shared = gpu.compile_outputs(&graph, &outputs)?;
    let independent = outputs
        .iter()
        .map(|&id| gpu.compile(&graph, id)?.kernel_count())
        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?
        .into_iter()
        .sum::<usize>();
    println!(
        "Shared CUDA Graph: {} kernels vs {} independently compiled kernels",
        shared.kernel_count()?,
        independent
    );
    assert_eq!(shared.kernel_count()?, 4);
    assert!(independent > 4);

    let proof = LeanProofEngine::default().generate_outputs(&graph, &outputs)?;
    let lean = Path::new("target/verineural/multi-output-gpu/multi_output.lean");
    let (checked, axiom_audit) = LeanProofEngine::default().verify_certified(&proof, lean)?;
    println!(
        "Lean checked {} ideal-Int statements, audited {} theorem dependencies",
        checked.theorem_names.len(),
        axiom_audit.axiom_dependencies.len()
    );

    let input = |id, data| Tensor::new(shape.clone(), data).map(|value| (id, value));
    let inputs = [
        input(x, vec![1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0])?,
        input(y, vec![2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0])?,
    ];
    let dir = Path::new("target/verineural/multi-output-gpu/shared");
    let mut execution = gpu.prepare(&shared, &inputs, dir)?;
    execution.replay()?;
    let observed = execution.read_outputs()?;
    let expected: [&[f32]; 4] = [
        &[3.0, 5.0, 7.0, 9.0],
        &[3.0, 5.0, 7.0, 9.0],
        &[6.0, 15.0, 28.0, 45.0],
        &[9.0, 20.0, 35.0, 54.0],
    ];
    for ((id, tensor), (expected_id, oracle)) in
        observed.iter().zip(outputs.iter().zip(expected.iter()))
    {
        assert_eq!(id, expected_id);
        assert_eq!(tensor.values(), *oracle);
    }

    // Replay the exact same captured kernel DAG with a new input batch.
    let changed = [
        input(x, vec![1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0])?,
        input(y, vec![1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0])?,
    ];
    execution.update_inputs(&changed)?;
    execution.replay()?;
    let changed_outputs = execution.read_outputs()?;
    let next_expected: [&[f32]; 4] = [
        &[2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0],
        &[2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0],
        &[2.0, 6.0, 12.0, 20.0],
        &[4.0, 9.0, 16.0, 25.0],
    ];
    for ((id, tensor), (expected_id, oracle)) in changed_outputs
        .iter()
        .zip(outputs.iter().zip(next_expected.iter()))
    {
        assert_eq!(id, expected_id);
        assert_eq!(tensor.values(), *oracle);
    }
    println!("CUDA Graph captured once, replayed twice; four outputs match exact FP32 fixtures.");
    println!(
        "Assurance: conditional ideal-Int Lean; structurally validated PTX; concrete GPU bits tested, not formally proved."
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/scan_invariant.rs
//! Consumer-defined fixed-horizon recurrence with independently checked
//! ideal-Int local claims and a global nonnegative state invariant.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    ContractClaim, Domain, LeanProofEngine, MultiOutputContract, MultiOutputModule,
    NamedPortContract, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NodeId, PortContract, Shape,
};

struct Accumulate {
    contract: MultiOutputContract,
}

impl MultiOutputModule for Accumulate {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "consumer_accumulate"
    }

    fn contract(&self) -> &MultiOutputContract {
        &self.contract
    }

    fn build(
        &self,
        graph: &mut NeuralGraph,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError> {
        // The f32 domain of additions stays Any: they can overflow. The
        // mathematical ideal-Int property is proved separately by Lean.
        let next = graph.add(inputs[0], inputs[1])?;
        let output = graph.relu(next)?;
        Ok(vec![next, output])
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let shape = Shape::new(vec![2])?;
    let any = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::Any);
    let transition = Accumulate {
        contract: MultiOutputContract {
            inputs: vec![
                NamedPortContract::new("state", any.clone()),
                NamedPortContract::new("input", any.clone()),
            ],
            outputs: vec![
                NamedPortContract {
                    name: "next_state",
                    port: any.clone(),
                    claims: vec![ContractClaim::Nonnegative],
                },
                NamedPortContract::new("output", any),
            ],
        },
    };
    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let initial = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let x0 = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let x1 = graph.input(shape, Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let scan = graph.scan_fixed(&transition, initial, &[x0, x1])?;
    let proof =
        LeanProofEngine::default().generate_fixed_scan_nonnegative(&graph, &scan, "accumulator")?;
    let output = Path::new("target/verineural/verification/scan_invariant.lean");
    let (checked, audit) = LeanProofEngine::default().verify_certified(&proof, output)?;
    println!(
        "Lean certified {} theorems in {}; bounded horizon {}, conditional source hypotheses {}, reviewed axioms {:?}",
        checked.theorem_names.len(),
        checked.path.display(),
        scan.outputs.len(),
        checked.assumptions.len(),
        audit
            .axiom_dependencies
            .values()
            .flatten()
            .collect::<std::collections::BTreeSet<_>>(),
    );
    println!(
        "Assurance: ideal-Int bounded invariant only; no FP32, GPU or unbounded induction proof"
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/stateful_model_gpu.rs
//! GPU acceptance for explicit named state feedback.
//!
//! One pure multi-output Model is compiled/captured once. Each step replays
//! the same CUDA Graph and transfers next_state into the state input on-device.
//! All expected values are independent, exactly representable FP32 fixtures.
//! This checks concrete GPU behavior, not Lean/IEEE/SASS equivalence.

use std::error::Error;
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    Domain, GpuEngine, GpuError, ModelBuilder, ModelExecution, ModelExecutionError, Tensor,
};

const WIDTH: usize = 4;

fn tensor(values: [f32; WIDTH]) -> Result<Tensor<f32>, Box<dyn Error>> {
    Ok(Tensor::from_vec([WIDTH], values.to_vec())?)
}

fn expect_bits(phase: &str, name: &str, actual: &Tensor<f32>, expected: [f32; WIDTH]) {
    let actual_bits = actual
        .values()
        .iter()
        .map(|v| v.to_bits())
        .collect::<Vec<_>>();
    let expected_bits = expected.iter().map(|v| v.to_bits()).collect::<Vec<_>>();
    assert_eq!(actual.shape().dims(), &[WIDTH], "{phase}: {name} shape");
    assert_eq!(actual_bits, expected_bits, "{phase}: {name} FP32 bits");
}

fn check(
    execution: &mut ModelExecution,
    phase: &str,
    state: [f32; WIDTH],
    increment: [f32; WIDTH],
    readout: [f32; WIDTH],
) -> Result<(), Box<dyn Error>> {
    expect_bits(phase, "state", &execution.state("state")?, state);
    expect_bits(
        phase,
        "increment",
        &execution.output("increment")?,
        increment,
    );
    expect_bits(phase, "readout", &execution.output("readout")?, readout);
    Ok(())
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn Error>> {
    let mut builder = ModelBuilder::new("stateful-gpu-fixture", "1");
    let state = builder.state("state", [WIDTH], Domain::Any)?;
    let token = builder.input("token", [WIDTH], Domain::Finite)?;
    let gain = builder.parameter("gain", [WIDTH], Domain::Finite)?;

    // next = state + token*gain; readout = next + gain.
    // This is consumer composition, not a built-in recurrent network.
    let ports = builder.block_multi(
        "affine_transition",
        &[("state", state), ("token", token), ("gain", gain)],
        &["next_state", "readout", "increment"],
        |graph, values| {
            let increment = graph.mul(values[1], values[2])?;
            let next = graph.add(values[0], increment)?;
            let readout = graph.add(next, values[2])?;
            Ok(vec![next, readout, increment])
        },
    )?;
    builder.next_state("state", ports["next_state"])?;
    builder.output("increment", ports["increment"])?;
    builder.output("readout", ports["readout"])?;

    let model = builder.finish()?;
    assert_eq!(model.state_links().len(), 1);
    assert_eq!(model.outputs().len(), 2);
    assert_eq!(model.graph().multi_modules().len(), 1);

    let gpu = GpuEngine::default();
    let mut execution = gpu.prepare_model(
        &model,
        [
            ("state", tensor([0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0])?),
            ("token", tensor([1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0])?),
            ("gain", tensor([2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0])?),
        ],
        Path::new("target/verineural/stateful-model-gpu"),
    )?;

    // Output allocation is not an executed value. Even if a source alias
    // exists, public output reads require a completed pure replay.
    assert!(matches!(
        execution.output("readout"),
        Err(ModelExecutionError::Gpu(GpuError::OutputNotReady))
    ));

    // run() leaves temporal state unchanged; next_state is deliberately NOT
    // a public model output and must still be compiled for state feedback.
    execution.run()?;
    check(
        &mut execution,
        "run without feedback",
        [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0],
        [2.0, 6.0, 12.0, 20.0],
        [4.0, 9.0, 16.0, 25.0],
    )?;

    execution.step()?;
    check(
        &mut execution,
        "step 1",
        [2.0, 6.0, 12.0, 20.0],
        [2.0, 6.0, 12.0, 20.0],
        [4.0, 9.0, 16.0, 25.0],
    )?;

    // Invalid named roles, shapes and non-finite input values must not
    // mutate the previously bound state, token or parameter buffers.
    assert!(execution.set_input("gain", &tensor([1.0; WIDTH])?).is_err());
    assert!(
        execution
            .set_parameter("token", &tensor([1.0; WIDTH])?)
            .is_err()
    );
    assert!(execution.set_state("gain", &tensor([1.0; WIDTH])?).is_err());
    assert!(
        execution
            .set_input("token", &Tensor::from_vec([2], vec![1.0, 2.0])?)
            .is_err()
    );
    assert!(
        execution
            .set_input("token", &tensor([1.0, f32::NAN, 1.0, 1.0])?)
            .is_err()
    );
    expect_bits(
        "rejected writes",
        "state",
        &execution.state("state")?,
        [2.0, 6.0, 12.0, 20.0],
    );

    // Only the token is uploaded. gain and accumulated state stay on-device.
    execution.set_input("token", &tensor([2.0, 1.0, 0.0, 3.0])?)?;
    assert!(matches!(
        execution.output("readout"),
        Err(ModelExecutionError::Gpu(GpuError::OutputNotReady))
    ));
    execution.step()?;
    check(
        &mut execution,
        "step 2, new token",
        [6.0, 9.0, 12.0, 35.0],
        [4.0, 3.0, 0.0, 15.0],
        [8.0, 12.0, 16.0, 40.0],
    )?;

    // No rebind whatsoever: unchanged gain and token, new accumulated state.
    execution.step()?;
    check(
        &mut execution,
        "step 3, persistent parameter",
        [10.0, 12.0, 12.0, 50.0],
        [4.0, 3.0, 0.0, 15.0],
        [12.0, 15.0, 16.0, 55.0],
    )?;

    // Explicit named parameter update must affect the very next replay
    // without recompilation or CUDA Graph reconstruction.
    execution.set_parameter("gain", &tensor([3.0, 2.0, 1.0, 4.0])?)?;
    assert!(matches!(
        execution.output("increment"),
        Err(ModelExecutionError::Gpu(GpuError::OutputNotReady))
    ));
    execution.step()?;
    check(
        &mut execution,
        "step 4, replaced parameter",
        [16.0, 14.0, 12.0, 62.0],
        [6.0, 2.0, 0.0, 12.0],
        [19.0, 16.0, 13.0, 66.0],
    )?;

    // Explicit state reset and a new token use the same captured graph.
    execution.set_state("state", &tensor([5.0, 4.0, 3.0, 2.0])?)?;
    execution.set_input("token", &tensor([1.0; WIDTH])?)?;
    execution.step()?;
    check(
        &mut execution,
        "step 5, state reset",
        [8.0, 6.0, 4.0, 6.0],
        [3.0, 2.0, 1.0, 4.0],
        [11.0, 8.0, 5.0, 10.0],
    )?;

    // Exercise the P0 cases that the ordinary additive state transition
    // cannot detect: unreachable state storage and aliasing public outputs.
    check_replacement_and_aliased_outputs(&gpu)?;

    // A new session would require another prepare_model call. This fixture
    // deliberately holds one ModelExecution for all six GPU replays.
    println!(
        "Stateful CUDA Graph: one capture, run + five steps; \
         next_state feedback, persistent parameters, named updates and reset \
         match exact FP32 fixtures."
    );
    println!(
        "Assurance: concrete GPU bit checks; no formal CUDA D2D, IEEE-754, \
         JIT/SASS or recurrent convergence proof."
    );
    Ok(())
}

/// Regression: both states are replaced with token, so neither is needed
/// for the pure computation. "hidden" is not a public output at all;
/// "visible" is public both directly and through a zero-copy reshape.
fn check_replacement_and_aliased_outputs(gpu: &GpuEngine) -> Result<(), Box<dyn Error>> {
    let mut builder = ModelBuilder::new("state-replacement-and-alias", "1");
    let _hidden = builder.state("hidden", [WIDTH], Domain::Any)?;
    let visible = builder.state("visible", [WIDTH], Domain::Any)?;
    let token = builder.input("token", [WIDTH], Domain::Finite)?;
    let gain = builder.parameter("gain", [WIDTH], Domain::Finite)?;
    let view = builder
        .graph_mut()
        .reshape(visible, verineural::Shape::new([2, 2])?)?;
    let scaled = builder.graph_mut().mul(token, gain)?;
    builder.next_state("hidden", token)?;
    builder.next_state("visible", token)?;
    builder.output("previous", visible)?;
    builder.output("previous_view", view)?;
    builder.output("scaled", scaled)?;
    let model = builder.finish()?;

    let mut execution = gpu.prepare_model(
        &model,
        [
            ("hidden", tensor([100.0, 101.0, 102.0, 103.0])?),
            ("visible", tensor([8.0, 9.0, 10.0, 11.0])?),
            ("token", tensor([1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0])?),
            ("gain", tensor([2.0; WIDTH])?),
        ],
        Path::new("target/verineural/stateful-model-gpu/replacement"),
    )?;

    assert!(matches!(
        execution.output("previous"),
        Err(ModelExecutionError::Gpu(GpuError::OutputNotReady))
    ));
    execution.run()?;
    expect_bits(
        "replacement run",
        "hidden",
        &execution.state("hidden")?,
        [100.0, 101.0, 102.0, 103.0],
    );
    expect_bits(
        "replacement run",
        "previous",
        &execution.output("previous")?,
        [8.0, 9.0, 10.0, 11.0],
    );
    execution.step()?;
    // Public output must represent the pre-feedback pure DAG evaluation,
    // while both inputs to the next step contain the new token.
    expect_bits(
        "replacement step 1",
        "hidden",
        &execution.state("hidden")?,
        [1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0],
    );
    expect_bits(
        "replacement step 1",
        "visible",
        &execution.state("visible")?,
        [1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0],
    );
    expect_bits(
        "replacement step 1",
        "previous",
        &execution.output("previous")?,
        [8.0, 9.0, 10.0, 11.0],
    );
    let view = execution.output("previous_view")?;
    assert_eq!(view.shape().dims(), &[2, 2]);
    assert_eq!(
        view.values()
            .iter()
            .map(|v| v.to_bits())
            .collect::<Vec<_>>(),
        [8.0f32, 9.0, 10.0, 11.0]
            .iter()
            .map(|v| v.to_bits())
            .collect::<Vec<_>>(),
        "zero-copy reshape alias must be a pre-feedback snapshot",
    );
    expect_bits(
        "replacement step 1",
        "scaled",
        &execution.output("scaled")?,
        [2.0, 4.0, 6.0, 8.0],
    );

    execution.set_input("token", &tensor([5.0, 6.0, 7.0, 8.0])?)?;
    execution.step()?;
    expect_bits(
        "replacement step 2",
        "previous",
        &execution.output("previous")?,
        [1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0],
    );
    expect_bits(
        "replacement step 2",
        "hidden",
        &execution.state("hidden")?,
        [5.0, 6.0, 7.0, 8.0],
    );
    expect_bits(
        "replacement step 2",
        "visible",
        &execution.state("visible")?,
        [5.0, 6.0, 7.0, 8.0],
    );
    expect_bits(
        "replacement step 2",
        "scaled",
        &execution.output("scaled")?,
        [10.0, 12.0, 14.0, 16.0],
    );

    // run() refreshes the public snapshot but does not move state.
    execution.run()?;
    expect_bits(
        "replacement run after feedback",
        "previous",
        &execution.output("previous")?,
        [5.0, 6.0, 7.0, 8.0],
    );
    expect_bits(
        "replacement run after feedback",
        "hidden",
        &execution.state("hidden")?,
        [5.0, 6.0, 7.0, 8.0],
    );
    println!(
        "P0 GPU regressions: unreachable state destinations are live; \
         public state/reshape outputs preserve pre-feedback FP32 bits."
    );
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/examples/symbolic_shapes.rs
//! One consumer-owned symbolic MatMul module instantiated at different shapes.
//! Lean proves an ideal-Int output claim, LLVM NVPTX generates two PTX programs.
//! No IEEE-754 / JIT / GPU machine equivalence is claimed.
use std::path::Path;

use verineural::{
    ContractClaim, Dimension, DimensionConstraint, Domain, GpuEngine, LeanProofEngine, NeuralError,
    NeuralGraph, NodeId, ParametricModule, ParametricSignature, Shape, SymbolicPort, SymbolicShape,
};

struct GenericMatMul {
    signature: ParametricSignature,
}

impl ParametricModule for GenericMatMul {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        "consumer_matmul"
    }
    fn semantic_version(&self) -> &'static str {
        "1.0"
    }
    fn signature(&self) -> &ParametricSignature {
        &self.signature
    }
    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        graph.matmul(inputs[0], inputs[1])
    }
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let port = |dims| SymbolicPort::new(SymbolicShape::new(dims), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
    let matmul = GenericMatMul {
        signature: ParametricSignature {
            inputs: vec![
                port(vec![Dimension::Symbol("m"), Dimension::Symbol("k")]),
                port(vec![Dimension::Symbol("k"), Dimension::Symbol("n")]),
            ],
            output: SymbolicPort::new(
                SymbolicShape::new(vec![Dimension::Symbol("m"), Dimension::Symbol("n")]),
                Domain::Any,
            ),
            constraints: vec![
                DimensionConstraint::AtLeast("m", 2),
                DimensionConstraint::AtMost("k", 16),
            ],
            claims: vec![ContractClaim::Nonnegative],
        },
    };
    let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
    let mut outputs = Vec::new();
    for (m, k, n) in [(2, 3, 4), (5, 3, 2)] {
        let a = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![m, k])?, Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
        let b = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![k, n])?, Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
        let (output, bindings) = graph.apply_parametric_module(&matmul, &[a, b])?;
        println!(
            "specialized {bindings:?} -> {:?}",
            graph.node(output)?.shape.dims()
        );
        outputs.push(output);
    }

    let checker = LeanProofEngine::default();
    let proof = checker.generate_outputs(&graph, &outputs)?;
    let root = Path::new("target/verineural/verification/symbolic");
    let (checked, audit) = checker.verify_certified(&proof, &root.join("symbols.lean"))?;
    println!(
        "Lean checked {} obligations with axiom policy {:?}",
        checked.theorem_names.len(),
        audit
            .axiom_dependencies
            .values()
            .flatten()
            .collect::<std::collections::BTreeSet<_>>()
    );

    let gpu = GpuEngine::default();
    for (i, output) in outputs.into_iter().enumerate() {
        let program = gpu.compile(&graph, output)?;
        let ptx = gpu.lower(&program, &root.join(format!("profile_{i}")))?;
        println!("NVPTX translated specialization {i}: {}", ptx.display());
    }
    println!("Assurance: ideal Int under source hypotheses; GPU machine semantics remain trusted");
    Ok(())
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/architecture.rs
//! Deterministic, architecture-neutral Semantic IR and complete Graphviz export.
//!
//! Export is a representation and integrity aid, NOT a proof that LLVM/PTX,
//! CUDA JIT or the GPU implements the graph's Lean/FP32 semantics. All nodes,
//! including unreachable ones, are displayed, and nested module boundaries
//! remain visible. Source input roles are caller-declared metadata.

use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};
use std::fmt::Write as _;
use std::fs;
use std::io::{self, Write as _};
use std::path::Path;
use std::process::{Command, Stdio};
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU64, Ordering};

use crate::{GpuProgram, ModuleInstanceRef, NeuralGraph, NodeId, Operation};

/// Stable provenance and presentation metadata for one architecture.
/// Input, parameter and temporal state are metadata on the same pure IR source.
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct ArchitectureMetadata {
    pub id: String,
    pub version: String,
    pub input_roles: BTreeMap<usize, String>,
    pub global_property: String,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct ArchitectureSnapshot {
    pub semantic_ir: String,
    pub dot: String,
    pub ir_sha256: String,
}

fn bad(message: impl Into<String>) -> io::Error {
    io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::InvalidData, message.into())
}

fn sha256(data: &[u8]) -> io::Result<String> {
    let mut process = Command::new("sha256sum")
        .stdin(Stdio::piped())
        .stdout(Stdio::piped())
        .stderr(Stdio::piped())
        .spawn()?;
    process
        .stdin
        .take()
        .ok_or_else(|| bad("sha256sum stdin unavailable"))?
        .write_all(data)?;
    let result = process.wait_with_output()?;
    if !result.status.success() {
        return Err(bad("sha256sum rejected Semantic IR input"));
    }
    let printed = String::from_utf8(result.stdout).map_err(|_| bad("invalid sha256sum output"))?;
    let digest = printed.split_whitespace().next().unwrap_or("");
    if digest.len() != 64 || !digest.bytes().all(|b| b.is_ascii_hexdigit()) {
        return Err(bad("sha256sum did not return a full SHA-256 digest"));
    }
    Ok(digest.to_owned())
}

fn quoted(s: &str) -> String {
    let mut out = String::from("\"");
    for c in s.chars() {
        match c {
            '"' => out.push_str("\\\""),
            '\\' => out.push_str("\\\\"),
            '\n' => out.push_str("\\n"),
            '\r' => out.push_str("\\r"),
            '\t' => out.push_str("\\t"),
            c if c.is_control() => out.push(' '),
            c => out.push(c),
        }
    }
    out.push('"');
    out
}

fn attrs(pairs: &[(&str, String)]) -> String {
    pairs
        .iter()
        .map(|(key, value)| format!("{key}={}", quoted(value)))
        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
        .join(", ")
}

/// A presentation-only theme. Canonical vn_* attributes remain independent of
/// color, DPI, font, and the Graphviz layout algorithm.
fn node_theme(kind: &str, op: &Operation) -> (&'static str, &'static str) {
    match kind {
        "input" => ("#EAF2FF", "#3972BD"),
        "parameter" => ("#FFF1DB", "#B9772A"),
        "state" => ("#E9F6F5", "#36827C"),
        "architecture_output" => ("#DDF8E9", "#26805A"),
        _ => match op {
            Operation::Add => ("#F1F5F9", "#64748B"),
            Operation::Mul => ("#EEF2FF", "#6477B5"),
            Operation::BiasAdd => ("#FDEEF3", "#B76A91"),
            Operation::Relu => ("#F0EDFF", "#8160BF"),
            Operation::MatMul => ("#E8F5FE", "#4C90B5"),
            _ => ("#FFFFFF", "#64748B"),
        },
    }
}

fn operation_title(operation: &Operation) -> &'static str {
    match operation {
        Operation::Input => "Input",
        Operation::Add => "Add",
        Operation::Mul => "Multiply",
        Operation::BiasAdd => "Bias add",
        Operation::Relu => "ReLU",
        Operation::PositiveMask => "Positive mask",
        Operation::SelectPositive => "Select positive",
        Operation::MatMul => "MatMul",
        Operation::Sqrt => "Sqrt",
        Operation::Reshape(_) => "Reshape",
        Operation::Pointwise(_) => "User-defined pointwise",
        Operation::ReduceSum { .. } => "Reduce sum",
        Operation::ReduceMax { .. } => "Reduce max",
        Operation::BroadcastTo(_) => "Broadcast",
        Operation::Permute { .. } => "Permute",
        Operation::ReverseAxis { .. } => "Reverse axis",
        Operation::Concat { .. } => "Concat",
        Operation::SliceAxis { .. } => "Slice axis",
        Operation::ArgMax { .. } => "Argmax",
        Operation::Take { .. } => "Take",
    }
}

fn cluster_theme(depth: usize) -> (&'static str, &'static str) {
    match depth % 3 {
        0 => ("#F5F8FF", "#93A9D4"),
        1 => ("#F1F5FD", "#A4B4CB"),
        _ => ("#F8FAFD", "#BCC8D7"),
    }
}

/// Distinguish parameter and tensor edges without forcing compass ports.
/// Graphviz can then place endpoints to minimize crossings.
fn edge_theme(role: &str, input_port: usize) -> (&'static str, &'static str) {
    if role == "parameter" {
        ("#C58A3A", "1.35")
    } else {
        let color = match input_port {
            0 => "#7489A8",
            1 => "#95A3B5",
            _ => "#8496AD",
        };
        (color, "1.15")
    }
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
struct ModuleScope {
    id: String,
    name: &'static str,
    version: &'static str,
    start: usize,
    end: usize,
    inputs: Vec<(String, usize)>,
    outputs: Vec<(String, usize)>,
    contract: String,
    requires: String,
    ensures: String,
    claims: String,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
struct ModuleLayout {
    scopes: Vec<ModuleScope>,
    parents: Vec<Option<usize>>,
    paths: Vec<String>,
    owners: Vec<Option<usize>>,
}

fn module_layout(graph: &NeuralGraph) -> io::Result<ModuleLayout> {
    let mut scopes = Vec::new();
    for (sequence, module) in graph.module_instances().enumerate() {
        match module {
            ModuleInstanceRef::Single(module) => scopes.push(ModuleScope {
                id: format!("m{sequence}"),
                name: module.name,
                version: module.semantic_version,
                start: module.body_start,
                end: module.body_end,
                inputs: module
                    .inputs
                    .iter()
                    .enumerate()
                    .map(|(port, id)| (format!("input_{port}"), id.index()))
                    .collect(),
                outputs: vec![("output".to_owned(), module.output.index())],
                contract: format!("{:?}", module.contract),
                requires: format!("{:?}", module.contract.requires),
                ensures: format!("{:?}", module.contract.ensures),
                claims: format!("{:?}", module.contract.claims),
            }),
            ModuleInstanceRef::Multi(module) => scopes.push(ModuleScope {
                id: format!("m{sequence}"),
                name: module.name,
                version: module.semantic_version,
                start: module.body_start,
                end: module.body_end,
                inputs: module
                    .inputs
                    .iter()
                    .zip(&module.contract.inputs)
                    .map(|(id, port)| (port.name.to_owned(), id.index()))
                    .collect(),
                outputs: module
                    .outputs
                    .iter()
                    .zip(&module.contract.outputs)
                    .map(|(id, port)| (port.name.to_owned(), id.index()))
                    .collect(),
                contract: format!("{:?}", module.contract),
                requires: format!("{:?}", module.contract.inputs),
                ensures: format!("{:?}", module.contract.outputs),
                claims: format!(
                    "{:?}",
                    module
                        .contract
                        .outputs
                        .iter()
                        .map(|port| (&port.name, &port.claims))
                        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                ),
            }),
        }
    }

    let node_count = graph.nodes().len();
    for scope in &scopes {
        if scope.start >= scope.end || scope.end > node_count {
            return Err(bad("module contains invalid node interval"));
        }
        if scope
            .outputs
            .iter()
            .any(|(_, output)| *output < scope.start || *output >= scope.end)
        {
            return Err(bad("module output lies outside its owned body"));
        }
    }

    let mut parents = vec![None; scopes.len()];
    for (i, scope) in scopes.iter().enumerate() {
        let mut candidates = Vec::new();
        for (j, other) in scopes.iter().enumerate() {
            if i == j {
                continue;
            }
            let overlaps = scope.start < other.end && other.start < scope.end;
            let contained = other.start <= scope.start && scope.end <= other.end;
            let contains = scope.start <= other.start && other.end <= scope.end;
            if overlaps && !contained && !contains {
                return Err(bad("crossing module body intervals"));
            }
            if contained && (!contains || j > i) {
                candidates.push(j);
            }
        }
        candidates.sort_by_key(|&j| (scopes[j].end - scopes[j].start, j));
        parents[i] = candidates.first().copied();
    }

    fn path_of(i: usize, scopes: &[ModuleScope], parents: &[Option<usize>]) -> String {
        let local = format!("{}_{}", scopes[i].id, scopes[i].name);
        parents[i].map_or_else(
            || local.clone(),
            |parent| format!("{}/{}", path_of(parent, scopes, parents), local),
        )
    }

    let paths = (0..scopes.len())
        .map(|index| path_of(index, &scopes, &parents))
        .collect::<Vec<_>>();
    let owners = (0..node_count)
        .map(|node| {
            (0..scopes.len())
                .filter(|&scope| node >= scopes[scope].start && node < scopes[scope].end)
                .min_by_key(|&scope| (scopes[scope].end - scopes[scope].start, scope))
        })
        .collect::<Vec<_>>();

    Ok(ModuleLayout {
        scopes,
        parents,
        paths,
        owners,
    })
}

fn source_is_outside_scope(source: usize, scope: &ModuleScope) -> bool {
    source < scope.start || source >= scope.end
}

/// All architecture writers invoke the same Graphviz executable from the
/// pinned Nix environment. PNG is always derived from the saved DOT.
pub(crate) fn render_dot_png(dot: &Path, png: &Path) -> io::Result<()> {
    let tmp = png.with_extension("png.tmp");
    let output = Command::new("dot")
        .arg("-Tpng")
        .arg(dot)
        .arg("-o")
        .arg(&tmp)
        .output()?;
    if !output.status.success() {
        let _ = fs::remove_file(&tmp);
        return Err(bad(format!(
            "Graphviz failed: {}",
            String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stderr)
        )));
    }
    fs::rename(tmp, png)?;
    Ok(())
}

/// Re-render from saved DOT and compare bytes, not just presence or checksums.
/// The unique sibling path avoids trampling another verifier's temporary image.
pub(crate) fn verify_rendered_dot_png(dot: &Path, png: &Path) -> io::Result<()> {
    static NEXT_REPLAY: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);
    let id = NEXT_REPLAY.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);
    let replay = dot.with_file_name(format!(
        ".verineural-png-replay-{}-{id}.png",
        std::process::id()
    ));
    let result = (|| {
        render_dot_png(dot, &replay)?;
        if fs::read(&replay)? != fs::read(png)? {
            return Err(bad(
                "architecture.png differs from Graphviz rendering of saved DOT",
            ));
        }
        Ok(())
    })();
    let _ = fs::remove_file(&replay);
    result
}

impl ArchitectureSnapshot {
    /// Re-render the pinned DOT with Graphviz into architecture.png.
    /// Only the configured artifact root receives writes.
    pub fn write(&self, root: &Path) -> io::Result<()> {
        fs::create_dir_all(root)?;
        fs::write(root.join("semantic.ir"), &self.semantic_ir)?;
        fs::write(root.join("architecture.dot"), &self.dot)?;
        render_dot_png(
            &root.join("architecture.dot"),
            &root.join("architecture.png"),
        )
    }

    /// Checks the exact deterministic Semantic IR and DOT content independently
    /// of the SHA-256 artifact manifest verified by the consumer.
    pub fn verify(&self, root: &Path) -> io::Result<()> {
        if fs::read_to_string(root.join("semantic.ir"))? != self.semantic_ir
            || fs::read_to_string(root.join("architecture.dot"))? != self.dot
        {
            return Err(bad(
                "architecture IR or DOT disagrees with current Rust graph",
            ));
        }
        if !self
            .dot
            .contains(&format!("vn_ir_sha256={}", quoted(&self.ir_sha256)))
        {
            return Err(bad(
                "architecture DOT lacks matching Semantic IR fingerprint",
            ));
        }
        verify_rendered_dot_png(
            &root.join("architecture.dot"),
            &root.join("architecture.png"),
        )
    }
}

/// Export all nodes, all module instances and the selected output.
/// The GPU plan is derived from the SAME IR, not from LLVM/PTX textual output.
pub fn snapshot_architecture(
    graph: &NeuralGraph,
    output: NodeId,
    plan: &GpuProgram,
    metadata: &ArchitectureMetadata,
) -> io::Result<ArchitectureSnapshot> {
    graph.node(output).map_err(|err| bad(err.to_string()))?;
    if plan.output().index() != output.index() {
        return Err(bad(
            "GPU program output differs from requested architecture output",
        ));
    }
    for v in [&metadata.id, &metadata.version] {
        if v.is_empty()
            || !v
                .chars()
                .all(|c| c.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || "-._".contains(c))
        {
            return Err(bad(
                "architecture id/version must use ASCII alphanumeric, - . _",
            ));
        }
    }
    for (&idx, role) in &metadata.input_roles {
        if !matches!(
            graph.nodes().get(idx).map(|node| &node.operation),
            Some(Operation::Input)
        ) || !matches!(role.as_str(), "input" | "parameter" | "state")
        {
            return Err(bad(
                "unsupported input role or non-input node role assignment",
            ));
        }
    }
    if graph.nodes().iter().enumerate().any(|(idx, node)| {
        matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input) && !metadata.input_roles.contains_key(&idx)
    }) {
        return Err(bad(
            "every architecture source input needs an explicit input/parameter/state role",
        ));
    }
    if metadata.global_property != "architecture_global_nonnegative" {
        return Err(bad(
            "only explicit, proved ideal-Int global nonnegativity is supported",
        ));
    }
    let gpu = plan.translation_plan().map_err(|e| bad(e.to_string()))?;
    let ir = graph.canonical_ir();
    let digest = sha256(ir.as_bytes())?;

    let layout = module_layout(graph)?;
    let scopes = &layout.scopes;
    let parents = &layout.parents;
    let paths = &layout.paths;
    let owners = &layout.owners;
    let reachable = graph
        .dependency_scope(&[output])
        .map_err(|err| bad(err.to_string()))?;
    let kernel_map: BTreeMap<_, _> = gpu.kernels.iter().map(|k| (k.node, k)).collect();
    let fused: BTreeSet<_> = plan
        .fused_relus()
        .values()
        .copied()
        .chain(
            plan.fused_pointwise_chains()
                .values()
                .flat_map(|x| x.iter().copied()),
        )
        .collect();
    // Visual topology is the real IR DAG, not a second network of relays.
    // Automatic edge ports let dot optimize crossing count and edge lengths.
    // DPI belongs in DOT so rerendering via plain "dot -Tpng" is consistent.
    let mut dot = String::from(
        r##"digraph verineural {
  graph [rankdir=LR, compound=true, newrank=true, splines=spline,
         concentrate=false, outputorder=edgesfirst, mclimit=4,
         nodesep=0.75, ranksep=1.15, pad=0.60, margin=0.18, dpi=180,
         bgcolor="#FFFFFF", fontname="DejaVu Sans", fontcolor="#24324B",
         labelloc=t, labeljust=l];
  node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="DejaVu Sans",
        fontsize=12, fontcolor="#24324B", penwidth=1.5, margin="0.17,0.13"];
  edge [color="#8796AA", penwidth=1.1, arrowsize=0.72];
"##,
    );
    writeln!(
        dot,
        "  label={};",
        quoted(&format!(
            "{}  ·  architecture v{}\nSemantic IR · FP32 · module composition",
            metadata.id.replace('-', " "),
            metadata.version
        ))
    )
    .expect("writing to string");
    for (key, value) in [
        ("vn_export_version", "3".to_owned()),
        ("vn_architecture_id", metadata.id.clone()),
        ("vn_architecture_version", metadata.version.clone()),
        ("vn_ir_sha256", digest.clone()),
        ("vn_fp32_profile", format!("{:?}", graph.policy())),
        ("vn_global_property", metadata.global_property.clone()),
        ("vn_global_proof", "Lean-check-required".into()),
        (
            "vn_gpu_assurance",
            "structural-LLVM-PTX-validation;JIT-SASS-trusted".into(),
        ),
        ("vn_architecture_output", format!("n{}", output.index())),
        (
            "vn_supported_roles",
            "input,parameter,state,primitive,module-boundary,output".into(),
        ),
        ("vn_unmodeled", "control,training".into()),
        ("vn_module_instances", scopes.len().to_string()),
    ] {
        writeln!(dot, "  {key}={};", quoted(&value)).expect("writing to string");
    }

    // One immutable rendering context for all recursive module scopes.
    // Single- and multi-output modules use the same normalized hierarchy.
    struct RenderContext<'a> {
        graph: &'a NeuralGraph,
        scopes: &'a [ModuleScope],
        owners: &'a [Option<usize>],
        parents: &'a [Option<usize>],
        paths: &'a [String],
        reachable: &'a BTreeSet<usize>,
        roles: &'a BTreeMap<usize, String>,
        kernel_map: &'a BTreeMap<usize, &'a crate::TranslationKernel>,
        fused: &'a BTreeSet<usize>,
        output: NodeId,
    }

    fn render_scope(
        parent: Option<usize>,
        context: &RenderContext<'_>,
        depth: usize,
        dot: &mut String,
    ) {
        let RenderContext {
            graph,
            scopes,
            owners,
            parents,
            paths,
            reachable,
            roles,
            kernel_map,
            fused,
            output,
        } = context;
        let indent = "  ".repeat(depth + 1);
        for (index, node) in graph
            .nodes()
            .iter()
            .enumerate()
            .filter(|(i, _)| owners[*i] == parent)
        {
            let dims = format!("{:?}", node.shape.dims());
            let kind = if index == output.index() {
                "architecture_output"
            } else if matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input) {
                roles.get(&index).map(String::as_str).unwrap_or("input")
            } else {
                "primitive"
            };
            let kernel = kernel_map.get(&index);
            let lowering = kernel.map_or_else(
                || {
                    if fused.contains(&index) {
                        "fused-into-consumer"
                    } else if graph
                        .storage(node.id)
                        .expect("snapshot node belongs to graph")
                        .is_alias()
                    {
                        "zero-copy-alias"
                    } else {
                        "not-lowered"
                    }
                },
                |_| "kernel",
            );
            let policy = format!("{:?}", node.semantics.fp32);
            let (fill, outline) = node_theme(kind, &node.operation);
            let title = match kind {
                "input" => "INPUT".to_owned(),
                "parameter" => "PARAMETER".to_owned(),
                "state" => "STATE".to_owned(),
                "architecture_output" => format!("OUTPUT · {}", operation_title(&node.operation)),
                _ => operation_title(&node.operation).to_owned(),
            };
            let label = format!("{title}  ·  n{index}\n{dims}");
            let properties = [
                ("label", label),
                ("fillcolor", fill.into()),
                ("color", outline.into()),
                (
                    "tooltip",
                    format!("node {index}: {}", node.operation.name()),
                ),
                ("vn_id", format!("n{index}")),
                ("vn_kind", kind.into()),
                ("vn_op", node.operation.name().into()),
                (
                    "vn_reduction_axis",
                    match node.operation {
                        Operation::ReduceSum { axis } | Operation::ReduceMax { axis } => {
                            axis.to_string()
                        }
                        _ => String::new(),
                    },
                ),
                (
                    "vn_axis",
                    match node.operation {
                        Operation::ReduceSum { axis }
                        | Operation::ReduceMax { axis }
                        | Operation::ReverseAxis { axis }
                        | Operation::Concat { axis }
                        | Operation::SliceAxis { axis, .. }
                        | Operation::ArgMax { axis, .. }
                        | Operation::Take { axis } => axis.to_string(),
                        _ => String::new(),
                    },
                ),
                (
                    "vn_permutation",
                    match &node.operation {
                        Operation::Permute { axes } => format!("{axes:?}"),
                        _ => String::new(),
                    },
                ),
                (
                    "vn_tie_break",
                    match node.operation {
                        Operation::ArgMax { tie_break, .. } => tie_break.name().to_owned(),
                        _ => String::new(),
                    },
                ),
                (
                    "vn_custom_semantics",
                    match &node.operation {
                        Operation::Pointwise(spec) => format!(
                            "{}@{}:{}",
                            spec.id(),
                            spec.version(),
                            spec.expression().canonical()
                        ),
                        _ => String::new(),
                    },
                ),
                (
                    "vn_instance_path",
                    parent.map_or_else(|| "root".to_owned(), |p| paths[p].clone()),
                ),
                (
                    "vn_inputs",
                    format!(
                        "{:?}",
                        node.inputs.iter().map(|n| n.index()).collect::<Vec<_>>()
                    ),
                ),
                ("vn_shape", dims),
                ("vn_dtype", node.dtype.name().into()),
                ("vn_layout", "row-major".into()),
                (
                    "vn_storage",
                    graph
                        .storage(node.id)
                        .expect("snapshot node belongs to graph")
                        .describe(),
                ),
                ("vn_domain", format!("{:?}", node.domain)),
                ("vn_semantics", format!("{:?}", node.semantics)),
                ("vn_requires", format!("{:?}", node.contract.requires)),
                ("vn_ensures", format!("{:?}", node.contract.ensures)),
                ("vn_claims", format!("{:?}", node.contract.claims)),
                ("vn_fp32_policy", policy),
                (
                    "vn_reachable_from_output",
                    reachable.contains(&index).to_string(),
                ),
                ("vn_gpu_lowering", lowering.into()),
                (
                    "vn_gpu_kernel",
                    kernel.map_or_else(|| "none".into(), |k| format!("vn_node_{}", k.entry_node)),
                ),
                (
                    "vn_gpu_memory",
                    kernel.map_or_else(
                        || "none".into(),
                        |k| format!("reads={:?},writes={}", k.reads, k.writes),
                    ),
                ),
                (
                    "vn_assurance",
                    "ideal-Int-Lean-conditional;FP32-test-only;JIT-trusted".into(),
                ),
            ];
            writeln!(dot, "{indent}n{index} [{}];", attrs(&properties)).expect("writing to string");
        }
        for (i, scope) in scopes
            .iter()
            .enumerate()
            .filter(|(i, _)| parents[*i] == parent)
        {
            writeln!(dot, "{indent}subgraph cluster_{} {{", scope.id).expect("writing to string");
            let inner = format!("{indent}  ");
            let (background, outline) = cluster_theme(depth);
            for (key, value) in [
                ("style", "rounded,filled".to_owned()),
                ("fillcolor", background.to_owned()),
                ("color", outline.to_owned()),
                ("fontname", "DejaVu Sans".to_owned()),
                ("fontcolor", "#344664".to_owned()),
                ("fontsize", "15".to_owned()),
                ("penwidth", "1.7".to_owned()),
                ("margin", "22".to_owned()),
                ("labelloc", "t".to_owned()),
                ("labeljust", "l".to_owned()),
            ] {
                writeln!(dot, "{inner}{key}={};", quoted(&value)).expect("writing to string");
            }
            let visible_inputs = scope
                .inputs
                .iter()
                .map(|(name, source)| format!("{name}:n{source}"))
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                .join("  ");
            let visible_outputs = scope
                .outputs
                .iter()
                .map(|(name, output)| format!("{name}:n{output}"))
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                .join("  ");
            writeln!(
                dot,
                "{inner}label={};",
                quoted(&format!(
                    "{}  ·  {}\n{visible_inputs}  →  {visible_outputs}",
                    scope.name.replace('_', " ").to_uppercase(),
                    scope.id,
                ))
            )
            .expect("writing to string");
            for (key, value) in [
                ("vn_instance_path", paths[i].clone()),
                ("vn_definition_id", scope.name.into()),
                ("vn_input_ports", format!("{:?}", scope.inputs)),
                ("vn_output_ports", format!("{:?}", scope.outputs)),
                ("vn_requires", scope.requires.clone()),
                ("vn_ensures", scope.ensures.clone()),
                ("vn_claims", scope.claims.clone()),
                ("vn_semantic_version", scope.version.into()),
                (
                    "vn_proof_status",
                    "conditional-ideal-Int;Lean-check-required".into(),
                ),
            ] {
                writeln!(dot, "{inner}{key}={};", quoted(&value)).expect("writing to string");
            }
            render_scope(Some(i), context, depth + 1, dot);
            writeln!(dot, "{indent}}}").expect("writing to string");
        }
    }
    let context = RenderContext {
        graph,
        scopes,
        owners,
        parents,
        paths,
        reachable: &reachable,
        roles: &metadata.input_roles,
        kernel_map: &kernel_map,
        fused: &fused,
        output,
    };
    render_scope(None, &context, 0, &mut dot);
    // Let dot choose input ranks: hard rank=same constraints create crossing
    // bundles when shared inputs and parameters feed distant submodules.
    // Validate the nested capture chain without adding visual relay edges.
    for (i, scope) in scopes.iter().enumerate() {
        for (port, (_, source_id)) in scope.inputs.iter().enumerate() {
            if !source_is_outside_scope(*source_id, scope) {
                return Err(bad(format!(
                    "module {} input {port} is not external to its body",
                    scope.id
                )));
            }
            if let Some(parent) = parents[i] {
                let parent_scope = &scopes[parent];
                if source_is_outside_scope(*source_id, parent_scope)
                    && !parent_scope
                        .inputs
                        .iter()
                        .any(|(_, parent_source)| parent_source == source_id)
                {
                    return Err(bad(format!(
                        "module {} captures n{} without a declared parent {} port",
                        scope.id, source_id, parent_scope.id
                    )));
                }
            }
        }
    }
    // One visible edge per real typed IR dependency, with complete vn_* data.
    for (i, node) in graph.nodes().iter().enumerate() {
        for (port, source) in node.inputs.iter().enumerate() {
            let from = graph.node(*source).map_err(|e| bad(e.to_string()))?;
            let transform = match node.operation {
                Operation::BiasAdd if port == 1 => "row-wise-broadcast",
                Operation::Reshape(_) => "zero-copy-reshape",
                Operation::Permute { .. } => "axis-permutation",
                Operation::BroadcastTo(_) => "explicit-broadcast",
                Operation::ReduceMax { .. } => "axis-reduction-max",
                Operation::ReverseAxis { .. } => "axis-reversal",
                Operation::Concat { .. } => "axis-concatenation",
                Operation::SliceAxis { .. } => "axis-slice",
                Operation::ArgMax { .. } => "argmax-indexing",
                Operation::Take { .. } if port == 1 => "index-selection",
                Operation::Take { .. } => "axis-selection",
                Operation::MatMul => "matrix-product-indexing",
                _ => "identity",
            };
            let role = metadata
                .input_roles
                .get(&source.index())
                .map(String::as_str)
                .filter(|r| *r == "parameter")
                .unwrap_or("data");
            let (edge_color, edge_width) = edge_theme(role, port);
            if let Some(owner) = owners[i] {
                let scope = &scopes[owner];
                if source_is_outside_scope(source.index(), scope)
                    && !scope
                        .inputs
                        .iter()
                        .any(|(_, declared)| *declared == source.index())
                {
                    return Err(bad(format!(
                        "node n{i} captures n{} outside module {} without a declared input",
                        source.index(),
                        scope.id
                    )));
                }
            }
            // Emphasize local chains, but still rank all cross-module data
            // and parameter dependencies in the correct direction.
            let weight = if role == "parameter" {
                "1"
            } else if owners[i] == owners[source.index()] {
                "5"
            } else {
                "2"
            };
            let src_module_port = owners[source.index()]
                .and_then(|owner| {
                    scopes[owner]
                        .outputs
                        .iter()
                        .find(|(_, index)| *index == source.index())
                })
                .map_or("none", |(name, _)| name.as_str());
            let dst_module_port = owners[i]
                .and_then(|owner| {
                    let scope = &scopes[owner];
                    source_is_outside_scope(source.index(), scope)
                        .then(|| {
                            scope
                                .inputs
                                .iter()
                                .find(|(_, index)| *index == source.index())
                        })
                        .flatten()
                })
                .map_or("none", |(name, _)| name.as_str());
            let data = [
                ("color", edge_color.into()),
                ("penwidth", edge_width.into()),
                ("weight", weight.into()),
                ("minlen", "1".into()),
                (
                    "constraint",
                    if role == "parameter" { "false" } else { "true" }.into(),
                ),
                ("vn_src_port", "output".into()),
                ("vn_dst_port", format!("input_{port}")),
                ("vn_module_src_port", src_module_port.into()),
                ("vn_module_dst_port", dst_module_port.into()),
                ("vn_semantic_src", format!("n{}", source.index())),
                ("vn_semantic_dst", format!("n{i}")),
                ("vn_visual_src", format!("n{}", source.index())),
                ("vn_role", role.into()),
                ("vn_shape", format!("{:?}", from.shape.dims())),
                ("vn_dtype", from.dtype.name().into()),
                ("vn_transform", transform.into()),
                ("vn_order", port.to_string()),
                ("vn_constraint", "source-shape-checked".into()),
            ];
            writeln!(dot, "  n{} -> n{i} [{}];", source.index(), attrs(&data))
                .expect("writing to string");
        }
    }
    dot.push_str("}\n");
    Ok(ArchitectureSnapshot {
        semantic_ir: ir,
        dot,
        ir_sha256: digest,
    })
}

/// One architecture-neutral DOT containing *all* Semantic IR nodes, including
/// unselected nodes, and typed port mappings of both module kinds.
///
/// The digest belongs to the caller's canonical auto-build semantic.ir, not
/// to the picture. The DOT is informational; it is not an independent proof.
pub(crate) fn auto_architecture_dot(
    graph: &NeuralGraph,
    plan: &crate::AutoBuildPlan,
    semantic_ir_sha256: &str,
) -> io::Result<String> {
    if semantic_ir_sha256.len() != 64 || !semantic_ir_sha256.bytes().all(|b| b.is_ascii_hexdigit())
    {
        return Err(bad("invalid canonical Semantic IR SHA-256 for DOT"));
    }

    let layout = module_layout(graph)?;
    let scopes = &layout.scopes;
    let parents = &layout.parents;
    let paths = &layout.paths;
    let owners = &layout.owners;
    let n = graph.nodes().len();
    let selected = plan
        .outputs
        .iter()
        .map(|id| id.index())
        .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();
    // All nodes are drawn, but Lean only models reachable dependencies.
    let reachable = graph
        .dependency_scope(&plan.outputs)
        .map_err(|err| bad(err.to_string()))?;
    let gpu_status = plan
        .gpu
        .iter()
        .map(|entry| match entry {
            crate::PlannedGpu::Supported { output, .. } => (output.index(), "nvptx-supported"),
            crate::PlannedGpu::Unsupported { output, .. } => (output.index(), "unsupported"),
        })
        .collect::<BTreeMap<_, _>>();
    let mut dot = String::from(
        r##"digraph verineural_auto {
  graph [rankdir=LR, compound=true, newrank=true, splines=spline,
         concentrate=false, outputorder=edgesfirst, mclimit=4,
         nodesep=0.75, ranksep=1.15, pad=0.60, margin=0.18, dpi=180,
         bgcolor="#FFFFFF", fontname="DejaVu Sans", fontcolor="#24324B",
         labelloc=t, labeljust=l];
  node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="DejaVu Sans",
        fontsize=12, fontcolor="#24324B", penwidth=1.5, margin="0.17,0.13"];
  edge [color="#8796AA", penwidth=1.1, arrowsize=0.72];
"##,
    );
    for (key, value) in [
        (
            "label",
            format!(
                "VeriNeural · auto architecture\n{} nodes · {} module instances · {} outputs",
                n,
                scopes.len(),
                plan.outputs.len()
            ),
        ),
        ("vn_export_version", "auto-v3".into()),
        ("vn_ir_sha256", semantic_ir_sha256.to_owned()),
        ("vn_fp32_profile", format!("{:?}", graph.policy())),
        ("vn_selected_outputs", format!("{:?}", selected)),
        (
            "vn_lean_assurance",
            "ideal-Int;conditional-source-assumptions;kernel-checked-at-build".into(),
        ),
        (
            "vn_gpu_assurance",
            "LLVM/PTX-structural;JIT-SASS-not-proven".into(),
        ),
        ("vn_connectivity", "Rust-structural-validation".into()),
        (
            "vn_unmodeled",
            "general-dtype;implicit-broadcast;machine-equivalence".into(),
        ),
    ] {
        writeln!(dot, "  {key}={};", quoted(&value)).expect("writing DOT");
    }
    struct Context<'a> {
        graph: &'a NeuralGraph,
        scopes: &'a [ModuleScope],
        parents: &'a [Option<usize>],
        owners: &'a [Option<usize>],
        paths: &'a [String],
        selected: &'a BTreeSet<usize>,
        reachable: &'a BTreeSet<usize>,
        gpu_status: &'a BTreeMap<usize, &'static str>,
    }
    fn render_scope(parent: Option<usize>, context: &Context<'_>, depth: usize, dot: &mut String) {
        let pad = "  ".repeat(depth + 1);
        for (i, node) in context
            .graph
            .nodes()
            .iter()
            .enumerate()
            .filter(|(i, _)| context.owners[*i] == parent)
        {
            let kind = if context.selected.contains(&i) {
                "architecture_output"
            } else if matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input) {
                "input"
            } else {
                "primitive"
            };
            let (fill, outline) = node_theme(kind, &node.operation);
            let title = if kind == "architecture_output" {
                format!("OUTPUT · {}", operation_title(&node.operation))
            } else {
                operation_title(&node.operation).to_uppercase()
            };
            let properties = [
                ("label", format!("{title} · n{i}\n{:?}", node.shape.dims())),
                ("fillcolor", fill.to_owned()),
                ("color", outline.to_owned()),
                ("vn_id", format!("n{i}")),
                ("vn_kind", kind.to_owned()),
                ("vn_op", node.operation.name().to_owned()),
                (
                    "vn_reduction_axis",
                    match node.operation {
                        Operation::ReduceSum { axis } | Operation::ReduceMax { axis } => {
                            axis.to_string()
                        }
                        _ => String::new(),
                    },
                ),
                (
                    "vn_axis",
                    match node.operation {
                        Operation::ReduceSum { axis }
                        | Operation::ReduceMax { axis }
                        | Operation::ReverseAxis { axis }
                        | Operation::Concat { axis }
                        | Operation::SliceAxis { axis, .. }
                        | Operation::ArgMax { axis, .. }
                        | Operation::Take { axis } => axis.to_string(),
                        _ => String::new(),
                    },
                ),
                (
                    "vn_permutation",
                    match &node.operation {
                        Operation::Permute { axes } => format!("{axes:?}"),
                        _ => String::new(),
                    },
                ),
                (
                    "vn_tie_break",
                    match node.operation {
                        Operation::ArgMax { tie_break, .. } => tie_break.name().to_owned(),
                        _ => String::new(),
                    },
                ),
                (
                    "vn_custom_semantics",
                    match &node.operation {
                        Operation::Pointwise(spec) => format!(
                            "{}@{}:{}",
                            spec.id(),
                            spec.version(),
                            spec.expression().canonical()
                        ),
                        _ => String::new(),
                    },
                ),
                (
                    "vn_instance_path",
                    parent.map_or_else(|| "root".to_owned(), |p| context.paths[p].clone()),
                ),
                (
                    "vn_inputs",
                    format!(
                        "{:?}",
                        node.inputs.iter().map(|id| id.index()).collect::<Vec<_>>()
                    ),
                ),
                ("vn_shape", format!("{:?}", node.shape.dims())),
                ("vn_dtype", node.dtype.name().into()),
                ("vn_layout", "row-major".into()),
                (
                    "vn_storage",
                    context
                        .graph
                        .storage(node.id)
                        .expect("auto DOT node belongs to graph")
                        .describe(),
                ),
                ("vn_domain", format!("{:?}", node.domain)),
                ("vn_contract", format!("{:?}", node.contract)),
                ("vn_semantics", format!("{:?}", node.semantics)),
                (
                    "vn_selected_output",
                    context.selected.contains(&i).to_string(),
                ),
                (
                    "vn_reachable_from_outputs",
                    context.reachable.contains(&i).to_string(),
                ),
                (
                    "vn_gpu_lowering",
                    context
                        .gpu_status
                        .get(&i)
                        .copied()
                        .unwrap_or("no-selected-output-profile")
                        .to_owned(),
                ),
                (
                    "vn_proof_status",
                    if context.reachable.contains(&i) {
                        "ideal-Int;checked-in-auto-bundle"
                    } else {
                        "unselected;no-Lean-obligation"
                    }
                    .into(),
                ),
            ];
            writeln!(dot, "{pad}n{i} [{}];", attrs(&properties)).expect("writing DOT");
        }
        for (i, scope) in context
            .scopes
            .iter()
            .enumerate()
            .filter(|(i, _)| context.parents[*i] == parent)
        {
            writeln!(dot, "{pad}subgraph cluster_{} {{", scope.id).expect("writing DOT");
            let inner = format!("{pad}  ");
            let (fill, outline) = cluster_theme(depth);
            let in_ports = scope
                .inputs
                .iter()
                .map(|(name, index)| format!("{name}:n{index}"))
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                .join("  ");
            let out_ports = scope
                .outputs
                .iter()
                .map(|(name, index)| format!("{name}:n{index}"))
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                .join("  ");
            for (key, value) in [
                ("style", "rounded,filled".into()),
                ("fillcolor", fill.into()),
                ("color", outline.into()),
                ("fontname", "DejaVu Sans".into()),
                ("fontsize", "14".into()),
                ("labelloc", "t".into()),
                ("labeljust", "l".into()),
                ("margin", "22".into()),
                (
                    "label",
                    format!(
                        "{} · {}\n{} → {}",
                        scope.name.replace('_', " ").to_uppercase(),
                        scope.id,
                        in_ports,
                        out_ports,
                    ),
                ),
                ("vn_instance_path", context.paths[i].clone()),
                ("vn_definition_id", scope.name.to_owned()),
                ("vn_semantic_version", scope.version.to_owned()),
                ("vn_contract", scope.contract.clone()),
                ("vn_input_ports", format!("{:?}", scope.inputs)),
                ("vn_output_ports", format!("{:?}", scope.outputs)),
                (
                    "vn_proof_status",
                    "module-contracts-checkable;see-Lean-artifact".into(),
                ),
            ] {
                writeln!(dot, "{inner}{key}={};", quoted(&value)).expect("writing DOT");
            }
            render_scope(Some(i), context, depth + 1, dot);
            writeln!(dot, "{pad}}}").expect("writing DOT");
        }
    }
    render_scope(
        None,
        &Context {
            graph,
            scopes,
            parents,
            owners,
            paths,
            selected: &selected,
            reachable: &reachable,
            gpu_status: &gpu_status,
        },
        0,
        &mut dot,
    );
    // Inputs are not forced onto a single rank; semantic input identity is
    // recorded in vn_kind, independently of the visual layout.
    // Exactly one rendered edge for every real Semantic IR dependency.
    // Module port mappings are attributes, never extra visual relay edges.
    for (i, node) in graph.nodes().iter().enumerate() {
        for (port, input) in node.inputs.iter().enumerate() {
            let source = graph.node(*input).map_err(|err| bad(err.to_string()))?;
            let (color, width) = edge_theme("data", port);
            let transform = match node.operation {
                Operation::BiasAdd if port == 1 => "row-wise-broadcast",
                Operation::Reshape(_) => "zero-copy-reshape",
                Operation::Permute { .. } => "axis-permutation",
                Operation::BroadcastTo(_) => "explicit-broadcast",
                Operation::ReduceMax { .. } => "axis-reduction-max",
                Operation::ReverseAxis { .. } => "axis-reversal",
                Operation::Concat { .. } => "axis-concatenation",
                Operation::SliceAxis { .. } => "axis-slice",
                Operation::ArgMax { .. } => "argmax-indexing",
                Operation::Take { .. } if port == 1 => "index-selection",
                Operation::Take { .. } => "axis-selection",
                Operation::MatMul => "matrix-product-indexing",
                _ => "identity",
            };
            let module_dst_port = owners[i]
                .and_then(|owner| {
                    let scope = &scopes[owner];
                    source_is_outside_scope(input.index(), scope)
                        .then(|| scope.inputs.iter().find(|(_, id)| *id == input.index()))
                })
                .flatten()
                .map_or("none", |(name, _)| name.as_str());
            let module_src_port = owners[input.index()]
                .and_then(|owner| {
                    scopes[owner]
                        .outputs
                        .iter()
                        .find(|(_, index)| *index == input.index())
                })
                .map_or("none", |(name, _)| name.as_str());
            let properties = [
                ("color", color.into()),
                ("penwidth", width.into()),
                (
                    "weight",
                    if owners[i] == owners[input.index()] {
                        "5".into()
                    } else {
                        "2".into()
                    },
                ),
                ("minlen", "1".into()),
                ("constraint", "true".into()),
                ("vn_src_port", "output".into()),
                ("vn_dst_port", format!("input_{port}")),
                ("vn_module_src_port", module_src_port.into()),
                ("vn_module_dst_port", module_dst_port.into()),
                ("vn_semantic_src", format!("n{}", input.index())),
                ("vn_semantic_dst", format!("n{i}")),
                ("vn_visual_src", format!("n{}", input.index())),
                ("vn_order", port.to_string()),
                ("vn_shape", format!("{:?}", source.shape.dims())),
                ("vn_dtype", source.dtype.name().into()),
                ("vn_role", "data".into()),
                ("vn_transform", transform.into()),
                ("vn_constraint", "source-shape-checked".into()),
            ];
            writeln!(
                dot,
                "  n{} -> n{i} [{}];",
                input.index(),
                attrs(&properties)
            )
            .expect("writing DOT");
        }
    }
    dot.push_str("}\n");
    Ok(dot)
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use crate::{Domain, GpuEngine, Shape};

    #[test]
    fn automatic_dot_represents_nested_multi_ports_and_all_real_edges() {
        use crate::{
            ArchitectureAutoCompiler, GpuRequirement, MathContract, MultiOutputContract,
            MultiOutputModule, NamedPortContract, NeuralError, NeuralModule, PortContract,
        };
        struct Activation {
            contract: MathContract,
        }
        impl NeuralModule for Activation {
            fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
                "consumer_activation"
            }
            fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract {
                &self.contract
            }
            fn build(
                &self,
                graph: &mut NeuralGraph,
                inputs: &[NodeId],
            ) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
                graph.relu(inputs[0])
            }
        }
        struct Step {
            contract: MultiOutputContract,
            child: Activation,
        }
        impl MultiOutputModule for Step {
            fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
                "consumer_step"
            }
            fn contract(&self) -> &MultiOutputContract {
                &self.contract
            }
            fn build(
                &self,
                graph: &mut NeuralGraph,
                inputs: &[NodeId],
            ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError> {
                let next = graph.apply_module(&self.child, &[inputs[0]])?;
                let readout = graph.add(next, inputs[1])?;
                Ok(vec![next, readout])
            }
        }
        fn prepare() -> (NeuralGraph, crate::AutoBuildPlan) {
            let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
            let shape = Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap();
            let positive = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
            let any = PortContract::new(shape.clone(), Domain::Any);
            let a = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
            let b = graph.input(shape, Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
            let _detached = graph.relu(b).unwrap();
            let module = Step {
                contract: MultiOutputContract {
                    inputs: vec![
                        NamedPortContract::new("state", positive.clone()),
                        NamedPortContract::new("input", positive.clone()),
                    ],
                    outputs: vec![
                        NamedPortContract::new("next_state", positive.clone()),
                        NamedPortContract::new("readout", any),
                    ],
                },
                child: Activation {
                    contract: MathContract::new(vec![positive.clone()], positive),
                },
            };
            let outputs = graph.apply_multi_module(&module, &[a, b]).unwrap();
            let plan = ArchitectureAutoCompiler::default()
                .plan(&graph, &outputs, &[], GpuRequirement::AllOutputs)
                .unwrap();
            (graph, plan)
        }

        let (g1, p1) = prepare();
        let (g2, p2) = prepare();
        let hash = "a".repeat(64);
        let dot = auto_architecture_dot(&g1, &p1, &hash).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(dot, auto_architecture_dot(&g2, &p2, &hash).unwrap());
        assert!(dot.contains(&format!(r#"vn_ir_sha256="{hash}""#)));
        assert!(dot.contains("subgraph cluster_m0"));
        assert!(dot.contains("subgraph cluster_m1"));
        assert!(dot.contains("next_state"));
        assert!(dot.contains("readout"));
        assert!(dot.contains("vn_src_port=\"output\""));
        assert!(dot.contains("vn_module_src_port="));
        assert!(dot.contains("vn_module_dst_port="));
        assert!(!dot.contains("rank=same;"));
        assert!(dot.contains("vn_input_ports"));
        assert!(dot.contains("vn_output_ports"));
        assert!(dot.contains(r#"vn_reachable_from_outputs="false""#));
        assert!(dot.contains(r#"vn_gpu_lowering="nvptx-supported""#));
        assert_eq!(dot.matches("vn_id=").count(), g1.nodes().len());
        let edges: usize = g1.nodes().iter().map(|n| n.inputs.len()).sum();
        assert_eq!(dot.matches(" -> n").count(), edges);
        assert!(!dot.contains("module-input-port"));
        assert!(!dot.contains("headport="));
        assert!(!dot.contains("tailport="));
        assert!(auto_architecture_dot(&g1, &p1, "bad").is_err());
    }

    #[test]
    fn graph_id_independent_complete_export_and_detects_tampering() {
        fn build() -> (NeuralGraph, NodeId, GpuProgram) {
            let mut g = NeuralGraph::default();
            let a = g.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
            let b = g.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
            let _unreachable = g.add(a, b).unwrap();
            let product = g.mul(a, b).unwrap();
            let program = GpuEngine::default().compile(&g, product).unwrap();
            (g, product, program)
        }
        let meta = ArchitectureMetadata {
            id: "coupled-cell".into(),
            version: "0.1.0".into(),
            input_roles: BTreeMap::from([(0, "input".into()), (1, "parameter".into())]),
            global_property: "architecture_global_nonnegative".into(),
        };
        let (g1, o1, p1) = build();
        let (g2, o2, p2) = build();
        let a = snapshot_architecture(&g1, o1, &p1, &meta).unwrap();
        let b = snapshot_architecture(&g2, o2, &p2, &meta).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(a.semantic_ir, b.semantic_ir);
        assert_eq!(a.dot, b.dot);
        assert!(a.dot.contains("vn_reachable_from_output=\"false\""));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("vn_ir_sha256="));
        assert_eq!(a.dot.matches("vn_id=").count(), g1.nodes().len());
        // Visual edges must correspond one-to-one with real typed IR inputs,
        // not synthetic module-port annotations that obscure the graph.
        let real_edges: usize = g1.nodes().iter().map(|n| n.inputs.len()).sum();
        assert_eq!(a.dot.matches(" -> ").count(), real_edges);
        assert_eq!(a.dot.matches("vn_semantic_dst=").count(), real_edges);
        assert!(!a.dot.contains("module-input-port"));
        assert!(!a.dot.contains(r#"style="dashed""#));
        assert!(!a.dot.contains("vn_input_port_")); // no modules in this graph
        assert!(!a.dot.contains("rank=same;"));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("splines=spline"));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("concentrate=false"));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("mclimit=4"));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("nodesep=0.75"));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("ranksep=1.15"));
        assert!(!a.dot.contains("tailport="));
        assert!(!a.dot.contains("headport="));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("constraint=\"false\""));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("constraint=\"true\""));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("minlen=\"1\""));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("vn_visual_src=\"n0\""));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("dpi=180"));
        assert!(a.dot.contains("fillcolor=\"#FFF1DB\""));
        // Labels must be multi-line, not a literal printed backslash-n.
        assert!(a.dot.contains(r#"n0 [label="INPUT  ·  n0\n[2]""#));
        assert!(!a.dot.contains(r#"INPUT  ·  n0\\n[2]"#));
        let mut changed = meta.clone();
        changed.version = "0.2.0".into();
        let changed_snapshot = snapshot_architecture(&g1, o1, &p1, &changed).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(a.ir_sha256, changed_snapshot.ir_sha256);
        assert_ne!(a.dot, changed_snapshot.dot);
        changed.input_roles.insert(20, "parameter".into());
        assert!(snapshot_architecture(&g1, o1, &p1, &changed).is_err());
    }
    #[test]
    fn snapshot_reports_shared_entrypoint_for_distinct_logical_nodes() {
        let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
        let x = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![4]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        let y = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![4]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        let first = graph.add(x, y).unwrap();
        let second = graph.add(first, y).unwrap();
        let program = GpuEngine::default().compile(&graph, second).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(program.kernel_entry(second.index()), Some(first.index()));
        let metadata = ArchitectureMetadata {
            id: "interned-producers".into(),
            version: "0.1.0".into(),
            input_roles: BTreeMap::from([
                (x.index(), "input".into()),
                (y.index(), "parameter".into()),
            ]),
            global_property: "architecture_global_nonnegative".into(),
        };
        let snapshot = snapshot_architecture(&graph, second, &program, &metadata).unwrap();
        let entry = format!("vn_gpu_kernel=\"vn_node_{}\"", first.index());
        let orphan = format!("vn_gpu_kernel=\"vn_node_{}\"", second.index());
        assert_eq!(snapshot.dot.matches(&entry).count(), 2);
        assert!(!snapshot.dot.contains(&orphan));
    }

    #[test]
    fn snapshot_png_replay_detects_image_tampering() {
        if Command::new("dot").arg("-V").output().is_err() {
            // Graphviz is supplied by the project's pinned Nix shell.
            return;
        }
        let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
        let input = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        let output = graph.relu(input).unwrap();
        let program = GpuEngine::default().compile(&graph, output).unwrap();
        let metadata = ArchitectureMetadata {
            id: "png-replay".into(),
            version: "0.1.0".into(),
            input_roles: BTreeMap::from([(input.index(), "input".into())]),
            global_property: "architecture_global_nonnegative".into(),
        };
        let snapshot = snapshot_architecture(&graph, output, &program, &metadata).unwrap();
        let root = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "verineural-png-replay-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        fs::create_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
        snapshot.write(&root).unwrap();
        snapshot.verify(&root).unwrap();
        fs::write(root.join("architecture.png"), b"not the Graphviz image").unwrap();
        assert!(snapshot.verify(&root).is_err());
        fs::remove_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
    }
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/auto_build.rs
//! One consumer-facing build path for arbitrary *supported* neural graphs.
//!
//! The graph and contracts remain the single source of truth. Binding checks
//! are structural Rust checks; the Lean kernel verifies mathematical claims
//! about the generated ideal-Int model; LLVM/PTX translation validation does
//! not prove actual binary32 or NVIDIA machine-code equivalence.

use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};
use std::error::Error;
use std::fmt;
use std::fs;
use std::io;
use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU64, Ordering};

use crate::{
    FixedScan, GpuEngine, GpuError, GpuProgram, LeanProgram, LeanProofEngine, NeuralError,
    NeuralGraph, NodeId, Operation, ProofError, ProofGoal, auto_bundle,
};

#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum GpuRequirement {
    /// Produce Lean proofs and explicitly mark unsupported GPU outputs.
    AllowUnsupported,
    /// Fail unless *every* requested output has supported NVPTX lowering.
    AllOutputs,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub enum ArchitectureProofTask {
    Goal(ProofGoal),
    /// Prove every state of one explicitly unrolled finite scan.
    FixedScanNonnegative {
        name: String,
        scan: FixedScan,
    },
}

impl ArchitectureProofTask {
    fn name(&self) -> &str {
        match self {
            Self::Goal(goal) => &goal.name,
            Self::FixedScanNonnegative { name, .. } => name,
        }
    }
}

#[derive(Debug)]
pub enum AutoBuildError {
    Graph(NeuralError),
    Proof(ProofError),
    Gpu(GpuError),
    Io(io::Error),
    InvalidConnection(String),
    DuplicateTask(String),
    Integrity(String),
}

impl fmt::Display for AutoBuildError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        match self {
            Self::Graph(e) => write!(f, "graph validation failed: {e}"),
            Self::Proof(e) => write!(f, "Lean obligation failed: {e}"),
            Self::Gpu(e) => write!(f, "GPU lowering failed: {e}"),
            Self::Io(e) => write!(f, "artifact I/O failed: {e}"),
            Self::InvalidConnection(e) => write!(f, "invalid architecture connectivity: {e}"),
            Self::DuplicateTask(e) => write!(f, "duplicate proof task name: {e}"),
            Self::Integrity(e) => write!(f, "auto-build artifact integrity failure: {e}"),
        }
    }
}

impl Error for AutoBuildError {
    fn source(&self) -> Option<&(dyn Error + 'static)> {
        match self {
            Self::Graph(e) => Some(e),
            Self::Proof(e) => Some(e),
            Self::Gpu(e) => Some(e),
            Self::Io(e) => Some(e),
            _ => None,
        }
    }
}
impl From<NeuralError> for AutoBuildError {
    fn from(value: NeuralError) -> Self {
        Self::Graph(value)
    }
}
impl From<ProofError> for AutoBuildError {
    fn from(value: ProofError) -> Self {
        Self::Proof(value)
    }
}
impl From<GpuError> for AutoBuildError {
    fn from(value: GpuError) -> Self {
        Self::Gpu(value)
    }
}
impl From<io::Error> for AutoBuildError {
    fn from(value: io::Error) -> Self {
        Self::Io(value)
    }
}

/// Rechecked graph bindings, not a formal theorem about GPU wiring.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct ConnectivityEvidence {
    pub data_edges: usize,
    pub module_ports: usize,
    pub module_instances: usize,
}

fn invalid(reason: impl Into<String>) -> AutoBuildError {
    AutoBuildError::InvalidConnection(reason.into())
}

fn check_port(
    graph: &NeuralGraph,
    id: NodeId,
    port: &crate::PortContract,
    where_: &str,
) -> Result<(), AutoBuildError> {
    let node = graph.node(id)?;
    if node.shape != port.shape || node.dtype != port.dtype || !node.domain.satisfies(port.domain) {
        return Err(invalid(format!(
            "{where_}: shape/dtype/domain mismatch at node {}",
            id.index()
        )));
    }
    Ok(())
}

/// Independently repeat the structural checks for *all* nodes and instances.
/// Constructor-time validation rejects bad captures; this pass also gives the
/// build an explicit, inspectable edge/port count.
pub fn check_architecture_connectivity(
    graph: &NeuralGraph,
) -> Result<ConnectivityEvidence, AutoBuildError> {
    let mut data_edges = 0;
    let mut module_ports = 0;
    for (index, node) in graph.nodes().iter().enumerate() {
        if node.id.index() != index {
            return Err(invalid(format!("node {index} has inconsistent identity")));
        }
        graph.node(node.id)?;
        if matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input) {
            if !node.inputs.is_empty() {
                return Err(invalid(format!("source node {index} has dependencies")));
            }
        } else {
            let mut shapes = Vec::new();
            for &input in &node.inputs {
                if input.index() >= index {
                    return Err(invalid(format!("node {index} has a non-DAG edge")));
                }
                shapes.push(graph.node(input)?.shape.clone());
                data_edges += 1;
            }
            if node.operation.infer_shape(&shapes)? != node.shape {
                return Err(invalid(format!("node {index} has inconsistent shape")));
            }
        }
        if node.contract.requires.len() != node.inputs.len() {
            return Err(invalid(format!("node {index} contract arity differs")));
        }
        for (&input, port) in node.inputs.iter().zip(&node.contract.requires) {
            check_port(graph, input, port, &format!("node {index} input"))?;
        }
        check_port(
            graph,
            node.id,
            &node.contract.ensures,
            &format!("node {index} result"),
        )?;
    }

    let mut module_instances = 0;
    for (index, module) in graph.module_instances().enumerate() {
        module_instances += 1;
        let body = module.body_range();
        let outputs = module.outputs();
        if body.start >= body.end
            || body.end > graph.nodes().len()
            || outputs.is_empty()
            || outputs
                .iter()
                .any(|output| output.index() < body.start || output.index() >= body.end)
        {
            return Err(invalid(format!(
                "module instance {index} has malformed body or outputs"
            )));
        }
        if module
            .inputs()
            .iter()
            .any(|input| input.index() >= body.start)
        {
            return Err(invalid(format!(
                "module instance {index} captures a forward input"
            )));
        }
        check_body_edges(
            graph,
            body.start,
            body.end,
            module.inputs(),
            &format!("module instance {index}"),
        )?;
    }

    for (index, module) in graph.modules().iter().enumerate() {
        if module.inputs.len() != module.contract.requires.len() {
            return Err(invalid(format!("module {index} has malformed ports")));
        }
        for (&input, port) in module.inputs.iter().zip(&module.contract.requires) {
            check_port(graph, input, port, &format!("module {index} input"))?;
            module_ports += 1;
        }
        check_port(
            graph,
            module.output,
            &module.contract.ensures,
            &format!("module {index} output"),
        )?;
        module_ports += 1;
    }

    for (index, module) in graph.multi_modules().iter().enumerate() {
        if module.inputs.len() != module.contract.inputs.len()
            || module.outputs.len() != module.contract.outputs.len()
            || module.outputs.is_empty()
        {
            return Err(invalid(format!("multi-module {index} has malformed ports")));
        }
        for (&input, port) in module.inputs.iter().zip(&module.contract.inputs) {
            check_port(
                graph,
                input,
                &port.port,
                &format!("multi-module {index} input"),
            )?;
            module_ports += 1;
        }
        let mut seen = BTreeSet::new();
        for (&output, port) in module.outputs.iter().zip(&module.contract.outputs) {
            if !seen.insert(output.index()) {
                return Err(invalid(format!(
                    "multi-module {index} has duplicate output identity"
                )));
            }
            check_port(
                graph,
                output,
                &port.port,
                &format!("multi-module {index} output"),
            )?;
            module_ports += 1;
        }
    }
    Ok(ConnectivityEvidence {
        data_edges,
        module_ports,
        module_instances,
    })
}

fn check_body_edges(
    graph: &NeuralGraph,
    start: usize,
    end: usize,
    declared: &[NodeId],
    instance: &str,
) -> Result<(), AutoBuildError> {
    for node in &graph.nodes()[start..end] {
        if matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input) {
            return Err(invalid(format!(
                "{instance}: hidden input {}",
                node.id.index()
            )));
        }
        for &input in &node.inputs {
            if input.index() < start && !declared.contains(&input) {
                return Err(invalid(format!(
                    "{instance}: undeclared capture {} -> {}",
                    input.index(),
                    node.id.index()
                )));
            }
        }
    }
    Ok(())
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub enum PlannedGpu {
    Supported {
        output: NodeId,
        program: Box<GpuProgram>,
    },
    Unsupported {
        output: NodeId,
        reason: String,
    },
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct AutoBuildPlan {
    pub connectivity: ConnectivityEvidence,
    pub outputs: Vec<NodeId>,
    pub architecture: LeanProgram,
    pub goals: Vec<(String, LeanProgram)>,
    pub gpu: Vec<PlannedGpu>,
    /// An additional union-of-outputs GPU program. Single-output legacy
    /// artifacts remain available for compatible consumer workflows.
    pub shared_gpu: Option<Box<GpuProgram>>,
    /// Deterministic model declaration included in the certified manifest.
    pub(crate) identity: Option<String>,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct OutputBuildEvidence {
    pub node: usize,
    pub ptx: Option<PathBuf>,
    pub reason: Option<String>,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct AutoBuildReport {
    pub directory: PathBuf,
    pub connectivity: ConnectivityEvidence,
    pub output_evidence: Vec<OutputBuildEvidence>,
    /// Shared single-module NVPTX evidence for multiple supported outputs.
    pub shared_gpu_ptx: Option<PathBuf>,
    pub architecture_theorems: usize,
    pub goal_theorems: Vec<(String, usize)>,
    pub source_hypotheses: Vec<crate::ProofAssumption>,
    pub goal_hypotheses: Vec<(String, Vec<crate::ProofAssumption>)>,
    /// Axiom audit per theorem, namespaced by the generated Lean file.
    pub axiom_dependencies: BTreeMap<String, Vec<String>>,
    pub lean_version: String,
    /// Hash of SHA256SUMS. Authenticity requires external pinning.
    pub manifest_sha256: String,
}

// Keep the last valid bundle while every new proof, GPU lowering and artifact
// check is performed. Staging and the previous bundle are on the same
// filesystem, so directory renames do not become cross-device copies.
static NEXT_BUILD_ID: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);

struct StagedBuild {
    directory: PathBuf,
    published: bool,
}

// Linux renameat2(RENAME_EXCHANGE) switches two existing directories in one
// filesystem operation: no interval when readers see no auto-build directory.
// The swap is fail-closed where the atomic primitive is unavailable.
#[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
fn atomic_exchange_dirs(old: &Path, new: &Path) -> io::Result<()> {
    use std::ffi::CString;
    use std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_uint};
    use std::os::unix::ffi::OsStrExt;

    unsafe extern "C" {
        fn renameat2(
            olddirfd: c_int,
            oldpath: *const c_char,
            newdirfd: c_int,
            newpath: *const c_char,
            flags: c_uint,
        ) -> c_int;
    }
    const AT_FDCWD: c_int = -100;
    const RENAME_EXCHANGE: c_uint = 2;
    let old = CString::new(old.as_os_str().as_bytes())
        .map_err(|_| io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::InvalidInput, "NUL in old path"))?;
    let new = CString::new(new.as_os_str().as_bytes())
        .map_err(|_| io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::InvalidInput, "NUL in new path"))?;
    let code = unsafe {
        renameat2(
            AT_FDCWD,
            old.as_ptr(),
            AT_FDCWD,
            new.as_ptr(),
            RENAME_EXCHANGE,
        )
    };
    if code == 0 {
        Ok(())
    } else {
        Err(io::Error::last_os_error())
    }
}

#[cfg(not(target_os = "linux"))]
fn atomic_exchange_dirs(_old: &Path, _new: &Path) -> io::Result<()> {
    Err(io::Error::new(
        io::ErrorKind::Unsupported,
        "atomic bundle replacement requires Linux renameat2(RENAME_EXCHANGE)",
    ))
}

impl StagedBuild {
    fn create(root: &Path) -> Result<Self, AutoBuildError> {
        fs::create_dir_all(root)?;
        loop {
            let id = NEXT_BUILD_ID.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);
            let suffix = format!("{}-{id}", std::process::id());
            let directory = root.join(format!(".auto-build.staging-{suffix}"));
            match fs::create_dir(&directory) {
                Ok(()) => {
                    return Ok(Self {
                        directory,
                        published: false,
                    });
                }
                Err(error) if error.kind() == io::ErrorKind::AlreadyExists => continue,
                Err(error) => return Err(error.into()),
            }
        }
    }

    fn publish(&mut self, final_dir: &Path) -> Result<(), AutoBuildError> {
        match fs::symlink_metadata(final_dir) {
            Ok(metadata) => {
                if !metadata.is_dir() || metadata.file_type().is_symlink() {
                    return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
                        "existing auto-build is not a real directory: {}",
                        final_dir.display()
                    )));
                }
                atomic_exchange_dirs(final_dir, &self.directory)?;
                // The exchange is the commit point: a cleanup failure must not
                // turn an already-published certificate into a reported failure.
                self.published = true;
                if let Err(error) = fs::remove_dir_all(&self.directory) {
                    eprintln!(
                        "verineural: previously published bundle remains at {}: {error}",
                        self.directory.display()
                    );
                }
                Ok(())
            }
            Err(error) if error.kind() == io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {
                // First publication has only one directory rename.
                fs::rename(&self.directory, final_dir)?;
                self.published = true;
                Ok(())
            }
            Err(error) => Err(error.into()),
        }
    }
}

impl Drop for StagedBuild {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        if !self.published {
            let _ = fs::remove_dir_all(&self.directory);
        }
    }
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)]
pub struct ArchitectureAutoCompiler {
    proof: LeanProofEngine,
    gpu: GpuEngine,
}

impl ArchitectureAutoCompiler {
    pub fn new(proof: LeanProofEngine, gpu: GpuEngine) -> Self {
        Self { proof, gpu }
    }

    /// Pure planning stage; checks wiring, all selected output claims and
    /// independent user goals before running either external tool.
    pub fn plan(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        outputs: &[NodeId],
        tasks: &[ArchitectureProofTask],
        gpu_requirement: GpuRequirement,
    ) -> Result<AutoBuildPlan, AutoBuildError> {
        let connectivity = check_architecture_connectivity(graph)?;
        let architecture = self.proof.generate_outputs(graph, outputs)?;
        let scope = graph.dependency_scope(outputs)?;
        let mut names = BTreeSet::new();
        let mut goals = Vec::new();
        for task in tasks {
            let name = task.name();
            if !names.insert(name.to_owned()) {
                return Err(AutoBuildError::DuplicateTask(name.to_owned()));
            }
            let goals_in_scope = match task {
                ArchitectureProofTask::Goal(goal) => {
                    scope.contains(&goal.output.index()) && graph.node(goal.output).is_ok()
                }
                ArchitectureProofTask::FixedScanNonnegative { scan, .. } => scan
                    .states
                    .iter()
                    .chain(&scan.outputs)
                    .all(|id| scope.contains(&id.index()) && graph.node(*id).is_ok()),
            };
            if !goals_in_scope {
                return Err(invalid(format!(
                    "proof task {name} is not connected to any selected architecture output"
                )));
            }
            let program = match task {
                ArchitectureProofTask::Goal(goal) => self.proof.generate_goal(graph, goal)?,
                ArchitectureProofTask::FixedScanNonnegative { name, scan } => self
                    .proof
                    .generate_fixed_scan_nonnegative(graph, scan, name)?,
            };
            goals.push((name.to_owned(), program));
        }
        let mut gpu = Vec::new();
        for &output in outputs {
            match self.gpu.compile(graph, output) {
                Ok(program) => gpu.push(PlannedGpu::Supported {
                    output,
                    program: Box::new(program),
                }),
                Err(error @ (GpuError::UnsupportedOperation { .. } | GpuError::NoKernelGraph))
                    if gpu_requirement == GpuRequirement::AllowUnsupported =>
                {
                    gpu.push(PlannedGpu::Unsupported {
                        output,
                        reason: error.to_string(),
                    });
                }
                Err(error) => return Err(AutoBuildError::Gpu(error)),
            }
        }
        let shared_gpu = if outputs.len() > 1
            && gpu
                .iter()
                .all(|part| matches!(part, PlannedGpu::Supported { .. }))
        {
            let program = self.gpu.compile_outputs(graph, outputs)?;
            (program.kernel_count()? > 0).then_some(Box::new(program))
        } else {
            None
        };
        Ok(AutoBuildPlan {
            connectivity,
            outputs: outputs.to_vec(),
            architecture,
            goals,
            gpu,
            shared_gpu,
            identity: None,
        })
    }

    /// One developer-invoked build. A complete new auto-build/ is staged and
    /// validated before replacing the previous good bundle. Failed builds
    /// leave the previously published evidence untouched.
    /// There is no CUDA execution or claim of IEEE-754 machine equivalence.
    pub fn build(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        outputs: &[NodeId],
        tasks: &[ArchitectureProofTask],
        gpu_requirement: GpuRequirement,
        root: &Path,
    ) -> Result<AutoBuildReport, AutoBuildError> {
        self.build_with_identity(graph, outputs, tasks, gpu_requirement, root, None)
    }

    /// Certified model build. A mismatched id/version or model declaration
    /// cannot replace a previously published bundle, even if its IR matches.
    pub fn build_identified(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        outputs: &[NodeId],
        tasks: &[ArchitectureProofTask],
        root: &Path,
        identity: &str,
    ) -> Result<AutoBuildReport, AutoBuildError> {
        self.build_with_identity(
            graph,
            outputs,
            tasks,
            GpuRequirement::AllOutputs,
            root,
            Some(identity),
        )
    }

    fn build_with_identity(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        outputs: &[NodeId],
        tasks: &[ArchitectureProofTask],
        gpu_requirement: GpuRequirement,
        root: &Path,
        identity: Option<&str>,
    ) -> Result<AutoBuildReport, AutoBuildError> {
        let mut plan = self.plan(graph, outputs, tasks, gpu_requirement)?;
        let final_dir = root.join("auto-build");
        if let Some(identity) = identity {
            auto_bundle::check_existing_identity(&final_dir, identity)?;
            plan.identity = Some(identity.to_owned());
        } else if final_dir.join("identity.txt").exists() {
            return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                "generic auto-build cannot overwrite an identified certified bundle".into(),
            ));
        }
        let mut staged = StagedBuild::create(root)?;
        let directory = staged.directory.clone();
        fs::write(directory.join("semantic.ir"), graph.canonical_ir())?;
        if let Some(identity) = &plan.identity {
            fs::write(directory.join("identity.txt"), identity)?;
        }
        let lean_dir = directory.join("lean");
        fs::create_dir_all(&lean_dir)?;
        let (checked, audit) = self
            .proof
            .verify_certified(&plan.architecture, &lean_dir.join("architecture.lean"))?;
        let mut goal_theorems = Vec::new();
        let mut goal_hypotheses = Vec::new();
        let mut axiom_dependencies = audit
            .axiom_dependencies
            .iter()
            .map(|(theorem, axioms)| (format!("architecture.{theorem}"), axioms.clone()))
            .collect::<BTreeMap<_, _>>();
        for (index, (name, program)) in plan.goals.iter().enumerate() {
            let file = lean_dir.join(format!("goal_{index}_{name}.lean"));
            let (proof, goal_audit) = self.proof.verify_certified(program, &file)?;
            if goal_audit.lean_version != audit.lean_version {
                return Err(invalid(
                    "Lean version changed during the architecture build",
                ));
            }
            goal_theorems.push((name.clone(), proof.theorem_names.len()));
            goal_hypotheses.push((name.clone(), proof.assumptions));
            for (theorem, axioms) in goal_audit.axiom_dependencies {
                axiom_dependencies.insert(format!("goal_{index}_{name}.{theorem}"), axioms);
            }
        }

        let mut output_evidence = Vec::new();
        for (index, target) in plan.gpu.iter().enumerate() {
            match target {
                PlannedGpu::Supported { output, program } => {
                    let gpu_dir = directory.join(format!("gpu_{index}"));
                    self.gpu.lower(program, &gpu_dir)?;
                    let memory = program.memory_lean_program()?;
                    let (_, memory_audit) = self
                        .proof
                        .verify_certified(&memory, &gpu_dir.join("memory.lean"))?;
                    if memory_audit.lean_version != audit.lean_version {
                        return Err(invalid(
                            "Lean version changed while checking GPU memory obligations",
                        ));
                    }
                    for (theorem, axioms) in memory_audit.axiom_dependencies {
                        axiom_dependencies.insert(format!("gpu_{index}.memory.{theorem}"), axioms);
                    }
                    output_evidence.push(OutputBuildEvidence {
                        node: output.index(),
                        ptx: Some(final_dir.join(format!("gpu_{index}/graph.ptx"))),
                        reason: None,
                    });
                }
                PlannedGpu::Unsupported { output, reason } => {
                    output_evidence.push(OutputBuildEvidence {
                        node: output.index(),
                        ptx: None,
                        reason: Some(reason.clone()),
                    });
                }
            }
        }
        let shared_gpu_ptx = if let Some(program) = &plan.shared_gpu {
            let gpu_dir = directory.join("gpu_shared");
            self.gpu.lower(program, &gpu_dir)?;
            let memory = program.memory_lean_program()?;
            let (_, memory_audit) = self
                .proof
                .verify_certified(&memory, &gpu_dir.join("memory.lean"))?;
            if memory_audit.lean_version != audit.lean_version {
                return Err(invalid(
                    "Lean version changed while checking shared GPU memory obligations",
                ));
            }
            for (theorem, axioms) in memory_audit.axiom_dependencies {
                axiom_dependencies.insert(format!("gpu_shared.memory.{theorem}"), axioms);
            }
            Some(final_dir.join("gpu_shared/graph.ptx"))
        } else {
            None
        };
        fs::write(
            lean_dir.join("audit.txt"),
            audit_text(&audit.lean_version, &axiom_dependencies),
        )?;
        // DOT/PNG are mandatory bundle evidence: render them before
        // report.txt and SHA256SUMS, never during the read-only replay path.
        let ir_sha256 = auto_bundle::hash_file(&directory.join("semantic.ir"))?;
        let dot = crate::architecture::auto_architecture_dot(graph, &plan, &ir_sha256)?;
        fs::write(directory.join("architecture.dot"), dot)?;
        crate::architecture::render_dot_png(
            &directory.join("architecture.dot"),
            &directory.join("architecture.png"),
        )?;
        let mut report = AutoBuildReport {
            directory: final_dir.clone(),
            connectivity: plan.connectivity,
            output_evidence,
            shared_gpu_ptx,
            architecture_theorems: checked.theorem_names.len(),
            goal_theorems,
            source_hypotheses: checked.assumptions,
            goal_hypotheses,
            axiom_dependencies,
            lean_version: audit.lean_version,
            manifest_sha256: String::new(),
        };
        fs::write(directory.join("report.txt"), report_text(graph, &report))?;
        report.manifest_sha256 = auto_bundle::write_manifest(&directory, &plan)?;
        auto_bundle::verify_manifest(&directory, &plan, Some(&report.manifest_sha256))?;
        if let Some(identity) = &plan.identity {
            // Guard against a different writer publishing while we staged.
            auto_bundle::check_existing_identity(&final_dir, identity)?;
        }
        staged.publish(&final_dir)?;
        Ok(report)
    }
}

fn audit_text(lean_version: &str, axiom_dependencies: &BTreeMap<String, Vec<String>>) -> String {
    let mut text = format!("lean_checker_version={lean_version}\n");
    for (theorem, axioms) in axiom_dependencies {
        text.push_str(&format!("axioms={theorem};dependencies={axioms:?}\n"));
    }
    text
}

fn report_text(graph: &NeuralGraph, report: &AutoBuildReport) -> String {
    let mut text = format!(
        "architecture_assurance=ideal-Int-Lean-kernel-checked\n\
             connectivity_assurance=Rust-structural-validation\n\
             fp32_machine_equivalence=not-proven\n\
             nvidia_jit_sass_equivalence=not-proven\n\
             gpu_memory_address_contract=ideal-Int-Lean-kernel-checked-under-hypotheses\n\
             gpu_llvm_ptx_translation=structurally-validated-not-semantically-proven\n\
             fp32_numeric_error_bounds=separate-RNE-certificate-required\n\
             cuda_graph_runtime=not-executed-by-certified-build\n\
             lean_version={}\n\
             nodes={}\ndata_edges={}\nmodule_ports={}\nmodule_instances={}\n\
             architecture_theorems={}\nsource_hypotheses={:?}\n",
        report.lean_version,
        graph.nodes().len(),
        report.connectivity.data_edges,
        report.connectivity.module_ports,
        report.connectivity.module_instances,
        report.architecture_theorems,
        report.source_hypotheses,
    );
    for (name, count) in &report.goal_theorems {
        let assumptions = report
            .goal_hypotheses
            .iter()
            .find(|(goal, _)| goal == name)
            .map(|(_, hypotheses)| hypotheses.as_slice())
            .unwrap_or(&[]);
        text.push_str(&format!(
            "goal={name};lean_theorems={count};status=proven-ideal-Int;hypotheses={assumptions:?}\n"
        ));
    }
    for (theorem, axioms) in &report.axiom_dependencies {
        text.push_str(&format!("axioms={theorem};dependencies={axioms:?}\n"));
    }
    if let Some(ptx) = &report.shared_gpu_ptx {
        text.push_str(&format!(
            "gpu_shared=status=structurally-translated;outputs={:?};ptx={}\n",
            report
                .output_evidence
                .iter()
                .map(|item| item.node)
                .collect::<Vec<_>>(),
            ptx.strip_prefix(&report.directory).unwrap_or(ptx).display()
        ));
    }
    for item in &report.output_evidence {
        if let Some(ptx) = &item.ptx {
            text.push_str(&format!(
                "gpu_output={};status=structurally-translated;ptx={}\n",
                item.node,
                ptx.strip_prefix(&report.directory).unwrap_or(ptx).display()
            ));
        } else {
            text.push_str(&format!(
                "gpu_output={};status=unsupported;reason={}\n",
                item.node,
                item.reason.as_deref().unwrap_or("unknown")
            ));
        }
    }
    text
}

impl ArchitectureAutoCompiler {
    /// Offline recheck of a previously emitted bundle against this precise
    /// graph, output selection, goal list and GPU policy. First verify the
    /// complete manifest and immutable IR, then rerun Lean and inspect the
    /// saved LLVM/PTX pairs. No CUDA driver or GPU execution is required.
    ///
    /// A caller needing authenticity must separately pin the SHA256SUMS hash:
    /// the bundle's own manifest cannot authenticate itself.
    pub fn verify_bundle(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        outputs: &[NodeId],
        tasks: &[ArchitectureProofTask],
        gpu_requirement: GpuRequirement,
        root: &Path,
        pinned_sha256: Option<&str>,
    ) -> Result<AutoBuildReport, AutoBuildError> {
        let plan = self.plan(graph, outputs, tasks, gpu_requirement)?;
        self.verify_planned_bundle(graph, plan, root, pinned_sha256)
    }

    /// Offline replay of an identified certified build, without a GPU.
    pub fn verify_identified(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        outputs: &[NodeId],
        tasks: &[ArchitectureProofTask],
        root: &Path,
        pinned_sha256: Option<&str>,
        identity: &str,
    ) -> Result<AutoBuildReport, AutoBuildError> {
        let mut plan = self.plan(graph, outputs, tasks, GpuRequirement::AllOutputs)?;
        plan.identity = Some(identity.to_owned());
        self.verify_planned_bundle(graph, plan, root, pinned_sha256)
    }

    // Verification consumes the *same* planned evidence shape as the build
    // path, without an extra public identity/proof-policy argument bundle.
    fn verify_planned_bundle(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        plan: AutoBuildPlan,
        root: &Path,
        pinned_sha256: Option<&str>,
    ) -> Result<AutoBuildReport, AutoBuildError> {
        let directory = root.join("auto-build");
        if let Some(identity) = plan.identity.as_deref() {
            auto_bundle::check_existing_identity(&directory, identity)?;
        }
        let digest = auto_bundle::verify_manifest(&directory, &plan, pinned_sha256)?;
        auto_bundle::verify_current_ir(&directory, &graph.canonical_ir())?;
        let ir_sha256 = auto_bundle::hash_file(&directory.join("semantic.ir"))?;
        let expected_dot = crate::architecture::auto_architecture_dot(graph, &plan, &ir_sha256)?;
        let dot_file = directory.join("architecture.dot");
        if fs::read_to_string(&dot_file)? != expected_dot {
            return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                "architecture.dot does not match current Semantic IR and output status".into(),
            ));
        }
        // The standalone snapshot and auto-build use the same strict,
        // render-and-compare verification, including cleanup on failure.
        crate::architecture::verify_rendered_dot_png(
            &dot_file,
            &directory.join("architecture.png"),
        )
        .map_err(|error| AutoBuildError::Integrity(error.to_string()))?;
        let lean_dir = directory.join("lean");
        let mut axiom_dependencies = BTreeMap::new();
        let (lean_version, architecture_theorems) = {
            let file = lean_dir.join("architecture.lean");
            verify_source(&self.proof, &file, &plan.architecture)?;
            let audit = self
                .proof
                .audit_file(&file, plan.architecture.theorem_names())?;
            for (theorem, axioms) in audit.axiom_dependencies {
                axiom_dependencies.insert(format!("architecture.{theorem}"), axioms);
            }
            (audit.lean_version, plan.architecture.theorem_names().len())
        };
        let mut goal_theorems = Vec::new();
        let mut goal_hypotheses = Vec::new();
        for (index, (name, program)) in plan.goals.iter().enumerate() {
            let file = lean_dir.join(format!("goal_{index}_{name}.lean"));
            verify_source(&self.proof, &file, program)?;
            let audit = self.proof.audit_file(&file, program.theorem_names())?;
            if audit.lean_version != lean_version {
                return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                    "Lean checker version changed while replaying proofs".into(),
                ));
            }
            for (theorem, axioms) in audit.axiom_dependencies {
                axiom_dependencies.insert(format!("goal_{index}_{name}.{theorem}"), axioms);
            }
            goal_theorems.push((name.clone(), program.theorem_names().len()));
            goal_hypotheses.push((name.clone(), program.assumptions().to_vec()));
        }
        let mut output_evidence = Vec::new();
        for (index, item) in plan.gpu.iter().enumerate() {
            let gpu_dir = directory.join(format!("gpu_{index}"));
            match item {
                PlannedGpu::Supported { output, program } => {
                    verify_gpu_translation(program, &gpu_dir, &format!("gpu_{index}"))?;
                    let memory = program.memory_lean_program()?;
                    let memory_file = gpu_dir.join("memory.lean");
                    verify_source(&self.proof, &memory_file, &memory)?;
                    let memory_audit = self
                        .proof
                        .audit_file(&memory_file, memory.theorem_names())?;
                    if memory_audit.lean_version != lean_version {
                        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                            "Lean checker version changed while replaying GPU memory proofs".into(),
                        ));
                    }
                    for (theorem, axioms) in memory_audit.axiom_dependencies {
                        axiom_dependencies.insert(format!("gpu_{index}.memory.{theorem}"), axioms);
                    }
                    let ptx_file = gpu_dir.join("graph.ptx");
                    output_evidence.push(OutputBuildEvidence {
                        node: output.index(),
                        ptx: Some(ptx_file),
                        reason: None,
                    });
                }
                PlannedGpu::Unsupported { output, reason } => {
                    if gpu_dir.exists() {
                        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
                            "unsupported GPU output {index} has unexpected compiled artifacts"
                        )));
                    }
                    output_evidence.push(OutputBuildEvidence {
                        node: output.index(),
                        ptx: None,
                        reason: Some(reason.clone()),
                    });
                }
            }
        }
        let shared_gpu_ptx = if let Some(program) = &plan.shared_gpu {
            let shared_dir = directory.join("gpu_shared");
            verify_gpu_translation(program, &shared_dir, "gpu_shared")?;
            let memory = program.memory_lean_program()?;
            let memory_file = shared_dir.join("memory.lean");
            verify_source(&self.proof, &memory_file, &memory)?;
            let memory_audit = self
                .proof
                .audit_file(&memory_file, memory.theorem_names())?;
            if memory_audit.lean_version != lean_version {
                return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                    "Lean checker version changed while replaying shared GPU memory proofs".into(),
                ));
            }
            for (theorem, axioms) in memory_audit.axiom_dependencies {
                axiom_dependencies.insert(format!("gpu_shared.memory.{theorem}"), axioms);
            }
            Some(shared_dir.join("graph.ptx"))
        } else {
            if directory.join("gpu_shared").exists() {
                return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                    "unexpected shared GPU artifact for unsupported output selection".into(),
                ));
            }
            None
        };
        if fs::read_to_string(lean_dir.join("audit.txt"))?
            != audit_text(&lean_version, &axiom_dependencies)
        {
            return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                "saved Lean axiom dependencies or checker version no longer match".into(),
            ));
        }
        let report = AutoBuildReport {
            directory: directory.clone(),
            connectivity: plan.connectivity,
            output_evidence,
            shared_gpu_ptx,
            architecture_theorems,
            goal_theorems,
            source_hypotheses: plan.architecture.assumptions().to_vec(),
            goal_hypotheses,
            axiom_dependencies,
            lean_version,
            manifest_sha256: digest,
        };
        if fs::read_to_string(directory.join("report.txt"))? != report_text(graph, &report) {
            return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                "auto-build report does not describe the freshly rechecked evidence".into(),
            ));
        }
        Ok(report)
    }
}

fn verify_gpu_translation(
    program: &GpuProgram,
    directory: &Path,
    label: &str,
) -> Result<(), AutoBuildError> {
    if fs::read_to_string(directory.join("graph.ll"))? != program.llvm_ir() {
        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
            "{label} LLVM differs from current Semantic IR"
        )));
    }
    let capability = program.capability_plan()?;
    if fs::read_to_string(directory.join("capability.plan"))? != capability.to_text() {
        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
            "{label} GPU capability plan mismatch"
        )));
    }
    let translation = program.translation_plan()?;
    if fs::read_to_string(directory.join("translation.plan"))? != translation.to_text() {
        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
            "{label} translation plan mismatch"
        )));
    }
    let ptx = fs::read_to_string(directory.join("graph.ptx"))?;
    let checked = translation
        .validate(program.llvm_ir(), &ptx)
        .map_err(|err| {
            AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!("{label} LLVM/PTX translation rejected: {err}"))
        })?;
    if fs::read_to_string(directory.join("translation.report"))? != checked.to_text() {
        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
            "{label} translation report mismatch"
        )));
    }
    Ok(())
}

fn verify_source(
    proof: &LeanProofEngine,
    path: &Path,
    expected: &LeanProgram,
) -> Result<(), AutoBuildError> {
    if fs::read_to_string(path)? != expected.source() {
        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
            "saved Lean source differs from the generated current proof: {}",
            path.display()
        )));
    }
    proof.check_file(path)?;
    Ok(())
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod staged_build_tests {
    use super::*;

    fn test_root(name: &str) -> PathBuf {
        std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "verineural-{name}-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ))
    }

    #[test]
    fn failed_staging_does_not_destroy_previous_bundle() {
        let root = test_root("rollback");
        let old = root.join("auto-build");
        fs::create_dir_all(&old).unwrap();
        fs::write(old.join("SHA256SUMS"), b"old-valid-bundle").unwrap();
        let staging_path = {
            let staged = StagedBuild::create(&root).unwrap();
            fs::write(staged.directory.join("architecture.lean"), b"incomplete").unwrap();
            staged.directory.clone()
        }; // Simulate a proof/backend failure before publication.
        assert!(!staging_path.exists());
        assert_eq!(
            fs::read(old.join("SHA256SUMS")).unwrap(),
            b"old-valid-bundle"
        );
        fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    #[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
    fn successful_publication_atomically_swaps_and_cleans_previous_bundle() {
        let root = test_root("publish");
        let _ = fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        let old = root.join("auto-build");
        fs::create_dir_all(&old).unwrap();
        fs::write(old.join("report.txt"), "old").unwrap();
        let mut staged = StagedBuild::create(&root).unwrap();
        let staging = staged.directory.clone();
        fs::write(staging.join("report.txt"), "new").unwrap();
        staged.publish(&old).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(fs::read_to_string(old.join("report.txt")).unwrap(), "new");
        assert!(!staging.exists());
        fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn initial_publication_and_rejection_of_symlink_bundle() {
        let root = test_root("initial");
        let _ = fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        let final_dir = root.join("auto-build");
        let mut staged = StagedBuild::create(&root).unwrap();
        fs::write(staged.directory.join("report.txt"), "initial").unwrap();
        staged.publish(&final_dir).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(
            fs::read_to_string(final_dir.join("report.txt")).unwrap(),
            "initial"
        );
        #[cfg(unix)]
        {
            use std::os::unix::fs::symlink;
            fs::rename(&final_dir, root.join("owned")).unwrap();
            symlink("owned", &final_dir).unwrap();
            let mut rejected = StagedBuild::create(&root).unwrap();
            assert!(matches!(
                rejected.publish(&final_dir),
                Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(_))
            ));
        }
        fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/auto_bundle.rs
//! Integrity and current-source binding for the developer-run auto build.
//! SHA256SUMS proves artifact integrity relative to a separately pinned digest;
//! it is not a signature and cannot prove NVIDIA machine semantics.
use std::fs;
use std::path::Path;

use crate::auto_build::{AutoBuildError, AutoBuildPlan, PlannedGpu};

const MANIFEST: &str = "SHA256SUMS";

pub(super) fn hash_file(path: &Path) -> Result<String, AutoBuildError> {
    crate::certificate::hash_file(path).map_err(|err| AutoBuildError::Integrity(err.to_string()))
}

/// The expected artifact set is derived from the current plan, never from
/// user-controlled manifest lines. Paths are relative to auto-build/.
pub(super) fn artifact_files(plan: &AutoBuildPlan) -> Vec<String> {
    let mut files = vec![
        "semantic.ir".to_owned(),
        "architecture.dot".to_owned(),
        "architecture.png".to_owned(),
        "report.txt".to_owned(),
        "lean/architecture.lean".to_owned(),
        "lean/audit.txt".to_owned(),
    ];
    if plan.identity.is_some() {
        files.push("identity.txt".to_owned());
    }
    for (index, (name, _)) in plan.goals.iter().enumerate() {
        files.push(format!("lean/goal_{index}_{name}.lean"));
    }
    for (index, item) in plan.gpu.iter().enumerate() {
        if matches!(item, PlannedGpu::Supported { .. }) {
            for name in [
                "graph.ll",
                "graph.ptx",
                "translation.plan",
                "translation.report",
                "capability.plan",
                "memory.lean",
            ] {
                files.push(format!("gpu_{index}/{name}"));
            }
        }
    }
    if plan.shared_gpu.is_some() {
        for name in [
            "graph.ll",
            "graph.ptx",
            "translation.plan",
            "translation.report",
            "capability.plan",
            "memory.lean",
        ] {
            files.push(format!("gpu_shared/{name}"));
        }
    }
    files.sort();
    files
}

fn identity_without_graph_allocation(text: &str) -> String {
    let mut normalized = text.to_owned();
    const MARKER: &str = "NodeId { graph: ";
    while let Some(start) = normalized.find(MARKER) {
        let search_from = start + MARKER.len();
        let Some(relative) = normalized[search_from..].find(", index: ") else {
            break;
        };
        let comma = search_from + relative;
        // Preserve the old Debug-shaped declaration except for the graph
        // allocation identity, which has no semantic meaning.
        normalized.replace_range(start..comma + 2, "NodeId { ");
    }
    normalized
}

fn compatible_identity(saved: &str, expected: &str) -> bool {
    saved == expected
        || identity_without_graph_allocation(saved) == identity_without_graph_allocation(expected)
}

/// Reject foreign or legacy bundles before starting a new staged build.
/// Identity is checked again during replay, and SHA256SUMS covers its bytes.
/// Older v1 identities are accepted only when removing NodeId graph allocation
/// numbers makes the complete declarations byte-for-byte equal.
pub(super) fn check_existing_identity(dir: &Path, expected: &str) -> Result<(), AutoBuildError> {
    match fs::symlink_metadata(dir) {
        Err(err) if err.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => return Ok(()),
        Err(err) => return Err(err.into()),
        Ok(meta) if meta.file_type().is_symlink() => {
            return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                "certified bundle directory cannot be a symlink".into(),
            ));
        }
        Ok(_) => {}
    }
    if !dir.is_dir() {
        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
            "certified output is not a directory: {}",
            dir.display()
        )));
    }
    let saved = fs::read_to_string(dir.join("identity.txt")).map_err(|_| {
        AutoBuildError::Integrity("existing bundle lacks a readable certified identity".into())
    })?;
    if !compatible_identity(&saved, expected) {
        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
            "existing bundle belongs to a different model identity or declaration".into(),
        ));
    }
    Ok(())
}

fn manifest_text(dir: &Path, plan: &AutoBuildPlan) -> Result<String, AutoBuildError> {
    let mut text = String::new();
    for name in artifact_files(plan) {
        let path = dir.join(&name);
        if !path.is_file() {
            return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
                "required auto-build artifact missing: {name}"
            )));
        }
        text.push_str(&format!("{}  {name}\n", hash_file(&path)?));
    }
    Ok(text)
}

pub(super) fn write_manifest(dir: &Path, plan: &AutoBuildPlan) -> Result<String, AutoBuildError> {
    fs::write(dir.join(MANIFEST), manifest_text(dir, plan)?)?;
    hash_file(&dir.join(MANIFEST))
}

pub(super) fn verify_manifest(
    dir: &Path,
    plan: &AutoBuildPlan,
    expected_digest: Option<&str>,
) -> Result<String, AutoBuildError> {
    let existing = fs::read_to_string(dir.join(MANIFEST))?;
    if let Some(identity) = &plan.identity {
        check_existing_identity(dir, identity)?;
    }
    let expected = manifest_text(dir, plan)?;
    if existing != expected {
        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
            "SHA256SUMS does not match the complete expected artifact set".into(),
        ));
    }
    let digest = hash_file(&dir.join(MANIFEST))?;
    if expected_digest.is_some_and(|pinned| pinned != digest) {
        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
            "externally pinned manifest digest mismatch".into(),
        ));
    }
    Ok(digest)
}

pub(super) fn verify_current_ir(dir: &Path, source: &str) -> Result<(), AutoBuildError> {
    if fs::read_to_string(dir.join("semantic.ir"))? != source {
        return Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(
            "saved auto-build IR differs from current Rust architecture".into(),
        ));
    }
    Ok(())
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use crate::{ArchitectureAutoCompiler, Domain, GpuRequirement, NeuralGraph, NodeId, Shape};

    fn graph() -> (NeuralGraph, NodeId) {
        let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
        let x = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
        let output = graph.relu(x).unwrap();
        (graph, output)
    }

    #[test]
    fn canonical_ir_is_graph_identity_independent_and_semantic() {
        let (g1, _) = graph();
        let (g2, _) = graph();
        let ir1 = g1.canonical_ir();
        assert_eq!(ir1, g2.canonical_ir());
        assert!(ir1.starts_with("verineural-semantic-ir-v4\n"));
        assert!(!ir1.contains("MathContract {"));
        assert!(!ir1.contains("FP32Policy {"));

        let mut other = NeuralGraph::default();
        let x = other.input(Shape::new(vec![3]).unwrap(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
        let _y = other.relu(x).unwrap();
        assert_ne!(ir1, other.canonical_ir());
    }

    #[test]
    fn auto_manifest_detects_tampering_and_rejects_unpinned_or_wrong_artifacts() {
        let (graph, output) = graph();
        let plan = ArchitectureAutoCompiler::default()
            .plan(&graph, &[output], &[], GpuRequirement::AllOutputs)
            .unwrap();
        let root = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "verineural-auto-bundle-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        if root.exists() {
            std::fs::remove_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
        }
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
        let files = artifact_files(&plan);
        assert!(files.contains(&"gpu_0/graph.ptx".to_owned()));
        assert!(files.contains(&"architecture.dot".to_owned()));
        assert!(files.contains(&"architecture.png".to_owned()));
        for file in &files {
            let path = root.join(file);
            if let Some(parent) = path.parent() {
                std::fs::create_dir_all(parent).unwrap();
            }
            std::fs::write(path, file.as_bytes()).unwrap();
        }
        let digest = write_manifest(&root, &plan).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(
            verify_manifest(&root, &plan, Some(&digest)).unwrap(),
            digest
        );
        assert!(matches!(
            verify_manifest(&root, &plan, Some(&"0".repeat(64))),
            Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(_))
        ));
        assert!(matches!(
            verify_current_ir(&root, "a different current graph"),
            Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(_))
        ));
        std::fs::write(root.join("gpu_0/graph.ptx"), b"tampered!").unwrap();
        assert!(matches!(
            verify_manifest(&root, &plan, None),
            Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(_))
        ));
        std::fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn legacy_identity_migrates_only_graph_allocation_numbers() {
        let root = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "verineural-identity-graph-migration-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        fs::create_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
        let old = "verineural-certified-model-v1\nid=lab\nversion=1\n\
goal=p;node=2;kind=Predicate(PointwiseLe(Node(NodeId { graph: 77, index: 0 }), Output))\n";
        let stable = "verineural-certified-model-v1\nid=lab\nversion=1\n\
goal=p;node=2;kind=Predicate(PointwiseLe(Node(NodeId { index: 0 }), Output))\n";
        fs::write(root.join("identity.txt"), old).unwrap();
        check_existing_identity(&root, stable).unwrap();

        let changed = stable.replace("index: 0", "index: 1");
        assert!(matches!(
            check_existing_identity(&root, &changed),
            Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(_))
        ));
        fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn certified_identity_prevents_cross_model_overwrite() {
        let root = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "verineural-identity-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        fs::create_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
        fs::write(root.join("identity.txt"), "id=xor\nversion=1\n").unwrap();
        check_existing_identity(&root, "id=xor\nversion=1\n").unwrap();
        assert!(matches!(
            check_existing_identity(&root, "id=other\nversion=1\n"),
            Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(_))
        ));
        fs::remove_file(root.join("identity.txt")).unwrap();
        assert!(check_existing_identity(&root, "id=xor\nversion=1\n").is_err());
        fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    #[cfg(unix)]
    fn existing_certified_bundle_symlink_is_rejected() {
        use std::os::unix::fs::symlink;
        let root = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "verineural-symlink-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        let _ = fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        fs::create_dir_all(root.join("real")).unwrap();
        fs::write(root.join("real/identity.txt"), "id=lab\nversion=1\n").unwrap();
        symlink("real", root.join("auto-build")).unwrap();
        assert!(matches!(
            check_existing_identity(&root.join("auto-build"), "id=lab\nversion=1\n"),
            Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(_))
        ));
        fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn shared_output_bundle_names_are_required_when_two_outputs_are_gpu_supported() {
        let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
        let shape = Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap();
        let a = graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
        let b = graph.input(shape, Domain::Finite);
        let common = graph.add(a, b).unwrap();
        let output = graph.relu(common).unwrap();
        let plan = ArchitectureAutoCompiler::default()
            .plan(&graph, &[common, output], &[], GpuRequirement::AllOutputs)
            .unwrap();
        let files = artifact_files(&plan);
        assert!(plan.shared_gpu.is_some());
        assert!(files.contains(&"gpu_shared/graph.ll".to_owned()));
        assert!(files.contains(&"gpu_shared/graph.ptx".to_owned()));
        assert!(files.contains(&"gpu_shared/translation.plan".to_owned()));
        assert!(files.contains(&"gpu_shared/translation.report".to_owned()));
        assert!(files.contains(&"gpu_0/graph.ptx".to_owned()));
        assert!(files.contains(&"gpu_1/graph.ptx".to_owned()));
    }

    #[test]
    fn auto_manifest_requires_entire_planned_gpu_and_lean_artifact_set() {
        let (graph, output) = graph();
        let plan = ArchitectureAutoCompiler::default()
            .plan(&graph, &[output], &[], GpuRequirement::AllOutputs)
            .unwrap();
        let root = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "verineural-auto-missing-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
        assert!(matches!(
            write_manifest(&root, &plan),
            Err(AutoBuildError::Integrity(_))
        ));
        std::fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/autodiff.rs
//! Bounded reverse-mode differentiation of the *same* typed Semantic Neural IR.
//! Creates a second ordinary NeuralGraph by appending derivatives to a clone.
//! No opaque callbacks, no architecture-specific kernels and no fictitious FP32
//! certificate: mathematical reverse rules and NVIDIA execution are separate.
use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};
use std::error::Error;
use std::fmt;

use crate::{DType, Domain, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NodeId, Operation, Shape, Tensor};

#[derive(Debug)]
pub enum DifferentiationError {
    Neural(NeuralError),
    Invalid(&'static str),
    Unsupported {
        node: usize,
        operation: &'static str,
    },
}

impl fmt::Display for DifferentiationError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        match self {
            Self::Neural(err) => write!(f, "{err}"),
            Self::Invalid(s) => write!(f, "invalid derivative request: {s}"),
            Self::Unsupported { node, operation } => write!(
                f,
                "reverse-mode node {node}: unsupported derivative for {operation}"
            ),
        }
    }
}
impl Error for DifferentiationError {}
impl From<NeuralError> for DifferentiationError {
    fn from(err: NeuralError) -> Self {
        Self::Neural(err)
    }
}

/// Differentiable graph contains the *primal* as an unchanged prefix.
/// Input/output NodeId values therefore retain their graph identity.
/// Added source tensors are explicit and appear in 'constants'.
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct ReverseGraph {
    graph: NeuralGraph,
    root: NodeId,
    seed: Option<NodeId>,
    gradients: Vec<(NodeId, NodeId)>,
    constants: Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>,
}

impl ReverseGraph {
    pub fn graph(&self) -> &NeuralGraph {
        &self.graph
    }
    pub fn root(&self) -> NodeId {
        self.root
    }
    pub fn seed(&self) -> NodeId {
        self.seed.expect("graph-provided VJP has no external seed")
    }
    pub fn gradients(&self) -> &[(NodeId, NodeId)] {
        &self.gradients
    }
    pub fn constants(&self) -> &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)] {
        &self.constants
    }
    pub fn gradient_of(&self, node: NodeId) -> Option<NodeId> {
        self.gradients
            .iter()
            .find(|(source, _)| *source == node)
            .map(|(_, grad)| *grad)
    }

    /// Add seed and internally generated zero/one tensors to primal bindings.
    /// Filter this result to GpuProgram::source_inputs before a sliced GPU run.
    pub fn bindings(
        &self,
        primal: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)],
        seed: Tensor<f32>,
    ) -> Result<Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>, DifferentiationError> {
        let source = self.seed.ok_or(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
            "graph-provided VJP does not accept an external seed",
        ))?;
        if seed.shape() != &self.graph.node(self.root)?.shape {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
                "seed shape differs from differentiated output",
            ));
        }
        if seed.values().iter().any(|v| !v.is_finite()) {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid("seed must be finite"));
        }
        let mut result = primal.to_vec();
        result.push((source, seed));
        result.extend(self.constants.iter().cloned());
        Ok(result)
    }
}

struct ReverseBuilder {
    graph: NeuralGraph,
    constants: Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>,
    fills: BTreeMap<(Vec<usize>, u32), NodeId>,
}

impl ReverseBuilder {
    fn fill(&mut self, shape: &Shape, value: f32) -> Result<NodeId, DifferentiationError> {
        let key = (shape.dims().to_vec(), value.to_bits());
        if let Some(id) = self.fills.get(&key) {
            return Ok(*id);
        }
        let tensor = Tensor::from_vec(key.0.clone(), vec![value; shape.element_count()])?;
        let id = self.graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
        self.constants.push((id, tensor));
        self.fills.insert(key, id);
        Ok(id)
    }

    fn neg(&mut self, value: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, DifferentiationError> {
        let shape = self.graph.node(value)?.shape.clone();
        let zero = self.fill(&shape, 0.)?;
        Ok(self.graph.sub(zero, value)?)
    }

    fn reduce_scalar(&mut self, grad: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, DifferentiationError> {
        let shape = self.graph.node(grad)?.shape.clone();
        if shape.dims() == [1, 1] {
            return Ok(grad);
        }
        if shape.rank() != 2 || shape.dims()[0] != 1 {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
                "scalar broadcast adjoint supports one row",
            ));
        }
        let ones = self.fill(&Shape::new(vec![shape.dims()[1], 1])?, 1.)?;
        Ok(self.graph.matmul(grad, ones)?)
    }

    fn scatter_slice(
        &mut self,
        grad: NodeId,
        start: usize,
        source_width: usize,
    ) -> Result<NodeId, DifferentiationError> {
        let written = self.graph.node(grad)?.shape.element_count();
        let mut parts = Vec::new();
        if start != 0 {
            parts.push(self.fill(&Shape::new(vec![1, start])?, 0.)?);
        }
        parts.push(grad);
        if start + written < source_width {
            parts.push(self.fill(&Shape::new(vec![1, source_width - start - written])?, 0.)?);
        }
        Ok(self.graph.concat(1, &parts)?)
    }
}

fn pointwise_kind(operation: &Operation) -> Option<&'static str> {
    let Operation::Pointwise(spec) = operation else {
        return None;
    };
    match (
        spec.id(),
        spec.version(),
        spec.arity(),
        spec.expression().canonical().as_str(),
    ) {
        ("verineural.sub", "1", 2, "sub(arg:0,arg:1)") => Some("sub"),
        ("verineural.div", "1", 2, "div(arg:0,arg:1)") => Some("div"),
        ("verineural.exp", "1", 1, "exp(arg:0)") => Some("exp"),
        ("verineural.sqrt", "1", 1, "sqrt(arg:0)") => Some("sqrt"),
        _ => None,
    }
}

fn supported(operation: &Operation, shape: &Shape, inputs: &[Shape]) -> bool {
    match operation {
        Operation::Input
        | Operation::Add
        | Operation::Mul
        | Operation::MatMul
        | Operation::BiasAdd
        | Operation::Reshape(_) => true,
        Operation::Permute { axes } => axes.as_slice() == [1, 0] && shape.rank() == 2,
        Operation::ReverseAxis { axis } => shape.rank() == 2 && *axis < 2,
        Operation::SliceAxis { axis: 1, .. } => {
            shape.rank() == 2 && shape.dims()[0] == 1 && inputs[0].dims()[0] == 1
        }
        Operation::Concat { axis: 1 } => {
            shape.rank() == 2 && shape.dims()[0] == 1 && inputs.iter().all(|s| s.dims()[0] == 1)
        }
        Operation::BroadcastTo(_) => {
            inputs[0] == *shape
                || (inputs[0].dims() == [1, 1] && shape.rank() == 2 && shape.dims()[0] == 1)
        }
        Operation::Pointwise(_) => pointwise_kind(operation).is_some(),
        _ => false,
    }
}

/// The seed is dL/d(root), supplied by the consumer. The returned graph
/// computes vector-Jacobian products for arbitrary requested primal inputs.
/// Input sources not depending on 'root' receive exact zero gradient.
/// All *reachable* primal operations are checked before derivative construction.
pub fn differentiate(
    primal: &NeuralGraph,
    root: NodeId,
    wrt: &[NodeId],
) -> Result<ReverseGraph, DifferentiationError> {
    let output = primal.node(root)?;
    let mut seeded = primal.clone();
    let seed = seeded.input(output.shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    differentiate_impl(&seeded, &[(root, seed)], wrt, Some(seed))
}

/// Compute the sum of vector-Jacobian products for multiple output roots.
/// Each seed is an existing IR expression, treated as a terminal adjoint.
/// Gradients do NOT propagate through the expression producing a seed.
/// This allows GPU loss-gradient construction and parameter VJPs in one
/// executable CUDA Graph; no machine-code/FP32 certificate is claimed.
pub fn differentiate_with_seeds(
    primal: &NeuralGraph,
    roots: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
    wrt: &[NodeId],
) -> Result<ReverseGraph, DifferentiationError> {
    differentiate_impl(primal, roots, wrt, None)
}

fn differentiate_impl(
    primal: &NeuralGraph,
    roots: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
    wrt: &[NodeId],
    external_seed: Option<NodeId>,
) -> Result<ReverseGraph, DifferentiationError> {
    let Some(&(root, _)) = roots.first() else {
        return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
            "at least one output/seed pair required",
        ));
    };
    let mut unique_roots = BTreeSet::new();
    for &(output, seed) in roots {
        let y = primal.node(output)?;
        let s = primal.node(seed)?;
        if !unique_roots.insert(output.index())
            || y.dtype != DType::F32
            || s.dtype != DType::F32
            || y.shape != s.shape
        {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
                "output/seed pairs must be unique, matching F32 tensors",
            ));
        }
    }
    if wrt.is_empty() {
        return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
            "at least one gradient target required",
        ));
    }
    let mut seen = BTreeSet::new();
    for &id in wrt {
        let node = primal.node(id)?;
        if !seen.insert(id.index())
            || node.dtype != DType::F32
            || !matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input)
        {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
                "gradient targets must be distinct F32 source nodes",
            ));
        }
    }

    let mut reachable = BTreeSet::new();
    let mut pending = roots.iter().map(|&(y, _)| y).collect::<Vec<_>>();
    while let Some(id) = pending.pop() {
        let node = primal.node(id)?;
        if !reachable.insert(id.index()) {
            continue;
        }
        let inputs = node
            .inputs
            .iter()
            .map(|x| primal.node(*x).map(|n| n.shape.clone()))
            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;
        if !supported(&node.operation, &node.shape, &inputs) {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Unsupported {
                node: id.index(),
                operation: node.operation.name(),
            });
        }
        pending.extend(node.inputs.iter().copied());
    }

    // Retain only primal nodes that can transmit an adjoint to requested
    // targets. This matters for a 1,920-node network when training one small
    // parameter: backprop must not materialize irrelevant derivative kernels.
    let mut relevant = wrt.iter().map(|id| id.index()).collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();
    for &index in &reachable {
        if primal.nodes()[index]
            .inputs
            .iter()
            .any(|id| relevant.contains(&id.index()))
        {
            relevant.insert(index);
        }
    }
    let mut b = ReverseBuilder {
        graph: primal.clone(),
        constants: Vec::new(),
        fills: BTreeMap::new(),
    };
    let mut adjoints = BTreeMap::<usize, NodeId>::new();
    for &(y, seed) in roots {
        adjoints.insert(y.index(), seed);
    }
    for index in reachable.into_iter().rev() {
        if !relevant.contains(&index) {
            continue;
        }
        let Some(delta) = adjoints.get(&index).copied() else {
            continue;
        };
        let node = primal.nodes()[index].clone();
        let ids = &node.inputs;
        let contributions: Vec<(NodeId, NodeId)> = match &node.operation {
            Operation::Input => vec![],
            Operation::Add => vec![(ids[0], delta), (ids[1], delta)],
            Operation::Mul => vec![
                (ids[0], b.graph.mul(delta, ids[1])?),
                (ids[1], b.graph.mul(delta, ids[0])?),
            ],
            Operation::MatMul => {
                let a_t = b.graph.permute(ids[0], &[1, 0])?;
                let b_t = b.graph.permute(ids[1], &[1, 0])?;
                vec![
                    (ids[0], b.graph.matmul(delta, b_t)?),
                    (ids[1], b.graph.matmul(a_t, delta)?),
                ]
            }
            Operation::BiasAdd => {
                let bias_shape = &primal.node(ids[1])?.shape;
                let mut db = delta;
                let rows = node.shape.dims()[0];
                if rows > 1 {
                    let ones = b.fill(&Shape::new(vec![1, rows])?, 1.)?;
                    db = b.graph.matmul(ones, delta)?;
                }
                db = b.graph.reshape(db, bias_shape.clone())?;
                vec![(ids[0], delta), (ids[1], db)]
            }
            Operation::Reshape(_) => vec![(
                ids[0],
                b.graph.reshape(delta, primal.node(ids[0])?.shape.clone())?,
            )],
            Operation::Permute { .. } => vec![(ids[0], b.graph.permute(delta, &[1, 0])?)],
            Operation::ReverseAxis { axis } => vec![(ids[0], b.graph.reverse_axis(delta, *axis)?)],
            Operation::Concat { axis: 1 } => {
                let left = primal.node(ids[0])?.shape.dims()[1];
                let right = primal.node(ids[1])?.shape.dims()[1];
                vec![
                    (ids[0], b.graph.slice_axis(delta, 1, 0, left)?),
                    (ids[1], b.graph.slice_axis(delta, 1, left, right)?),
                ]
            }
            Operation::SliceAxis { axis: 1, start, .. } => {
                let width = primal.node(ids[0])?.shape.dims()[1];
                vec![(ids[0], b.scatter_slice(delta, *start, width)?)]
            }
            Operation::BroadcastTo(_) => {
                let source_shape = &primal.node(ids[0])?.shape;
                let grad = if source_shape == &node.shape {
                    delta
                } else {
                    b.reduce_scalar(delta)?
                };
                vec![(ids[0], grad)]
            }
            Operation::Pointwise(_) => match pointwise_kind(&node.operation) {
                Some("sub") => vec![(ids[0], delta), (ids[1], b.neg(delta)?)],
                Some("div") => {
                    let da = b.graph.div(delta, ids[1])?;
                    let scaled = b.graph.mul(delta, node.id)?;
                    let db = b.graph.div(scaled, ids[1])?;
                    vec![(ids[0], da), (ids[1], b.neg(db)?)]
                }
                Some("exp") => vec![(ids[0], b.graph.mul(delta, node.id)?)],
                Some("sqrt") => {
                    let two_y = b.graph.add(node.id, node.id)?;
                    vec![(ids[0], b.graph.div(delta, two_y)?)]
                }
                _ => unreachable!("prevalidated pointwise signature"),
            },
            _ => unreachable!("prevalidated differentiability rule"),
        };
        for (source, grad) in contributions {
            if !relevant.contains(&source.index()) {
                continue;
            }
            if let Some(existing) = adjoints.get(&source.index()).copied() {
                let summed = b.graph.add(existing, grad)?;
                adjoints.insert(source.index(), summed);
            } else {
                adjoints.insert(source.index(), grad);
            }
        }
    }
    let gradients = wrt
        .iter()
        .map(|&target| {
            let grad = match adjoints.get(&target.index()).copied() {
                Some(id) => id,
                None => b.fill(&primal.node(target)?.shape, 0.)?,
            };
            Ok((target, grad))
        })
        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, DifferentiationError>>()?;
    Ok(ReverseGraph {
        graph: b.graph,
        root,
        seed: external_seed,
        gradients,
        constants: b.constants,
    })
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/bin/cargo-verineural.rs
//! Cargo subcommand dispatches consumer-owned certified entrypoints.
//! Build semantics stay in Model::certify, never in this launcher.
use std::env;
use std::error::Error;
use std::fmt;
use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
use std::process::{Command, ExitCode};

const USAGE: &str = "usage: cargo verineural <build|verify> --certified [--manifest-path path/to/Cargo.toml] [--artifact-root path] [--pinned-sha256 64-hex-digest (verify only)]";

#[derive(Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
struct CliError(String);
impl fmt::Display for CliError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        f.write_str(&self.0)
    }
}
impl Error for CliError {}

#[derive(Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
struct Cli {
    verify: bool,
    manifest: PathBuf,
    artifact_root: Option<PathBuf>,
    pinned: Option<String>,
}

fn fail(message: &str) -> CliError {
    CliError(format!("{message}\n{USAGE}"))
}

fn parse(args: impl IntoIterator<Item = String>, cwd: &Path) -> Result<Cli, CliError> {
    let mut args = args.into_iter().peekable();
    if args.peek().is_some_and(|a| a == "verineural") {
        args.next();
    }
    let verify = match args.next().as_deref() {
        Some("build") => false,
        Some("verify") => true,
        Some("--help" | "-h") => return Err(CliError(USAGE.into())),
        _ => return Err(fail("expected build or verify")),
    };
    let mut certified = false;
    let mut manifest: Option<PathBuf> = None;
    let mut artifact_root = None;
    let mut pinned = None;
    while let Some(flag) = args.next() {
        match flag.as_str() {
            "--certified" if !certified => certified = true,
            "--manifest-path" if manifest.is_none() => {
                manifest = Some(PathBuf::from(
                    args.next().ok_or_else(|| fail("missing manifest path"))?,
                ));
            }
            "--artifact-root" if artifact_root.is_none() => {
                artifact_root = Some(PathBuf::from(
                    args.next().ok_or_else(|| fail("missing artifact root"))?,
                ));
            }
            "--pinned-sha256" if verify && pinned.is_none() => {
                let raw = args.next().ok_or_else(|| fail("missing pinned sha256"))?;
                if raw.len() != 64 || !raw.bytes().all(|c| c.is_ascii_hexdigit()) {
                    return Err(fail(
                        "pinned SHA256 must be exactly 64 hexadecimal characters",
                    ));
                }
                pinned = Some(raw);
            }
            _ => return Err(fail("unsupported, repeated or misplaced option")),
        }
    }
    if !certified {
        return Err(fail("--certified is required"));
    }
    let manifest = manifest.unwrap_or_else(|| PathBuf::from("Cargo.toml"));
    if manifest.file_name().is_none_or(|n| n != "Cargo.toml") {
        return Err(fail("--manifest-path must name Cargo.toml"));
    }
    let manifest = if manifest.is_absolute() {
        manifest
    } else {
        cwd.join(manifest)
    };
    Ok(Cli {
        verify,
        manifest,
        artifact_root,
        pinned,
    })
}

// Cargo's workspace example binaries share one target directory. Select the
// consumer-specific `<name>_certified.rs` target without hardcoding a lab.
fn certified_example(package: &Path) -> Result<String, CliError> {
    let entries = std::fs::read_dir(package.join("examples"))
        .map_err(|error| fail(&format!("cannot list consumer examples: {error}")))?;
    let mut matches = Vec::new();
    for entry in entries {
        let entry = entry.map_err(|error| fail(&format!("cannot read example: {error}")))?;
        if !entry
            .file_type()
            .map_err(|error| fail(&format!("cannot stat example: {error}")))?
            .is_file()
        {
            continue;
        }
        let name = entry.file_name();
        let Some(stem) = name
            .to_str()
            .and_then(|name| name.strip_suffix("_certified.rs"))
        else {
            continue;
        };
        if !stem.is_empty() && stem.bytes().all(|c| c.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || c == b'_') {
            matches.push(format!("{stem}_certified"));
        }
    }
    matches.sort();
    match matches.as_slice() {
        [only] => Ok(only.clone()),
        [] => Err(fail(
            "consumer must provide exactly one examples/<name>_certified.rs",
        )),
        _ => Err(fail(
            "multiple certified entrypoints; select a package with exactly one",
        )),
    }
}

fn run() -> Result<ExitCode, Box<dyn Error>> {
    let opts = parse(env::args().skip(1), &env::current_dir()?)?;
    let manifest = opts.manifest.canonicalize().map_err(|e| {
        CliError(format!(
            "cannot read package manifest {}: {e}",
            opts.manifest.display()
        ))
    })?;
    let package = manifest
        .parent()
        .ok_or_else(|| fail("manifest has no package directory"))?;
    let manifest_text = std::fs::read_to_string(&manifest)?;
    if !manifest_text.lines().any(|line| line.trim() == "[package]") {
        return Err(fail("select a Cargo package, not the workspace root").into());
    }
    if !package.join("src/lib.rs").is_file() {
        return Err(fail("package must define an architecture in src/lib.rs").into());
    }
    let example = certified_example(package)?;
    let mut cargo = Command::new(env::var_os("CARGO").unwrap_or_else(|| "cargo".into()));
    cargo
        .arg("run")
        .arg("--manifest-path")
        .arg(&manifest)
        .arg("--example")
        .arg(example)
        .arg("--");
    if opts.verify {
        cargo.arg("--verify");
    }
    if let Some(root) = opts.artifact_root {
        cargo.arg("--artifact-root").arg(root);
    }
    if let Some(pin) = opts.pinned {
        cargo.arg("--pinned-sha256").arg(pin);
    }
    let status = cargo.status()?;
    Ok(ExitCode::from(
        status.code().unwrap_or(1).try_into().unwrap_or(1),
    ))
}

fn main() -> ExitCode {
    match run() {
        Ok(code) => code,
        Err(error) => {
            eprintln!("verineural: {error}");
            ExitCode::FAILURE
        }
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    fn strings(args: &[&str]) -> Vec<String> {
        args.iter().map(|v| (*v).to_owned()).collect()
    }

    #[test]
    fn cargo_subcommand_and_manifest_paths() {
        let cli = parse(
            strings(&[
                "verineural",
                "build",
                "--certified",
                "--manifest-path",
                "labs/x/Cargo.toml",
                "--artifact-root",
                "out",
            ]),
            Path::new("/repo"),
        )
        .unwrap();
        assert_eq!(cli.manifest, Path::new("/repo/labs/x/Cargo.toml"));
        assert_eq!(cli.artifact_root.as_deref(), Some(Path::new("out")));
        assert!(!cli.verify);
    }

    #[test]
    fn certified_entrypoint_is_unique_and_architecture_neutral() {
        let root = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "verineural-example-selection-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join("examples")).unwrap();
        assert!(certified_example(&root).is_err());
        std::fs::write(root.join("examples/xor_certified.rs"), "").unwrap();
        std::fs::write(root.join("examples/other.rs"), "").unwrap();
        assert_eq!(certified_example(&root).unwrap(), "xor_certified");
        std::fs::write(root.join("examples/other_certified.rs"), "").unwrap();
        assert!(certified_example(&root).is_err());
        std::fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn no_implicit_certification_or_invalid_pin() {
        assert!(parse(strings(&["build"]), Path::new("/tmp")).is_err());
        assert!(
            parse(
                strings(&["build", "--certified", "--pinned-sha256", "00"]),
                Path::new("/tmp")
            )
            .is_err()
        );
        assert!(
            parse(
                strings(&["verify", "--certified", "--pinned-sha256", "00"]),
                Path::new("/tmp")
            )
            .is_err()
        );
        let pin = "a".repeat(64);
        assert!(
            parse(
                vec![
                    "verify".into(),
                    "--certified".into(),
                    "--pinned-sha256".into(),
                    pin
                ],
                Path::new("/tmp")
            )
            .is_ok()
        );
    }
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/canonical.rs
//! Canonical, versioned serialization of Semantic Neural IR.
//!
//! This module is intentionally boring. The format is explicit and does not
//! depend on Rust `Debug`, so cosmetic struct changes do not silently rewrite
//! semantic fingerprints.

use std::fmt::Write as _;

use crate::{
    ContractClaim, FmaMode, GpuSemantics, ModuleInstanceRef, NeuralGraph, Operation, PortContract,
    Predicate, ReductionOrder, RoundingMode, Shape, SubnormalMode, ValueRef,
};

const FORMAT_VERSION: &str = "verineural-semantic-ir-v4";

fn escaped(value: &str) -> String {
    let mut out = String::new();
    for byte in value.as_bytes() {
        match *byte {
            b'A'..=b'Z' | b'a'..=b'z' | b'0'..=b'9' | b'-' | b'_' | b'.' => {
                out.push(char::from(*byte));
            }
            other => {
                write!(out, "%{other:02X}").expect("writing to String");
            }
        }
    }
    out
}

fn shape(shape: &Shape) -> String {
    if shape.dims().is_empty() {
        "scalar".to_owned()
    } else {
        shape
            .dims()
            .iter()
            .map(usize::to_string)
            .collect::<Vec<_>>()
            .join("x")
    }
}

fn operation(operation: &Operation) -> String {
    match operation {
        Operation::Reshape(output) => format!("reshape:{}", shape(output)),
        Operation::Pointwise(spec) => format!(
            "pointwise:{}@{}:arity={}:{}",
            escaped(spec.id()),
            escaped(spec.version()),
            spec.arity(),
            spec.expression().canonical()
        ),
        Operation::ReduceSum { axis } => format!("reduce_sum_axis:{axis}"),
        Operation::ReduceMax { axis } => format!("reduce_max_axis:{axis}"),
        Operation::BroadcastTo(output) => format!("broadcast_to:{}", shape(output)),
        Operation::Permute { axes } => format!(
            "permute_axes:{}",
            axes.iter()
                .map(usize::to_string)
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                .join(",")
        ),
        Operation::ReverseAxis { axis } => format!("reverse_axis:{axis}"),
        Operation::Concat { axis } => format!("concat_axis:{axis}"),
        Operation::SliceAxis { axis, start, len } => {
            format!("slice_axis:{axis}:start={start}:len={len}")
        }
        Operation::ArgMax { axis, tie_break } => {
            format!("argmax_axis:{axis}:tie={}", tie_break.name())
        }
        Operation::Take { axis } => format!("take_axis:{axis}"),
        other => other.name().to_owned(),
    }
}

fn policy(graph: &NeuralGraph) -> String {
    let policy = graph.policy();
    let rounding = match policy.rounding {
        RoundingMode::NearestTiesToEven => "nearest_ties_to_even",
    };
    let fma = match policy.fma {
        FmaMode::SeparateOperations => "separate_operations",
    };
    let subnormals = match policy.subnormals {
        SubnormalMode::Preserve => "preserve",
    };
    let reduction = match policy.reduction {
        ReductionOrder::LeftToRight => "left_to_right",
    };
    format!("rounding={rounding},fma={fma},subnormals={subnormals},reduction={reduction}")
}

fn nodes(ids: impl IntoIterator<Item = usize>) -> String {
    let text = ids
        .into_iter()
        .map(|id| id.to_string())
        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
        .join(",");
    if text.is_empty() {
        "-".to_owned()
    } else {
        text
    }
}

fn port(port: &PortContract) -> String {
    format!(
        "{}@{}@{}",
        shape(&port.shape),
        port.dtype.name(),
        port.domain.name()
    )
}

fn value_ref(value: &ValueRef) -> String {
    match value {
        ValueRef::Input(index) => format!("input:{index}"),
        ValueRef::Output => "output".to_owned(),
        ValueRef::Node(id) => format!("node:{}", id.index()),
    }
}

fn predicate(predicate: &Predicate) -> String {
    match predicate {
        Predicate::Nonnegative(value) => format!("nonnegative({})", value_ref(value)),
        Predicate::Equal(a, b) => format!("equal({},{})", value_ref(a), value_ref(b)),
        Predicate::PointwiseLe(a, b) => format!("pointwise_le({},{})", value_ref(a), value_ref(b)),
    }
}

fn claims(claims: &[ContractClaim]) -> String {
    let text = claims
        .iter()
        .map(|claim| match claim {
            ContractClaim::Nonnegative => "nonnegative".to_owned(),
            ContractClaim::EqualsInput(index) => format!("equals_input:{index}"),
            ContractClaim::Predicate(value) => predicate(value),
        })
        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
        .join("+");
    if text.is_empty() {
        "-".to_owned()
    } else {
        text
    }
}

fn ports(ports: impl IntoIterator<Item = String>) -> String {
    let text = ports.into_iter().collect::<Vec<_>>().join(",");
    if text.is_empty() {
        "-".to_owned()
    } else {
        text
    }
}

fn gpu_semantics(gpu: GpuSemantics) -> &'static str {
    match gpu {
        GpuSemantics::NotLowered => "not_lowered",
    }
}

pub(crate) fn graph_ir(graph: &NeuralGraph) -> String {
    let mut text = String::new();
    writeln!(text, "{FORMAT_VERSION}").expect("writing to String");
    writeln!(text, "policy={}", policy(graph)).expect("writing to String");

    for (index, node) in graph.nodes().iter().enumerate() {
        writeln!(
            text,
            "node={index};op={};inputs={};shape={};dtype={};domain={};storage={};requires={};ensures={};claims={};ideal={};gpu={}",
            operation(&node.operation),
            nodes(node.inputs.iter().map(|id| id.index())),
            shape(&node.shape),
            node.dtype.name(),
            node.domain.name(),
            graph
                .storage(node.id)
                .expect("canonical node belongs to graph")
                .describe(),
            ports(node.contract.requires.iter().map(port)),
            port(&node.contract.ensures),
            claims(&node.contract.claims),
            operation(&node.semantics.ideal),
            gpu_semantics(node.semantics.gpu),
        )
        .expect("writing to String");
    }

    for (sequence, module) in graph.module_instances().enumerate() {
        match module {
            ModuleInstanceRef::Single(module) => {
                writeln!(
                    text,
                    "module={sequence};kind=single;name={};version={};inputs={};body={}..{};outputs={};input_ports={};output_ports={}",
                    escaped(module.name),
                    escaped(module.semantic_version),
                    nodes(module.inputs.iter().map(|id| id.index())),
                    module.body_start,
                    module.body_end,
                    module.output.index(),
                    ports(module.contract.requires.iter().enumerate().map(|(index, port_contract)| {
                        format!("input_{index}:{}", port(port_contract))
                    })),
                    format_args!("output:{}!{}", port(&module.contract.ensures), claims(&module.contract.claims)),
                )
                .expect("writing to String");
            }
            ModuleInstanceRef::Multi(module) => {
                writeln!(
                    text,
                    "module={sequence};kind=multi;name={};version={};inputs={};body={}..{};outputs={};input_ports={};output_ports={}",
                    escaped(module.name),
                    escaped(module.semantic_version),
                    nodes(module.inputs.iter().map(|id| id.index())),
                    module.body_start,
                    module.body_end,
                    nodes(module.outputs.iter().map(|id| id.index())),
                    ports(module.inputs.iter().zip(&module.contract.inputs).map(|(id, named)| {
                        format!("{}:{}:{}", escaped(named.name), id.index(), port(&named.port))
                    })),
                    ports(module.outputs.iter().zip(&module.contract.outputs).map(|(id, named)| {
                        format!(
                            "{}:{}:{}!{}",
                            escaped(named.name),
                            id.index(),
                            port(&named.port),
                            claims(&named.claims)
                        )
                    })),
                )
                .expect("writing to String");
            }
        }
    }

    text
}

impl NeuralGraph {
    /// Stable Semantic Neural IR serialization used by every artifact writer.
    /// Graph identity, Rust `Debug` formatting and artifact paths are excluded.
    pub fn canonical_ir(&self) -> String {
        graph_ir(self)
    }
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/certificate.rs
//! Stage 5: one evidence bundle for a concrete IR/Lean/PTX/GPU run.
//!
//! This is an *integrity-checked validation report*, not a proof that PTX,
//! JIT-generated machine code or IEEE-754 behavior preserves the Lean model.

use std::error::Error;
use std::fmt;
use std::fs;
use std::io;
use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
use std::process::Command;

use crate::{GpuEngine, GpuError, LeanProofEngine, NeuralGraph, NodeId, ProofError, Tensor};

const ARTIFACTS: [&str; 7] = [
    "graph.ir",
    "proof.lean",
    "graph.ll",
    "graph.ptx",
    "inputs.bits",
    "output.bits",
    "report.json",
];
const MANIFEST: &str = "SHA256SUMS";

/// These labels describe distinct evidence levels, not a single certification grade.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum EvidenceStatus {
    Proven,
    Validated,
    Trusted,
    Unsupported,
}

impl EvidenceStatus {
    pub const fn as_str(self) -> &'static str {
        match self {
            Self::Proven => "proven",
            Self::Validated => "validated",
            Self::Trusted => "trusted",
            Self::Unsupported => "unsupported",
        }
    }
}

#[derive(Debug)]
pub enum CertificateError {
    Proof(ProofError),
    Gpu(GpuError),
    Io(io::Error),
    WrongOutputShape,
    NumericalMismatch {
        index: usize,
        gpu_bits: u32,
        cpu_bits: u32,
    },
    HashTool(String),
    Integrity(String),
}

impl fmt::Display for CertificateError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        match self {
            Self::Proof(err) => write!(f, "proof step failed: {err}"),
            Self::Gpu(err) => write!(f, "GPU step failed: {err}"),
            Self::Io(err) => write!(f, "certificate I/O failed: {err}"),
            Self::WrongOutputShape => write!(f, "GPU and CPU output shapes differ"),
            Self::NumericalMismatch {
                index,
                gpu_bits,
                cpu_bits,
            } => write!(
                f,
                "FP32 mismatch at {index}: GPU={gpu_bits:08x}, CPU={cpu_bits:08x}"
            ),
            Self::HashTool(message) => write!(f, "sha256sum failed: {message}"),
            Self::Integrity(message) => write!(f, "bundle integrity failure: {message}"),
        }
    }
}

impl Error for CertificateError {}

impl From<ProofError> for CertificateError {
    fn from(value: ProofError) -> Self {
        Self::Proof(value)
    }
}

impl From<GpuError> for CertificateError {
    fn from(value: GpuError) -> Self {
        Self::Gpu(value)
    }
}

impl From<io::Error> for CertificateError {
    fn from(value: io::Error) -> Self {
        Self::Io(value)
    }
}

/// Successful validation with a SHA-256 digest that can be pinned externally.
/// Neither this structure nor the on-disk JSON is a signed certificate.
#[derive(Debug)]
pub struct Stage5Report {
    pub directory: PathBuf,
    pub manifest_sha256: String,
    pub theorem_count: usize,
    pub compared_fp32_values: usize,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)]
pub struct CertificateEngine {
    proof: LeanProofEngine,
    gpu: GpuEngine,
}

impl CertificateEngine {
    pub fn new(proof: LeanProofEngine, gpu: GpuEngine) -> Self {
        Self { proof, gpu }
    }

    /// Fail closed: old report and manifest are removed *before* any checking.
    ///
    /// The caller supplies a separately computed Rust f32 reference. Its
    /// correctness is trusted, not proven. A bitwise comparison is evidence
    /// for these specific input values only.
    pub fn run(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        output: NodeId,
        inputs: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)],
        cpu_reference: &Tensor<f32>,
        directory: &Path,
    ) -> Result<Stage5Report, CertificateError> {
        fs::create_dir_all(directory)?;
        for name in ["report.json", MANIFEST] {
            match fs::remove_file(directory.join(name)) {
                Ok(()) => {}
                Err(err) if err.kind() == io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {}
                Err(err) => return Err(err.into()),
            }
        }

        let result: Result<Stage5Report, CertificateError> = (|| {
            let model = self.proof.generate(graph, output)?;
            let (checked, audit) = self
                .proof
                .verify_certified(&model, &directory.join("proof.lean"))?;
            let program = self.gpu.compile(graph, output)?;
            let actual = self.gpu.execute(&program, inputs, directory)?;
            if actual.shape() != cpu_reference.shape() {
                return Err(CertificateError::WrongOutputShape);
            }
            for (index, (&gpu, &cpu)) in actual
                .values()
                .iter()
                .zip(cpu_reference.values())
                .enumerate()
            {
                if gpu.to_bits() != cpu.to_bits() {
                    return Err(CertificateError::NumericalMismatch {
                        index,
                        gpu_bits: gpu.to_bits(),
                        cpu_bits: cpu.to_bits(),
                    });
                }
            }

            fs::write(directory.join("graph.ir"), ir_snapshot(graph, output))?;
            fs::write(directory.join("inputs.bits"), input_snapshot(graph, inputs))?;
            fs::write(
                directory.join("output.bits"),
                actual
                    .values()
                    .iter()
                    .zip(cpu_reference.values())
                    .enumerate()
                    .map(|(i, (gpu, cpu))| {
                        format!("{i} gpu={:08x} cpu={:08x}\n", gpu.to_bits(), cpu.to_bits())
                    })
                    .collect::<String>(),
            )?;

            let hashes = ARTIFACTS[..ARTIFACTS.len() - 1]
                .iter()
                .map(|name| Ok((*name, hash_file(&directory.join(name))?)))
                .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, CertificateError>>()?;
            let theorem_names = checked
                .theorem_names
                .iter()
                .map(|name| format!("\"{}\"", escape_json(name)))
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                .join(", ");
            let hypotheses = checked
                .assumptions
                .iter()
                .map(|a| {
                    format!(
                        "{{\"input_node\":{},\"domain\":\"{:?}\"}}",
                        a.input_node, a.domain
                    )
                })
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                .join(", ");
            let input_domains = program
                .source_inputs()
                .iter()
                .map(|&id| {
                    let node = &graph.nodes()[id.index()];
                    format!(
                        "{{\"node\":{},\"shape\":{:?},\"domain\":\"{:?}\"}}",
                        id.index(),
                        node.shape.dims(),
                        node.domain
                    )
                })
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                .join(", ");
            let artifacts = hashes
                .iter()
                .map(|(name, hash)| format!("{{\"path\":\"{name}\",\"sha256\":\"{hash}\"}}"))
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                .join(",\n    ");
            let report = format!(
                concat!(
                    "{{\n",
                    "  \"schema\": \"verineural.stage5.v1\",\n",
                    "  \"output_node\": {},\n",
                    "  \"statuses\": {{\"mathematical\":\"{}\",\"composition\":\"{}\",",
                    "\"numerical\":\"{}\",\"gpu_execution\":\"{}\",",
                    "\"compilation\":\"{}\",\"fp32_semantics\":\"{}\",",
                    "\"machine_code_correctness\":\"{}\"}},\n",
                    "  \"proven_scope\": \"Lean 4 ideal Int model: shapes, per-node definitions, and applicable nonnegativity/module obligations only\",\n",
                    "  \"numerical_scope\": \"bitwise CPU/GPU equality for the recorded concrete f32 inputs only\",\n",
                    "  \"compilation_scope\": \"LLVM NVPTX/PTX generated and run; semantic preservation is trusted, not proved; experimental fusion is not FP32-certified\",\n",
                    "  \"certified_machine_code\": false,\n",
                    "  \"gpu_launch\": {{\"execution\":\"cuda_graph_capture_nonblocking_stream\",\"threads_per_block\":{},\"relu_fusion\":\"{}\",\"applied_fusions\":{}}},\n",
                    "  \"theorems\": [{}],\n",
                    "  \"lean_hypotheses\": [{}],\n",
                    "  \"lean_checker_version\": \"{}\",\n",
                    "  \"lean_axiom_policy\": [\"propext\"],\n",
                    "  \"lean_axiom_dependencies\": {{{}}},\n",
                    "  \"declared_input_domains\": [{}],\n",
                    "  \"compared_fp32_values\": {},\n",
                    "  \"artifacts\": [\n    {}\n  ],\n",
                    "  \"tcb\": [\"Rust graph and certificate serializer\",",
                    "\"Lean model generator\", \"Lean 4 executable and kernel\",",
                    "\"LLVM llc NVPTX compiler\", \"CUDA driver/JIT/runtime\",",
                    "\"NVIDIA hardware\", \"Rust f32 CPU reference\",",
                    "\"coreutils sha256sum\"],\n",
                    "  \"limitations\": [\"Hashes detect changes relative to a pinned digest; they do not authenticate the author\",",
                    "\"Lean integer semantics is not linked by proof to GPU floating-point behavior\",",
                    "\"Input domain declarations are caller assumptions checked for the concrete GPU inputs\",",
                    "\"No verified GPU memory, compiler correctness, IEEE-754 or numerical error bound\"]\n",
                    "}}\n"
                ),
                output.index(),
                EvidenceStatus::Proven.as_str(),
                EvidenceStatus::Proven.as_str(),
                EvidenceStatus::Validated.as_str(),
                EvidenceStatus::Validated.as_str(),
                EvidenceStatus::Trusted.as_str(),
                EvidenceStatus::Unsupported.as_str(),
                EvidenceStatus::Unsupported.as_str(),
                program.launch_config().threads_per_block(),
                program.launch_config().relu_fusion().as_str(),
                program.fused_relus().len(),
                theorem_names,
                hypotheses,
                escape_json(&audit.lean_version),
                axiom_dependencies_json(&audit),
                input_domains,
                actual.values().len(),
                artifacts,
            );
            fs::write(directory.join("report.json"), report)?;
            fs::write(directory.join(MANIFEST), manifest_contents(directory)?)?;
            self.verify_bundle(directory)?;
            Ok(Stage5Report {
                directory: directory.to_path_buf(),
                manifest_sha256: hash_file(&directory.join(MANIFEST))?,
                theorem_count: checked.theorem_names.len(),
                compared_fp32_values: actual.values().len(),
            })
        })();
        if result.is_err() {
            // A partially written report must never survive any failed run.
            for name in ["report.json", MANIFEST] {
                let _ = fs::remove_file(directory.join(name));
            }
        }
        result
    }

    /// Verify the report against a SHA256SUMS digest pinned outside the bundle.
    pub fn verify_bundle_with_digest(
        &self,
        directory: &Path,
        pinned_sha256: &str,
    ) -> Result<(), CertificateError> {
        let actual = hash_file(&directory.join(MANIFEST))?;
        if actual != pinned_sha256 {
            return Err(CertificateError::Integrity(
                "pinned SHA256SUMS digest mismatch".into(),
            ));
        }
        self.verify_bundle(directory)
    }

    /// Recompute all bundled hashes and rerun the trusted Lean checker.
    ///
    /// This confirms integrity relative to SHA256SUMS and Lean acceptance,
    /// NOT authenticity of SHA256SUMS itself or GPU semantic correctness.
    /// Pin the printed digest of SHA256SUMS outside the bundle.
    pub fn verify_bundle(&self, directory: &Path) -> Result<(), CertificateError> {
        let on_disk = fs::read_to_string(directory.join(MANIFEST))?;
        let expected = manifest_contents(directory)?;
        if on_disk != expected {
            return Err(CertificateError::Integrity(
                "SHA256SUMS differs from one or more artifacts".into(),
            ));
        }
        let source_file = directory.join("proof.lean");
        self.proof.check_file(&source_file)?;
        let lean = fs::read_to_string(&source_file)?;
        let generated = lean
            .split_once("namespace VeriNeural.Generated")
            .map(|(_, tail)| tail)
            .ok_or_else(|| {
                CertificateError::Integrity("missing generated Lean namespace".into())
            })?;
        let names = generated
            .lines()
            .filter_map(|line| {
                line.trim_start()
                    .strip_prefix("theorem ")
                    .and_then(|line| line.split_whitespace().next())
                    .map(ToOwned::to_owned)
            })
            .collect::<Vec<_>>();
        let audit = self.proof.audit_file(&source_file, &names)?;
        let report = fs::read_to_string(directory.join("report.json"))?;
        let version = format!(
            "\"lean_checker_version\": \"{}\"",
            escape_json(&audit.lean_version)
        );
        let policy = "\"lean_axiom_policy\": [\"propext\"]";
        let dependencies = format!(
            "\"lean_axiom_dependencies\": {{{}}}",
            axiom_dependencies_json(&audit)
        );
        if report.matches(&version).count() != 1
            || report.matches(policy).count() != 1
            || report.matches(&dependencies).count() != 1
        {
            return Err(CertificateError::Integrity(
                "saved Lean version, axiom policy or dependencies disagree with audited proof"
                    .into(),
            ));
        }
        Ok(())
    }
}

/// Certificate selection layered over the one canonical graph serialization.
/// Graph identity and process-global IDs do not contribute to the fingerprint.
fn ir_snapshot(graph: &NeuralGraph, output: NodeId) -> String {
    format!(
        "{}certificate_output={}\n",
        graph.canonical_ir(),
        output.index()
    )
}

fn input_snapshot(graph: &NeuralGraph, inputs: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)]) -> String {
    let mut ordered = inputs.iter().collect::<Vec<_>>();
    ordered.sort_by_key(|(id, _)| id.index());
    let mut text = String::from("verineural-inputs-f32-bits-v1\n");
    for (id, value) in ordered {
        text.push_str(&format!(
            "node={};declared_domain={:?};shape={:?};bits=",
            id.index(),
            graph.nodes()[id.index()].domain,
            value.shape().dims()
        ));
        for bits in value.values() {
            text.push_str(&format!("{:08x},", bits.to_bits()));
        }
        text.push('\n');
    }
    text
}

fn axiom_dependencies_json(audit: &crate::LeanAxiomAudit) -> String {
    audit
        .axiom_dependencies
        .iter()
        .map(|(theorem, axioms)| {
            let values = axioms
                .iter()
                .map(|axiom| format!("\"{}\"", escape_json(axiom)))
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                .join(", ");
            format!("\"{}\": [{}]", escape_json(theorem), values)
        })
        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
        .join(", ")
}

fn escape_json(value: &str) -> String {
    let mut out = String::new();
    for c in value.chars() {
        match c {
            '"' => out.push_str("\\\""),
            '\\' => out.push_str("\\\\"),
            '\n' => out.push_str("\\n"),
            '\r' => out.push_str("\\r"),
            '\t' => out.push_str("\\t"),
            c if c.is_control() => out.push_str(&format!("\\u{:04x}", c as u32)),
            c => out.push(c),
        }
    }
    out
}

pub(crate) fn hash_file(path: &Path) -> Result<String, CertificateError> {
    let output = Command::new("sha256sum").arg(path).output()?;
    if !output.status.success() {
        return Err(CertificateError::HashTool(
            String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stderr).to_string(),
        ));
    }
    let text = String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout);
    let digest = text.split_whitespace().next().unwrap_or("");
    if digest.len() != 64 || !digest.bytes().all(|b| b.is_ascii_hexdigit()) {
        return Err(CertificateError::HashTool("invalid SHA-256 digest".into()));
    }
    Ok(digest.to_owned())
}

fn manifest_contents(directory: &Path) -> Result<String, CertificateError> {
    let lines = ARTIFACTS
        .iter()
        .map(|name| Ok(format!("{}  {}\n", hash_file(&directory.join(name))?, name)))
        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, CertificateError>>()?;
    Ok(lines.concat())
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use crate::{Domain, Shape};

    #[test]
    fn snapshots_ignore_process_graph_ids() {
        let make = || {
            let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
            let input = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
            let output = graph.relu(input).unwrap();
            (graph, output)
        };
        let (a, a_out) = make();
        let (b, b_out) = make();
        assert_eq!(ir_snapshot(&a, a_out), ir_snapshot(&b, b_out));
    }

    #[test]
    fn statuses_do_not_equate_validation_with_proof() {
        assert_eq!(EvidenceStatus::Proven.as_str(), "proven");
        assert_eq!(EvidenceStatus::Validated.as_str(), "validated");
        assert_eq!(EvidenceStatus::Trusted.as_str(), "trusted");
        assert_eq!(EvidenceStatus::Unsupported.as_str(), "unsupported");
        assert_eq!(escape_json("a\"b\n"), "a\\\"b\\n");
    }

    #[test]
    fn tampering_with_bundled_artifact_is_rejected_before_lean() {
        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("verineural-stage5-{}", std::process::id()));
        fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();
        for name in ARTIFACTS {
            fs::write(dir.join(name), name).unwrap();
        }
        fs::write(dir.join(MANIFEST), manifest_contents(&dir).unwrap()).unwrap();
        fs::write(dir.join("graph.ptx"), "modified").unwrap();
        let engine = CertificateEngine::new(LeanProofEngine::new("false"), GpuEngine::default());
        assert!(matches!(
            engine.verify_bundle(&dir),
            Err(CertificateError::Integrity(_))
        ));
        fs::remove_dir_all(dir).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn unsupported_proof_clears_stale_success_report() {
        let dir =
            std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("verineural-stage5-fail-{}", std::process::id()));
        fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();
        fs::write(dir.join("report.json"), "stale").unwrap();
        fs::write(dir.join(MANIFEST), "stale").unwrap();
        let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
        let input = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![1]).unwrap(), Domain::NonNegativeFinite);
        let output = graph.sqrt(input).unwrap();
        let expected = Tensor::new(Shape::new(vec![1]).unwrap(), vec![1.0]).unwrap();
        let result = CertificateEngine::default().run(&graph, output, &[], &expected, &dir);
        assert!(matches!(result, Err(CertificateError::Proof(_))));
        assert!(!dir.join("report.json").exists());
        assert!(!dir.join(MANIFEST).exists());
        fs::remove_dir_all(dir).unwrap();
    }
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/certified.rs
//! One proof-gated entry point for finished models. The existing auto-builder
//! owns Lean checking, Graphviz rendering, GPU translation and SHA256SUMS.
//! These are proofs about ideal-Int math and structural translation, NOT
//! formal proofs about FP32 GPU/SASS execution.
use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};

/// A selected Cargo package root owns its own certified evidence directory.
/// Relative overrides are resolved against this package, never the process CWD.
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct CertifiedBuildConfig {
    package_root: PathBuf,
    artifact_root: Option<PathBuf>,
}

impl CertifiedBuildConfig {
    pub fn new(package_root: impl Into<PathBuf>) -> Self {
        Self {
            package_root: package_root.into(),
            artifact_root: None,
        }
    }

    pub fn artifact_root(mut self, root: impl Into<PathBuf>) -> Self {
        self.artifact_root = Some(root.into());
        self
    }

    /// Proof goals are always mandatory. There is no weaker certified mode.
    pub fn require_all_proofs(self) -> Self {
        self
    }

    /// GPU support is required for every declared output in certified builds.
    pub fn require_gpu_lowering(self) -> Self {
        self
    }

    pub fn resolved_root(&self) -> PathBuf {
        match &self.artifact_root {
            None => self.package_root.clone(),
            Some(path) if path.is_absolute() => path.clone(),
            Some(path) => self.package_root.join(path),
        }
    }

    pub fn package_root(&self) -> &Path {
        &self.package_root
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn custom_roots_are_resolved_only_relative_to_the_package() {
        let package = Path::new("labs/model-0.1.0");
        assert_eq!(CertifiedBuildConfig::new(package).resolved_root(), package);
        assert_eq!(
            CertifiedBuildConfig::new(package)
                .artifact_root("generated/run1")
                .resolved_root(),
            package.join("generated/run1")
        );
        assert_eq!(
            CertifiedBuildConfig::new(package)
                .artifact_root("/tmp/model-run1")
                .resolved_root(),
            Path::new("/tmp/model-run1")
        );
    }
}

/// Human-facing artifact paths point to the single audited auto-build bundle.
/// Previous same-id/version lab snapshots are preserved when first migrated.
const ROOT_LINKS: [(&str, &str); 7] = [
    ("semantic.ir", "auto-build/semantic.ir"),
    ("architecture.dot", "auto-build/architecture.dot"),
    ("architecture.png", "auto-build/architecture.png"),
    ("architecture.lean", "auto-build/lean/architecture.lean"),
    ("SHA256SUMS", "auto-build/SHA256SUMS"),
    ("report.txt", "auto-build/report.txt"),
    ("identity.txt", "auto-build/identity.txt"),
];

fn root_identity(identity: &str) -> Result<(&str, &str), crate::AutoBuildError> {
    let id = identity.lines().find_map(|s| s.strip_prefix("id="));
    let version = identity.lines().find_map(|s| s.strip_prefix("version="));
    match (id, version) {
        (Some(id), Some(version)) => Ok((id, version)),
        _ => Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(
            "model identity lacks id/version".into(),
        )),
    }
}

pub(crate) fn preflight_root(root: &Path, identity: &str) -> Result<(), crate::AutoBuildError> {
    let (id, version) = root_identity(identity)?;
    let legacy_identity = root.join("architecture.identity");
    let legacy_ok = if legacy_identity.is_file() {
        std::fs::read_to_string(&legacy_identity)? == format!("id={id}\nversion={version}\n")
    } else {
        false
    };
    for (name, target) in ROOT_LINKS {
        let path = root.join(name);
        match std::fs::symlink_metadata(&path) {
            Ok(meta) if meta.file_type().is_symlink() => {
                if std::fs::read_link(&path)? != Path::new(target) {
                    return Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
                        "unexpected external artifact symlink: {}",
                        path.display()
                    )));
                }
            }
            Ok(meta) if meta.is_file() && legacy_ok => {
                let backup = root.join(".verineural-pre-stage10");
                if let Ok(backup_meta) = std::fs::symlink_metadata(&backup) {
                    if !backup_meta.is_dir() || backup_meta.file_type().is_symlink() {
                        return Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                            "legacy backup must be a real directory".into(),
                        ));
                    }
                }
                if std::fs::symlink_metadata(backup.join(name)).is_ok() {
                    return Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
                        "legacy backup already exists; refusing partial migration of {name}"
                    )));
                }
            }
            Ok(_) => {
                return Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
                    "refusing to replace unowned artifact: {}",
                    path.display()
                )));
            }
            Err(err) if err.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {}
            Err(err) => return Err(err.into()),
        }
    }
    Ok(())
}

/// A stable set of relative links names one underlying bundle. Root link
/// changes cannot be one atomic filesystem operation, but an unsuccessful
/// first migration must leave no partially installed links or moved files.
#[cfg(unix)]
fn publish_root_transaction(
    root: &Path,
    identity: &str,
    // Test-only fault boundary: inject an error after a fixed number of edits.
    interrupt_after: Option<usize>,
) -> Result<(), crate::AutoBuildError> {
    use std::os::unix::fs::symlink;

    preflight_root(root, identity)?;
    let backup = root.join(".verineural-pre-stage10");
    // (root name, whether an original regular file was moved, whether our
    // symlink was installed). Only ever undo our own changes.
    let mut updated: Vec<(&str, bool, bool)> = Vec::new();
    let outcome = (|| -> Result<(), crate::AutoBuildError> {
        for (name, target) in ROOT_LINKS {
            let path = root.join(name);
            match std::fs::symlink_metadata(&path) {
                Ok(meta) if meta.file_type().is_symlink() => continue,
                Ok(meta) if meta.is_file() => {
                    if interrupt_after == Some(updated.len()) {
                        return Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                            "interrupted root artifact migration".into(),
                        ));
                    }
                    std::fs::create_dir_all(&backup)?;
                    std::fs::rename(&path, backup.join(name))?;
                    updated.push((name, true, false));
                }
                Err(error) if error.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {
                    if interrupt_after == Some(updated.len()) {
                        return Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(
                            "interrupted root artifact migration".into(),
                        ));
                    }
                    updated.push((name, false, false));
                }
                Ok(_) => {
                    return Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
                        "root artifact changed during publication: {}",
                        path.display()
                    )));
                }
                Err(error) => return Err(error.into()),
            }
            symlink(target, &path)?;
            if let Some(last) = updated.last_mut() {
                last.2 = true;
            }
        }
        Ok(())
    })();

    if let Err(error) = outcome {
        let mut rollback_error = None;
        for (name, old_file, installed) in updated.into_iter().rev() {
            let path = root.join(name);
            if installed {
                if let Err(err) = std::fs::remove_file(&path) {
                    rollback_error.get_or_insert(err);
                    continue;
                }
            }
            if old_file {
                if let Err(err) = std::fs::rename(backup.join(name), &path) {
                    rollback_error.get_or_insert(err);
                }
            }
        }
        return if let Some(rollback_error) = rollback_error {
            Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
                "root publication failed ({error}); rollback also failed ({rollback_error})"
            )))
        } else {
            Err(error)
        };
    }
    Ok(())
}

#[cfg(unix)]
pub(crate) fn publish_root(root: &Path, identity: &str) -> Result<(), crate::AutoBuildError> {
    publish_root_transaction(root, identity, None)
}

#[cfg(not(unix))]
pub(crate) fn publish_root(_root: &Path, _identity: &str) -> Result<(), crate::AutoBuildError> {
    Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(
        "Stage 10 root-level bundle links require Unix symlink support".into(),
    ))
}

pub(crate) fn verify_root(root: &Path, identity: &str) -> Result<(), crate::AutoBuildError> {
    preflight_root(root, identity)?;
    for (name, target) in ROOT_LINKS {
        let path = root.join(name);
        if std::fs::read_link(&path).ok().as_deref() != Some(Path::new(target)) {
            return Err(crate::AutoBuildError::Integrity(format!(
                "missing or replaced certified root link: {}",
                path.display()
            )));
        }
    }
    Ok(())
}

/// Shared Cargo example entry point for any consumer-defined model.
///
/// Architecture definitions belong in the consumer's src/lib.rs. An example
/// can call this function without implementing proof orchestration or CLI
/// parsing a second time.
pub fn certified_example_main(
    model: &crate::Model,
    package_root: impl Into<PathBuf>,
) -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let mut args = std::env::args().skip(1);
    let mut verify = false;
    let mut root: Option<PathBuf> = None;
    let mut pin: Option<String> = None;
    while let Some(arg) = args.next() {
        match arg.as_str() {
            "--verify" if !verify => verify = true,
            "--artifact-root" if root.is_none() => {
                root = Some(args.next().ok_or("--artifact-root requires a path")?.into());
            }
            "--pinned-sha256" if pin.is_none() => {
                let digest = args.next().ok_or("--pinned-sha256 requires a digest")?;
                if digest.len() != 64 || !digest.bytes().all(|c| c.is_ascii_hexdigit()) {
                    return Err("--pinned-sha256 requires exactly 64 hexadecimal characters".into());
                }
                pin = Some(digest);
            }
            _ => return Err(format!("unknown or repeated certified option: {arg}").into()),
        }
    }
    if pin.is_some() && !verify {
        return Err("--pinned-sha256 only applies to --verify".into());
    }
    let mut config = CertifiedBuildConfig::new(package_root)
        .require_all_proofs()
        .require_gpu_lowering();
    if let Some(root) = root {
        config = config.artifact_root(root);
    }
    let report = if verify {
        model.verify_certified(config, pin.as_deref())?
    } else {
        model.certify(config)?
    };
    println!(
        "{}",
        if verify {
            "Certified replay passed"
        } else {
            "Certified build published"
        }
    );
    println!("Evidence: {}", report.directory.display());
    println!("Lean checker: {}", report.lean_version);
    println!("Mandatory goals verified: {}", report.goal_theorems.len());
    println!("SHA256SUMS: {} (pin externally)", report.manifest_sha256);
    println!(
        "Assurance: Lean ideal-Int proofs and GPU structural translation; NOT FP32/SASS machine proof"
    );
    Ok(())
}

#[cfg(all(test, unix))]
mod root_tests {
    use super::*;
    use std::os::unix::fs::symlink;

    fn test_root(label: &str) -> PathBuf {
        std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "verineural-root-{label}-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ))
    }

    #[test]
    fn only_same_identity_legacy_artifacts_can_be_migrated() {
        let root = test_root("migration");
        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
        std::fs::write(root.join("architecture.identity"), "id=lab\nversion=1\n").unwrap();
        std::fs::write(root.join("architecture.dot"), "legacy dot").unwrap();
        let identity = "verineural-certified-model-v1\nid=lab\nversion=1\n";
        preflight_root(&root, identity).unwrap();
        assert!(
            preflight_root(
                &root,
                "verineural-certified-model-v1\nid=foreign\nversion=1\n"
            )
            .is_err()
        );
        publish_root(&root, identity).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(
            std::fs::read_link(root.join("architecture.dot")).unwrap(),
            Path::new("auto-build/architecture.dot")
        );
        assert_eq!(
            std::fs::read_to_string(root.join(".verineural-pre-stage10/architecture.dot")).unwrap(),
            "legacy dot"
        );
        verify_root(&root, identity).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn migration_fails_before_mutation_if_a_backup_conflicts() {
        let root = test_root("backup-conflict");
        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(".verineural-pre-stage10")).unwrap();
        std::fs::write(root.join("architecture.identity"), "id=lab\nversion=1\n").unwrap();
        std::fs::write(root.join("architecture.dot"), "original").unwrap();
        std::fs::write(root.join("architecture.png"), "original png").unwrap();
        std::fs::write(
            root.join(".verineural-pre-stage10/architecture.png"),
            "previous",
        )
        .unwrap();
        let identity = "verineural-certified-model-v1\nid=lab\nversion=1\n";
        assert!(publish_root(&root, identity).is_err());
        assert_eq!(
            std::fs::read_to_string(root.join("architecture.dot")).unwrap(),
            "original"
        );
        assert_eq!(
            std::fs::read_to_string(root.join("architecture.png")).unwrap(),
            "original png"
        );
        std::fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn interrupted_legacy_migration_restores_every_original_file() {
        let root = test_root("rollback-legacy");
        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
        std::fs::write(root.join("architecture.identity"), "id=lab\nversion=1\n").unwrap();
        std::fs::write(root.join("architecture.dot"), "old dot").unwrap();
        std::fs::write(root.join("architecture.png"), "old png").unwrap();
        let identity = "verineural-certified-model-v1\nid=lab\nversion=1\n";
        assert!(publish_root_transaction(&root, identity, Some(2)).is_err());
        assert_eq!(
            std::fs::read_to_string(root.join("architecture.dot")).unwrap(),
            "old dot"
        );
        assert_eq!(
            std::fs::read_to_string(root.join("architecture.png")).unwrap(),
            "old png"
        );
        assert!(!root.join("semantic.ir").exists());
        assert!(
            !root
                .join(".verineural-pre-stage10/architecture.dot")
                .exists()
        );
        publish_root(&root, identity).unwrap();
        verify_root(&root, identity).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn interrupted_fresh_publication_clears_all_new_links() {
        let root = test_root("rollback-fresh");
        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
        let identity = "verineural-certified-model-v1\nid=lab\nversion=1\n";
        assert!(publish_root_transaction(&root, identity, Some(3)).is_err());
        for (name, _) in ROOT_LINKS {
            assert!(std::fs::symlink_metadata(root.join(name)).is_err());
        }
        publish_root(&root, identity).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn reject_external_root_link_and_unowned_file() {
        let root = test_root("rogue");
        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&root).unwrap();
        let identity = "verineural-certified-model-v1\nid=lab\nversion=1\n";
        std::fs::write(root.join("semantic.ir"), "other").unwrap();
        assert!(preflight_root(&root, identity).is_err());
        std::fs::remove_file(root.join("semantic.ir")).unwrap();
        symlink("/tmp/outside/ir", root.join("semantic.ir")).unwrap();
        assert!(preflight_root(&root, identity).is_err());
        std::fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
    }
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/consumer.rs
//! Small consumer-facing binding/obligation helpers. The Semantic IR,
//! module contracts and Lean proof engine remain the only sources of truth.
use std::error::Error;
use std::fmt;
use std::path::Path;

use crate::{
    CheckedLean, FixedScan, LeanAxiomAudit, LeanProgram, LeanProofEngine, MathContract,
    MultiOutputModule, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NeuralModule, NodeId, PortContract, Predicate,
    ProofError, ProofGoal, ProofGoalKind, ValueRef,
};

/// A structured error at a caller-owned component path and named port.
/// The underlying shape, domain or contract error is preserved, not translated
/// into an allegedly verified mathematical claim.
#[derive(Debug)]
pub struct BindingError {
    pub component_path: String,
    pub port: String,
    pub constraint: String,
    pub source: Option<NeuralError>,
}

impl fmt::Display for BindingError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        write!(
            f,
            "component {} port {}: {}",
            self.component_path, self.port, self.constraint
        )?;
        if let Some(source) = &self.source {
            write!(f, ": {source}")?;
        }
        Ok(())
    }
}

impl Error for BindingError {
    fn source(&self) -> Option<&(dyn Error + 'static)> {
        self.source.as_ref().map(|source| source as &dyn Error)
    }
}

/// A proof failure is associated with the explicitly requested theorem.
/// A generated theorem is not a checked theorem.
#[derive(Debug)]
pub struct ObligationError {
    pub theorem: String,
    pub source: ProofError,
}

impl fmt::Display for ObligationError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        write!(f, "proof obligation {}: {}", self.theorem, self.source)
    }
}

impl Error for ObligationError {
    fn source(&self) -> Option<&(dyn Error + 'static)> {
        Some(&self.source)
    }
}

/// Lightweight facade over the existing atomic module insertion/rollback.
pub struct ComponentBinder<'a> {
    graph: &'a mut NeuralGraph,
    path: String,
}

impl NeuralGraph {
    /// Label subsequent module calls without duplicating the graph or contracts.
    pub fn component(&mut self, path: impl Into<String>) -> ComponentBinder<'_> {
        ComponentBinder {
            graph: self,
            path: path.into(),
        }
    }
}

impl ComponentBinder<'_> {
    fn failed(
        &self,
        port: impl Into<String>,
        constraint: impl Into<String>,
        source: Option<NeuralError>,
    ) -> BindingError {
        BindingError {
            component_path: self.path.clone(),
            port: port.into(),
            constraint: constraint.into(),
            source,
        }
    }

    fn check_input(
        &self,
        id: NodeId,
        name: &str,
        required: &PortContract,
    ) -> Result<(), BindingError> {
        let actual = self.graph.node(id).map_err(|error| {
            self.failed(name, "input must belong to the current graph", Some(error))
        })?;
        if actual.shape != required.shape {
            return Err(self.failed(
                name,
                "input shape",
                Some(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                    expected: required.shape.clone(),
                    actual: actual.shape.clone(),
                }),
            ));
        }
        if actual.dtype != required.dtype {
            return Err(self.failed(
                name,
                "input dtype",
                Some(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                    operation: "component_input",
                    expected: required.dtype,
                    actual: actual.dtype,
                }),
            ));
        }
        if !actual.domain.satisfies(required.domain) {
            return Err(self.failed(
                name,
                "input value domain",
                Some(NeuralError::DomainNotEstablished {
                    required: required.domain,
                    actual: actual.domain,
                }),
            ));
        }
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Invoke one existing single-output module with positional ports.
    /// Port names in diagnostics are stable input_0, input_1, etc.
    pub fn single<M: NeuralModule>(
        &mut self,
        module: &M,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<NodeId, BindingError> {
        let contract: &MathContract = module.contract();
        if inputs.len() != contract.requires.len() {
            return Err(self.failed(
                "inputs",
                format!(
                    "expected {} inputs, received {}",
                    contract.requires.len(),
                    inputs.len()
                ),
                None,
            ));
        }
        for (index, (&id, required)) in inputs.iter().zip(&contract.requires).enumerate() {
            self.check_input(id, &format!("input_{index}"), required)?;
        }
        self.graph.apply_module(module, inputs).map_err(|source| {
            self.failed(
                "output",
                format!("{} postcondition or body", module.name()),
                Some(source),
            )
        })
    }

    /// Bind named input ports in arbitrary caller order. Reject missing,
    /// duplicate and unexpected bindings before mutating the graph.
    pub fn multi<M: MultiOutputModule>(
        &mut self,
        module: &M,
        bindings: &[(&str, NodeId)],
    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, BindingError> {
        let ports = &module.contract().inputs;
        let mut ordered = Vec::with_capacity(ports.len());
        for required in ports {
            let mut found = None;
            for &(name, id) in bindings {
                if name == required.name && found.replace(id).is_some() {
                    return Err(self.failed(name, "duplicate port binding", None));
                }
            }
            let id = found
                .ok_or_else(|| self.failed(required.name, "missing required port binding", None))?;
            self.check_input(id, required.name, &required.port)?;
            ordered.push(id);
        }
        for &(name, _) in bindings {
            if !ports.iter().any(|port| port.name == name) {
                return Err(self.failed(name, "unexpected port binding", None));
            }
        }
        self.graph
            .apply_multi_module(module, &ordered)
            .map_err(|source| {
                self.failed(
                    "outputs",
                    format!("{} output postconditions or body", module.name()),
                    Some(source),
                )
            })
    }

    /// Resolve results by their declared names instead of array positions.
    pub fn multi_named<M: MultiOutputModule>(
        &mut self,
        module: &M,
        bindings: &[(&str, NodeId)],
    ) -> Result<std::collections::BTreeMap<String, NodeId>, BindingError> {
        let outputs = self.multi(module, bindings)?;
        Ok(module
            .contract()
            .outputs
            .iter()
            .zip(outputs)
            .map(|(port, node)| (port.name.to_owned(), node))
            .collect())
    }

    /// A finite scan, not a proof for an unbounded recurrent system.
    pub fn scan<M: MultiOutputModule>(
        &mut self,
        transition: &M,
        initial_state: NodeId,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<FixedScan, BindingError> {
        let ports = &transition.contract().inputs;
        if ports.len() == 2 && ports[0].name == "state" && ports[1].name == "input" {
            self.check_input(initial_state, "state", &ports[0].port)?;
            for (step, &input) in inputs.iter().enumerate() {
                self.check_input(input, &format!("input[{step}]"), &ports[1].port)?;
            }
        }
        self.graph
            .scan_fixed(transition, initial_state, inputs)
            .map_err(|source| {
                self.failed(
                    "next_state",
                    "bounded state-transition contract",
                    Some(source),
                )
            })
    }
}

impl ProofGoal {
    /// Make the source assumptions explicit; they are never inferred as facts.
    pub fn nonnegative(name: impl Into<String>, output: NodeId, assumptions: Vec<NodeId>) -> Self {
        Self {
            name: name.into(),
            output,
            kind: ProofGoalKind::Nonnegative { assumptions },
        }
    }

    pub fn bounded_above(name: impl Into<String>, lower: NodeId, output: NodeId) -> Self {
        Self {
            name: name.into(),
            output,
            kind: ProofGoalKind::Predicate(Predicate::pointwise_le(
                ValueRef::Node(lower),
                ValueRef::Output,
            )),
        }
    }

    /// Return an independently generated theorem, without claiming it checked.
    pub fn generate_source(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        checker: &LeanProofEngine,
    ) -> Result<LeanProgram, ObligationError> {
        checker
            .generate_goal(graph, self)
            .map_err(|source| ObligationError {
                theorem: format!("architecture_property_{}", self.name),
                source,
            })
    }

    /// Check the Lean file and its transitive axiom dependencies.
    pub fn certify(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        checker: &LeanProofEngine,
        path: &Path,
    ) -> Result<(CheckedLean, LeanAxiomAudit), ObligationError> {
        let program = self.generate_source(graph, checker)?;
        checker
            .verify_certified(&program, path)
            .map_err(|source| ObligationError {
                theorem: format!("architecture_property_{}", self.name),
                source,
            })
    }
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/cuda.rs
//! CUDA Driver API bindings loaded from the system NVIDIA driver at runtime.
//! GPU kernels execute only as CUDA Graph nodes on an explicit non-blocking stream.
//! Legacy/default streams, direct standalone kernel launches and silent fallbacks
//! are forbidden. Host transfers also use this explicit stream.

/// Host-wall readback decomposition, not CUDA device-event timing.
/// The stream is already synchronized by GpuExecution::replay().
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]
pub(crate) struct CudaD2hTiming {
    pub enqueue: std::time::Duration,
    pub synchronize: std::time::Duration,
    pub host_copy: std::time::Duration,
    pub transfers: usize,
    pub bytes: usize,
}

#[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
mod platform {
    use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};
    use std::ffi::{CString, c_char, c_int, c_uint, c_void};
    use std::mem::transmute_copy;
    use std::ptr;

    use super::super::gpu::GpuError;
    use super::CudaD2hTiming;
    use std::time::Instant;

    #[link(name = "dl")]
    unsafe extern "C" {
        fn dlopen(filename: *const c_char, flags: c_int) -> *mut c_void;
        fn dlsym(handle: *mut c_void, symbol: *const c_char) -> *mut c_void;
        fn dlclose(handle: *mut c_void) -> c_int;
    }

    const RTLD_NOW: c_int = 2;
    const CU_STREAM_NON_BLOCKING: c_uint = 1;
    const CU_STREAM_CAPTURE_MODE_THREAD_LOCAL: c_int = 1;
    const CU_EVENT_DEFAULT: c_uint = 0;

    // Runtime-only binary32 domain check; never advertised as a Lean proof.
    // Integer bit tests avoid FTZ and preserve the host's signed-zero rule.
    // The kernel launches exclusively during capture into a CUDA Graph.
    // A single CUDA Graph kernel checks one bucket of arbitrarily shaped
    // tensors. Entries are (device pointer, element count, domain mask) in
    // unsigned 64-bit words; all FP32 classification is bitwise.
    const DOMAIN_GUARD_PTX: &str = r#"
.version 7.0
.target sm_52
.address_size 64

.visible .entry vn_domain_guard(
    .param .u64 descriptors,
    .param .u64 flag,
    .param .u32 first
)
{
    .reg .pred %p<10>;
    .reg .b32 %r<16>;
    .reg .b64 %rd<14>;
    ld.param.u64 %rd1, [descriptors];
    ld.param.u64 %rd2, [flag];
    ld.param.u32 %r1, [first];
    mov.u32 %r2, %ctaid.y;
    add.u32 %r3, %r1, %r2;
    mul.wide.u32 %rd3, %r3, 24;
    add.u64 %rd4, %rd1, %rd3;
    ld.global.u64 %rd5, [%rd4];
    add.u64 %rd6, %rd4, 8;
    ld.global.u64 %rd7, [%rd6];
    add.u64 %rd8, %rd4, 16;
    ld.global.u64 %rd9, [%rd8];
    mov.u32 %r4, %tid.x;
    mov.u32 %r5, %ctaid.x;
    mov.u32 %r6, %ntid.x;
    mad.lo.u32 %r7, %r5, %r6, %r4;
    cvt.u64.u32 %rd10, %r7;
    setp.ge.u64 %p1, %rd10, %rd7;
    @%p1 bra DONE;
    mul.wide.u32 %rd11, %r7, 4;
    add.u64 %rd12, %rd5, %rd11;
    ld.global.u32 %r8, [%rd12];
    and.b32 %r9, %r8, 0x7f800000;
    setp.eq.u32 %p2, %r9, 0x7f800000;
    and.b32 %r10, %r8, 0x80000000;
    and.b32 %r11, %r8, 0x7fffffff;
    setp.ne.u32 %p3, %r10, 0;
    setp.ne.u32 %p4, %r11, 0;
    and.pred %p5, %p3, %p4;
    setp.ne.u64 %p6, %rd9, 0;
    and.pred %p7, %p5, %p6;
    or.pred %p8, %p2, %p7;
    mov.u32 %r12, 1;
    @%p8 atom.global.or.b32 %r13, [%rd2], %r12;
DONE:
    ret;
}
"#;

    // An architecture-neutral transfer kernel: 2D grid's Y selects a
    // descriptor, X copies FP32 *bits* without arithmetic or conversion.
    // Only plans without read/write aliasing are permitted by the caller.
    const FEEDBACK_BATCH_PTX: &str = r#"
.version 7.0
.target sm_52
.address_size 64

.visible .entry vn_feedback_batch(
    .param .u64 descriptors,
    .param .u32 first
)
{
    .reg .pred %p<2>;
    .reg .b32 %r<7>;
    .reg .b64 %rd<14>;
    ld.param.u64 %rd1, [descriptors];
    ld.param.u32 %r1, [first];
    mov.u32 %r2, %ctaid.y;
    add.u32 %r3, %r1, %r2;
    mul.wide.u32 %rd2, %r3, 24;
    add.u64 %rd3, %rd1, %rd2;
    ld.global.u64 %rd4, [%rd3];
    add.u64 %rd5, %rd3, 8;
    ld.global.u64 %rd6, [%rd5];
    add.u64 %rd7, %rd3, 16;
    ld.global.u64 %rd8, [%rd7];
    mov.u32 %r4, %tid.x;
    mov.u32 %r5, %ctaid.x;
    mov.u32 %r6, %ntid.x;
    mad.lo.u32 %r2, %r5, %r6, %r4;
    cvt.u64.u32 %rd9, %r2;
    setp.ge.u64 %p1, %rd9, %rd8;
    @%p1 bra DONE;
    mul.wide.u32 %rd10, %r2, 4;
    add.u64 %rd11, %rd6, %rd10;
    ld.global.u32 %r3, [%rd11];
    add.u64 %rd12, %rd4, %rd10;
    st.global.u32 [%rd12], %r3;
DONE:
    ret;
}
"#;

    // Bucket dissimilar sizes so tiny tensors never inherit the launch
    // width of the largest tensor. Groups are disjoint; starts index the
    // packed descriptor table. Kernel launches remain inside CUDA Graph.
    type TransferBucket = (u32, u32, u32);
    type TransferPlan = (Vec<usize>, Vec<TransferBucket>);

    fn transfer_buckets(lengths: &[usize]) -> Result<TransferPlan, GpuError> {
        let mut order = (0..lengths.len()).collect::<Vec<_>>();
        order.sort_by_key(|&i| lengths[i].next_power_of_two());
        let mut buckets = Vec::new();
        let mut first = 0;
        while first < order.len() {
            let key = lengths[order[first]].next_power_of_two();
            let mut end = first + 1;
            while end < order.len() && lengths[order[end]].next_power_of_two() == key {
                end += 1;
            }
            for start in (first..end).step_by(65_535) {
                let stop = end.min(start + 65_535);
                let biggest = lengths[order[stop - 1]];
                let x = u32::try_from(biggest.div_ceil(256))
                    .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: biggest })?;
                buckets.push((
                    u32::try_from(start)
                        .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: start })?,
                    u32::try_from(stop - start).map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize {
                        elements: stop - start,
                    })?,
                    x,
                ));
            }
            first = end;
        }
        Ok((order, buckets))
    }

    fn descriptor_bytes(entries: &[[u64; 3]]) -> Vec<u8> {
        entries
            .iter()
            .flat_map(|triple| triple.iter().flat_map(|v| v.to_ne_bytes()))
            .collect()
    }

    struct Library(*mut c_void);

    impl Library {
        fn open() -> Result<Self, GpuError> {
            // The host driver, NOT the CUDA toolkit's stub library, provides
            // libcuda.so.1. NixOS exposes its kernel-matched driver under
            // /run/opengl-driver/lib, which may be absent from the dynamic
            // loader search path inside nix develop.
            for name in [c"libcuda.so.1", c"/run/opengl-driver/lib/libcuda.so.1"] {
                // SAFETY: each candidate is a NUL-terminated static string.
                let handle = unsafe { dlopen(name.as_ptr(), RTLD_NOW) };
                if !handle.is_null() {
                    return Ok(Self(handle));
                }
            }
            Err(GpuError::Driver(
                "could not load host libcuda.so.1 (also tried /run/opengl-driver/lib/libcuda.so.1); check the NVIDIA driver and its library path".into(),
            ))
        }

        fn function<T: Copy>(&self, name: &'static str) -> Result<T, GpuError> {
            let cname = CString::new(name)
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::Driver("invalid CUDA symbol name".into()))?;
            // SAFETY: handle is live and cname is NUL-terminated.
            let symbol = unsafe { dlsym(self.0, cname.as_ptr()) };
            if symbol.is_null() {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(format!("missing CUDA symbol {name}")));
            }
            if std::mem::size_of::<T>() != std::mem::size_of::<*mut c_void>() {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "CUDA symbol has an invalid ABI size".into(),
                ));
            }
            // SAFETY: each caller chooses T to match the exact CUDA C ABI.
            Ok(unsafe { transmute_copy(&symbol) })
        }
    }

    impl Drop for Library {
        fn drop(&mut self) {
            // SAFETY: the handle was returned by dlopen and is owned by us.
            unsafe { dlclose(self.0) };
        }
    }

    type Handle = *mut c_void;
    type DevicePtr = u64;
    type ResultCode = c_int;

    struct Functions {
        init: unsafe extern "C" fn(c_uint) -> ResultCode,
        device_get: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut c_int, c_int) -> ResultCode,
        primary_retain: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut Handle, c_int) -> ResultCode,
        primary_release: unsafe extern "C" fn(c_int) -> ResultCode,
        context_push: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle) -> ResultCode,
        context_pop: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut Handle) -> ResultCode,
        module_load: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut Handle, *const c_void) -> ResultCode,
        module_unload: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle) -> ResultCode,
        module_function: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut Handle, Handle, *const c_char) -> ResultCode,
        mem_allocate: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut DevicePtr, usize) -> ResultCode,
        mem_free: unsafe extern "C" fn(DevicePtr) -> ResultCode,
        pinned_allocate: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut *mut c_void, usize) -> ResultCode,
        pinned_free: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut c_void) -> ResultCode,
        host_to_device: unsafe extern "C" fn(DevicePtr, *const c_void, usize, Handle) -> ResultCode,
        device_to_host: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut c_void, DevicePtr, usize, Handle) -> ResultCode,
        device_to_device: unsafe extern "C" fn(DevicePtr, DevicePtr, usize, Handle) -> ResultCode,
        device_memset_u32: unsafe extern "C" fn(DevicePtr, c_uint, usize, Handle) -> ResultCode,
        stream_create: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut Handle, c_uint) -> ResultCode,
        stream_destroy: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle) -> ResultCode,
        stream_sync: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle) -> ResultCode,
        stream_capture_begin: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle, c_int) -> ResultCode,
        stream_capture_end: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle, *mut Handle) -> ResultCode,
        graph_instantiate: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut Handle, Handle, u64) -> ResultCode,
        graph_launch: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle, Handle) -> ResultCode,
        graph_destroy: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle) -> ResultCode,
        graph_exec_destroy: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle) -> ResultCode,
        event_create: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut Handle, c_uint) -> ResultCode,
        event_record: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle, Handle) -> ResultCode,
        event_sync: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle) -> ResultCode,
        event_elapsed: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut f32, Handle, Handle) -> ResultCode,
        event_destroy: unsafe extern "C" fn(Handle) -> ResultCode,
        launch: unsafe extern "C" fn(
            Handle,
            c_uint,
            c_uint,
            c_uint,
            c_uint,
            c_uint,
            c_uint,
            c_uint,
            Handle,
            *mut *mut c_void,
            *mut *mut c_void,
        ) -> ResultCode,
    }

    impl Functions {
        fn load(lib: &Library) -> Result<Self, GpuError> {
            Ok(Self {
                init: lib.function("cuInit")?,
                device_get: lib.function("cuDeviceGet")?,
                primary_retain: lib.function("cuDevicePrimaryCtxRetain")?,
                primary_release: lib.function("cuDevicePrimaryCtxRelease")?,
                context_push: lib.function("cuCtxPushCurrent_v2")?,
                context_pop: lib.function("cuCtxPopCurrent_v2")?,
                module_load: lib.function("cuModuleLoadData")?,
                module_unload: lib.function("cuModuleUnload")?,
                module_function: lib.function("cuModuleGetFunction")?,
                mem_allocate: lib.function("cuMemAlloc_v2")?,
                mem_free: lib.function("cuMemFree_v2")?,
                pinned_allocate: lib.function("cuMemAllocHost_v2")?,
                pinned_free: lib.function("cuMemFreeHost")?,
                host_to_device: lib.function("cuMemcpyHtoDAsync_v2")?,
                device_to_host: lib.function("cuMemcpyDtoHAsync_v2")?,
                device_to_device: lib.function("cuMemcpyDtoDAsync_v2")?,
                device_memset_u32: lib.function("cuMemsetD32Async")?,
                stream_create: lib.function("cuStreamCreate")?,
                stream_destroy: lib.function("cuStreamDestroy_v2")?,
                stream_sync: lib.function("cuStreamSynchronize")?,
                // CUDA Driver API: the unversioned cuStreamBeginCapture takes ONE
                // argument. We need the two-argument v2 ABI (mode included).
                stream_capture_begin: lib.function("cuStreamBeginCapture_v2")?,
                stream_capture_end: lib.function("cuStreamEndCapture")?,
                graph_instantiate: lib.function("cuGraphInstantiateWithFlags")?,
                graph_launch: lib.function("cuGraphLaunch")?,
                graph_destroy: lib.function("cuGraphDestroy")?,
                graph_exec_destroy: lib.function("cuGraphExecDestroy")?,
                event_create: lib.function("cuEventCreate")?,
                event_record: lib.function("cuEventRecord")?,
                event_sync: lib.function("cuEventSynchronize")?,
                event_elapsed: lib.function("cuEventElapsedTime")?,
                event_destroy: lib.function("cuEventDestroy_v2")?,
                launch: lib.function("cuLaunchKernel")?,
            })
        }
    }

    fn check(function: &'static str, code: ResultCode) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        if code == 0 {
            Ok(())
        } else {
            Err(GpuError::Cuda { function, code })
        }
    }

    struct ContextGuard {
        pop: unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut Handle) -> ResultCode,
        expected: Handle,
    }

    impl Drop for ContextGuard {
        fn drop(&mut self) {
            let mut popped = ptr::null_mut();
            // SAFETY: this guard exists only after a successful push on this thread.
            let code = unsafe { (self.pop)(&mut popped) };
            debug_assert_eq!(code, 0);
            debug_assert_eq!(popped, self.expected);
        }
    }

    // A pinned allocation can be reused only after its previous async
    // transfer has completed on the session's explicit stream.
    struct PinnedBuffer {
        address: *mut c_void,
        capacity: usize,
    }

    /// Owns the stream, PTX module, device allocations and a retained reference
    /// to the shared primary CUDA context. Each session retains/releases once.
    /// The library is dropped last, after all CUDA handles are released.
    pub(crate) struct CudaSession {
        functions: Functions,
        device: c_int,
        context: Handle,
        module: Handle,
        allocations: Vec<(DevicePtr, usize)>,
        // Allocations are stable for the session lifetime. Keep O(log n)
        // preflight lookup while retaining reverse allocation-order teardown.
        allocation_capacity: BTreeMap<DevicePtr, usize>,
        staging_pending: Vec<PinnedBuffer>,
        staging_available: Vec<PinnedBuffer>,
        kernels: BTreeMap<String, Handle>,
        stream: Handle,
        graph: Handle,
        graph_exec: Handle,
        // Reusable CUDA Graph for stable feedback D2D copies, independent
        // from the main compute graph. No default stream or host staging.
        feedback_graph: Handle,
        feedback_graph_exec: Handle,
        feedback_plan: Vec<(DevicePtr, DevicePtr, usize)>,
        feedback_module: Handle,
        feedback_kernel: Handle,
        feedback_descriptors: DevicePtr,
        feedback_descriptor_capacity: usize,
        // Separate descriptor/graph cache for architecture-neutral packed
        // readback. Never evict the recurrent feedback graph.
        readback_graph: Handle,
        readback_graph_exec: Handle,
        readback_plan: Vec<(DevicePtr, DevicePtr, usize)>,
        readback_descriptors: DevicePtr,
        readback_descriptor_capacity: usize,
        readback_device_buffer: DevicePtr,
        readback_device_capacity: usize,
        // Independent reusable CUDA Graph for scatter after packed H2D.
        upload_graph: Handle,
        upload_graph_exec: Handle,
        upload_plan: Vec<(DevicePtr, DevicePtr, usize)>,
        upload_descriptors: DevicePtr,
        upload_descriptor_capacity: usize,
        upload_device_buffer: DevicePtr,
        upload_device_capacity: usize,
        // A separate, reusable guard Graph checks all runtime-domain
        // obligations before any state-feedback copies are launched.
        guard_module: Handle,
        guard_kernel: Handle,
        guard_flag: DevicePtr,
        guard_graph: Handle,
        guard_graph_exec: Handle,
        guard_plan: Vec<(DevicePtr, usize, bool)>,
        guard_descriptors: DevicePtr,
        guard_descriptor_capacity: usize,
        capturing: bool,
        _library: Library,
    }

    impl CudaSession {
        fn enter_context(&self) -> Result<ContextGuard, GpuError> {
            // SAFETY: the context is owned by this session and remains live.
            check("cuCtxPushCurrent_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.context_push)(self.context)
            })?;
            Ok(ContextGuard {
                pop: self.functions.context_pop,
                expected: self.context,
            })
        }

        fn pop_context(&self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            let mut popped = ptr::null_mut();
            // SAFETY: callers only pop a context previously pushed on this thread.
            check("cuCtxPopCurrent_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.context_pop)(&mut popped)
            })?;
            if popped != self.context {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "CUDA popped a different context than the session owns".into(),
                ));
            }
            Ok(())
        }

        pub fn new(ptx: &[u8]) -> Result<Self, GpuError> {
            let library = Library::open()?;
            let functions = Functions::load(&library)?;
            // SAFETY: CUDA has been dynamically loaded with matching ABI.
            check("cuInit", unsafe { (functions.init)(0) })?;
            let mut device = 0;
            // SAFETY: device is a valid writable pointer.
            check("cuDeviceGet", unsafe {
                (functions.device_get)(&mut device, 0)
            })?;
            // The primary context is shared by all sessions on this device.
            // Unlike cuCtxCreate, retain does not push it on this thread.
            let mut context = ptr::null_mut();
            check("cuDevicePrimaryCtxRetain", unsafe {
                (functions.primary_retain)(&mut context, device)
            })?;
            if context.is_null() {
                // A successful retain must be balanced even for a bad handle.
                unsafe { (functions.primary_release)(device) };
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "CUDA returned a null primary context".into(),
                ));
            }
            let mut session = Self {
                functions,
                device,
                context,
                module: ptr::null_mut(),
                allocations: Vec::new(),
                allocation_capacity: BTreeMap::new(),
                staging_pending: Vec::new(),
                staging_available: Vec::new(),
                kernels: BTreeMap::new(),
                stream: ptr::null_mut(),
                graph: ptr::null_mut(),
                graph_exec: ptr::null_mut(),
                feedback_graph: ptr::null_mut(),
                feedback_graph_exec: ptr::null_mut(),
                feedback_plan: Vec::new(),
                feedback_module: ptr::null_mut(),
                feedback_kernel: ptr::null_mut(),
                feedback_descriptors: 0,
                feedback_descriptor_capacity: 0,
                readback_graph: ptr::null_mut(),
                readback_graph_exec: ptr::null_mut(),
                readback_plan: Vec::new(),
                readback_descriptors: 0,
                readback_descriptor_capacity: 0,
                readback_device_buffer: 0,
                readback_device_capacity: 0,
                upload_graph: ptr::null_mut(),
                upload_graph_exec: ptr::null_mut(),
                upload_plan: Vec::new(),
                upload_descriptors: 0,
                upload_descriptor_capacity: 0,
                upload_device_buffer: 0,
                upload_device_capacity: 0,
                guard_module: ptr::null_mut(),
                guard_kernel: ptr::null_mut(),
                guard_flag: 0,
                guard_graph: ptr::null_mut(),
                guard_graph_exec: ptr::null_mut(),
                guard_plan: Vec::new(),
                guard_descriptors: 0,
                guard_descriptor_capacity: 0,
                capturing: false,
                _library: library,
            };
            // This guard is dropped before session teardown on any error.
            let _context = session.enter_context()?;
            let bytes = CString::new(ptx)
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::Driver("PTX contains interior NUL byte".into()))?;
            // SAFETY: PTX has an extra terminating NUL and lives through the call.
            check("cuModuleLoadData", unsafe {
                (session.functions.module_load)(
                    &mut session.module,
                    bytes.as_ptr().cast::<c_void>(),
                )
            })?;
            // Never pass 0/CU_STREAM_LEGACY/CU_STREAM_PER_THREAD as a launch stream.
            // No fallback: require an explicitly allocated non-blocking stream.
            check("cuStreamCreate", unsafe {
                (session.functions.stream_create)(&mut session.stream, CU_STREAM_NON_BLOCKING)
            })?;
            if session.stream.is_null() {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "CUDA returned a null stream handle".into(),
                ));
            }

            // _context pops the retained primary context after setup. Sessions
            // share a device context but never share stream/module ownership.
            Ok(session)
        }

        pub fn allocate(&mut self, elements: usize) -> Result<DevicePtr, GpuError> {
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            let bytes = elements
                .checked_mul(std::mem::size_of::<f32>())
                .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements })?;
            let mut address = 0;
            // SAFETY: address is writable, CUDA manages allocated device memory.
            check("cuMemAlloc_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.mem_allocate)(&mut address, bytes)
            })?;
            self.allocations.push((address, elements));
            self.allocation_capacity.insert(address, elements);
            Ok(address)
        }

        /// Allocate independent non-overlapping F32 tensors inside one
        /// owned CUDA allocation. CUDA Graph kernels still receive ordinary
        /// device addresses. Only the slab base pointer is freed on drop.
        pub fn allocate_batch(&mut self, sizes: &[usize]) -> Result<Vec<DevicePtr>, GpuError> {
            if sizes.is_empty() {
                return Ok(Vec::new());
            }
            // Check every size/offset before asking the driver to allocate.
            let mut offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sizes.len());
            let mut total = 0usize;
            for &elements in sizes {
                if elements == 0 {
                    return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements });
                }
                offsets.push(total);
                total = total
                    .checked_add(elements)
                    .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements })?;
            }
            total
                .checked_mul(std::mem::size_of::<f32>())
                .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: total })?;
            let base = self.allocate(total)?;
            let addresses = offsets
                .into_iter()
                .map(|offset| {
                    let bytes = offset
                        .checked_mul(std::mem::size_of::<f32>())
                        .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: offset })?;
                    let bytes = u64::try_from(bytes)
                        .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: offset })?;
                    base.checked_add(bytes)
                        .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: offset })
                })
                .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, GpuError>>()?;
            // Preserve *logical per-tensor bounds*. Using only the original
            // slab capacity would allow a faulty kernel to write into the
            // next tensor without being rejected by require_allocation().
            for (&address, &elements) in addresses.iter().zip(sizes) {
                self.allocation_capacity.insert(address, elements);
            }
            Ok(addresses)
        }

        /// Check the actual device allocations backing a logical memory
        /// contract before graph capture. This is a preflight check, not an
        /// assertion about LLVM/PTX's machine-level memory accesses.
        pub fn require_allocation(
            &self,
            address: DevicePtr,
            elements: usize,
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            // Find the containing logical tensor view. An allocation slab
            // registers each tensor extent independently, so preflight
            // cannot accidentally authorize access to its neighbour.
            // Ordinary allocations and packed staging buffers each register
            // a single full-size view, including valid interior slices.
            let valid = self
                .allocation_capacity
                .range(..=address)
                .next_back()
                .is_some_and(|(&base, &capacity)| {
                    let offset = address - base;
                    offset % 4 == 0
                        && (offset / 4) <= capacity as u64
                        && elements <= capacity - (offset / 4) as usize
                });
            if !valid {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "CUDA kernel memory contract references an unallocated or undersized buffer"
                        .into(),
                ));
            }
            Ok(())
        }

        // Find the smallest completed allocation that fits, or allocate one.
        // Never recycle in-flight buffers: async CUDA copies still read them.
        fn staging_buffer(&mut self, bytes: usize) -> Result<PinnedBuffer, GpuError> {
            let best = self
                .staging_available
                .iter()
                .enumerate()
                .filter(|(_, entry)| entry.capacity >= bytes)
                .min_by_key(|(_, entry)| entry.capacity)
                .map(|(index, _)| index);
            if let Some(index) = best {
                return Ok(self.staging_available.swap_remove(index));
            }
            let mut address = ptr::null_mut();
            check("cuMemAllocHost_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.pinned_allocate)(&mut address, bytes)
            })?;
            if address.is_null() {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "CUDA returned null pinned allocation".into(),
                ));
            }
            Ok(PinnedBuffer {
                address,
                capacity: bytes,
            })
        }

        // Packed metadata is never interpreted as f32. The transfer is
        // staged in pinned host memory until the non-blocking stream sync.
        fn upload_descriptor_bytes(
            &mut self,
            address: DevicePtr,
            bytes: &[u8],
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            let staging = self.staging_buffer(bytes.len())?;
            unsafe {
                ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(bytes.as_ptr(), staging.address.cast::<u8>(), bytes.len())
            };
            let pinned = staging.address;
            self.staging_pending.push(staging);
            check("cuMemcpyHtoDAsync_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.host_to_device)(address, pinned, bytes.len(), self.stream)
            })
        }

        /// One pinned H2D DMA followed by a reusable CUDA Graph that scatters
        /// F32 bit patterns to original input allocations. No FP32 arithmetic.
        pub fn copy_f32_batch_to_device_packed(
            &mut self,
            transfers: &[(DevicePtr, &[f32])],
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            if transfers.is_empty() {
                return Ok(());
            }
            // Preflight everything before the first transfer.
            let mut total = 0usize;
            let mut spans = Vec::with_capacity(transfers.len());
            for &(address, values) in transfers {
                self.require_allocation(address, values.len())?;
                if values.is_empty() || values.len() > i32::MAX as usize {
                    return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedSize {
                        elements: values.len(),
                    });
                }
                spans.push((address, total, values));
                total = total
                    .checked_add(values.len())
                    .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: total })?;
            }
            let bytes = total
                .checked_mul(std::mem::size_of::<f32>())
                .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: total })?;
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            if total > self.upload_device_capacity {
                self.upload_device_buffer = self.allocate(total)?;
                self.upload_device_capacity = total;
            }
            let staging = self.staging_buffer(bytes)?;
            for &(_, offset, values) in &spans {
                // SAFETY: checked offsets and lengths fit the pinned buffer.
                unsafe {
                    ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(
                        values.as_ptr(),
                        staging.address.cast::<f32>().add(offset),
                        values.len(),
                    )
                };
            }
            let pinned = staging.address;
            self.staging_pending.push(staging);
            check("cuMemcpyHtoDAsync_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.host_to_device)(
                    self.upload_device_buffer,
                    pinned,
                    bytes,
                    self.stream,
                )
            })?;
            let mut copies = Vec::with_capacity(spans.len());
            for &(dest, offset, values) in &spans {
                let src = self
                    .upload_device_buffer
                    .checked_add((offset * std::mem::size_of::<f32>()) as u64)
                    .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: offset })?;
                copies.push((dest, src, values.len()));
            }
            self.launch_upload_scatter(&copies)?;
            self.flush_input_copies()
        }

        /// Stage input bytes in page-locked memory and enqueue on our explicit
        /// non-blocking stream. No buffer is recycled before synchronization.
        pub fn copy_to_device(
            &mut self,
            address: DevicePtr,
            values: &[f32],
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            let bytes = std::mem::size_of_val(values);
            let staging = self.staging_buffer(bytes)?;
            // SAFETY: staging has capacity for values.len() f32s.
            unsafe {
                ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(
                    values.as_ptr(),
                    staging.address.cast::<f32>(),
                    values.len(),
                )
            };
            // Keep the staging allocation alive even if enqueueing fails:
            // CUDA may have observed it before returning an error.
            let pinned = staging.address;
            self.staging_pending.push(staging);
            check("cuMemcpyHtoDAsync_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.host_to_device)(address, pinned, bytes, self.stream)
            })
        }

        /// State feedback happens on the existing explicit non-blocking stream.
        /// It is not part of graph capture and never round-trips through the host.
        pub fn copy_device_to_device(
            &mut self,
            destination: DevicePtr,
            source: DevicePtr,
            elements: usize,
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            self.require_allocation(destination, elements)?;
            self.require_allocation(source, elements)?;
            let bytes = elements
                .checked_mul(std::mem::size_of::<f32>())
                .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements })?;
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            check("cuMemcpyDtoDAsync_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.device_to_device)(destination, source, bytes, self.stream)
            })
        }

        /// Check actual output domains on GPU and read only one status word.
        /// False means at least one FP32 NaN, Infinity, or (if requested)
        /// strictly negative nonzero value. Negative zero is accepted.
        /// The status is initialized before *every* replay. This is a
        /// runtime hardware check, not a static proof or semantic-IR kernel.
        pub fn validate_output_domains(
            &mut self,
            sources: &[(DevicePtr, usize, bool)],
        ) -> Result<bool, GpuError> {
            if sources.is_empty() {
                return Ok(true);
            }
            if self.capturing {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "cannot validate feedback while CUDA Graph capture is active".into(),
                ));
            }
            // A published graph owns an immutable descriptor table, and
            // allocations cannot be freed before CudaSession teardown.
            // Only a changed plan needs another full host preflight.
            let rebuild = self.guard_plan.as_slice() != sources || self.guard_graph_exec.is_null();
            if rebuild {
                for &(address, elements, _) in sources {
                    self.require_allocation(address, elements)?;
                    if elements == 0 || elements > i32::MAX as usize {
                        return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements });
                    }
                }
            }
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            if self.guard_module.is_null() {
                let source = CString::new(DOMAIN_GUARD_PTX)
                    .map_err(|_| GpuError::Driver("domain guard PTX contains NUL".into()))?;
                check("cuModuleLoadData", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.module_load)(
                        &mut self.guard_module,
                        source.as_ptr().cast::<c_void>(),
                    )
                })?;
                check("cuModuleGetFunction", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.module_function)(
                        &mut self.guard_kernel,
                        self.guard_module,
                        c"vn_domain_guard".as_ptr(),
                    )
                })?;
                self.guard_flag = self.allocate(1)?;
            }
            if rebuild {
                self.synchronize()?;
                if !self.guard_graph_exec.is_null() {
                    check("cuGraphExecDestroy", unsafe {
                        (self.functions.graph_exec_destroy)(self.guard_graph_exec)
                    })?;
                    self.guard_graph_exec = ptr::null_mut();
                }
                if !self.guard_graph.is_null() {
                    check("cuGraphDestroy", unsafe {
                        (self.functions.graph_destroy)(self.guard_graph)
                    })?;
                    self.guard_graph = ptr::null_mut();
                }
                self.guard_plan.clear();
                let (order, batches) =
                    transfer_buckets(&sources.iter().map(|source| source.1).collect::<Vec<_>>())?;
                let entries = order
                    .iter()
                    .map(|&index| {
                        let (address, elements, nonnegative) = sources[index];
                        [address, elements as u64, u64::from(nonnegative)]
                    })
                    .collect::<Vec<_>>();
                let bytes = descriptor_bytes(&entries);
                let words = bytes.len() / std::mem::size_of::<f32>();
                if words > self.guard_descriptor_capacity {
                    self.guard_descriptors = self.allocate(words)?;
                    self.guard_descriptor_capacity = words;
                }
                self.upload_descriptor_bytes(self.guard_descriptors, &bytes)?;
                // A fresh immutable descriptor table must outlive every
                // capture and replay that addresses it.
                self.synchronize()?;
                check("cuStreamBeginCapture_v2", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.stream_capture_begin)(
                        self.stream,
                        CU_STREAM_CAPTURE_MODE_THREAD_LOCAL,
                    )
                })?;
                self.capturing = true;
                for (start, count, grid) in batches {
                    let mut descriptors = self.guard_descriptors;
                    let mut flag = self.guard_flag;
                    let mut first = start;
                    let mut args = [
                        (&mut descriptors as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                        (&mut flag as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                        (&mut first as *mut u32).cast::<c_void>(),
                    ];
                    check("cuLaunchKernel", unsafe {
                        (self.functions.launch)(
                            self.guard_kernel,
                            grid,
                            count,
                            1,
                            256,
                            1,
                            1,
                            0,
                            self.stream,
                            args.as_mut_ptr(),
                            ptr::null_mut(),
                        )
                    })?;
                }
                let mut graph = ptr::null_mut();
                let ended = check("cuStreamEndCapture", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.stream_capture_end)(self.stream, &mut graph)
                });
                self.capturing = false;
                self.guard_graph = graph;
                ended?;
                if self.guard_graph.is_null() {
                    return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                        "domain guard CUDA Graph capture returned null".into(),
                    ));
                }
                check("cuGraphInstantiateWithFlags", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.graph_instantiate)(
                        &mut self.guard_graph_exec,
                        self.guard_graph,
                        0,
                    )
                })?;
                self.guard_plan.extend_from_slice(sources);
            }
            check("cuMemsetD32Async", unsafe {
                (self.functions.device_memset_u32)(self.guard_flag, 0, 1, self.stream)
            })?;
            check("cuGraphLaunch", unsafe {
                (self.functions.graph_launch)(self.guard_graph_exec, self.stream)
            })?;
            let mut result = [0i32; 1];
            self.copy_indices_to_host(&mut result, self.guard_flag)?;
            Ok(result[0] == 0)
        }

        /// Capture the checked stable device-feedback copy plan once and
        /// replay it on the explicit non-blocking stream. A change in bindings
        /// invalidates the cache and is recaptured after synchronization.
        /// This is a *transfer* graph, not a bypass around the domain gate.
        pub fn launch_feedback_copies(
            &mut self,
            copies: &[(DevicePtr, DevicePtr, usize)],
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            if copies.is_empty() {
                return Ok(());
            }
            if self.capturing {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "feedback is forbidden during CUDA Graph capture".into(),
                ));
            }
            let rebuild =
                self.feedback_plan.as_slice() != copies || self.feedback_graph_exec.is_null();
            if rebuild {
                // The cached graph retains its checked descriptor table for
                // the session lifetime. Changing even one pointer/extent
                // requires fresh size and simultaneous-assignment checks.
                for &(dest, src, elements) in copies {
                    self.require_allocation(dest, elements)?;
                    self.require_allocation(src, elements)?;
                    if elements == 0 || elements > i32::MAX as usize {
                        return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements });
                    }
                }
                let destinations = copies
                    .iter()
                    .map(|&(dst, _, _)| dst)
                    .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();
                if destinations.len() != copies.len()
                    || copies
                        .iter()
                        .any(|&(dst, src, _)| dst != src && destinations.contains(&src))
                {
                    return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                        node: 0,
                        reason: "grouped feedback destinations overlap another transfer",
                    });
                }
            }
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            if self.feedback_module.is_null() {
                let source = CString::new(FEEDBACK_BATCH_PTX)
                    .map_err(|_| GpuError::Driver("feedback kernel PTX contains NUL".into()))?;
                check("cuModuleLoadData", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.module_load)(
                        &mut self.feedback_module,
                        source.as_ptr().cast::<c_void>(),
                    )
                })?;
                check("cuModuleGetFunction", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.module_function)(
                        &mut self.feedback_kernel,
                        self.feedback_module,
                        c"vn_feedback_batch".as_ptr(),
                    )
                })?;
            }
            if rebuild {
                self.synchronize()?;
                if !self.feedback_graph_exec.is_null() {
                    check("cuGraphExecDestroy", unsafe {
                        (self.functions.graph_exec_destroy)(self.feedback_graph_exec)
                    })?;
                    self.feedback_graph_exec = ptr::null_mut();
                }
                if !self.feedback_graph.is_null() {
                    check("cuGraphDestroy", unsafe {
                        (self.functions.graph_destroy)(self.feedback_graph)
                    })?;
                    self.feedback_graph = ptr::null_mut();
                }
                self.feedback_plan.clear();
                let (order, batches) =
                    transfer_buckets(&copies.iter().map(|copy| copy.2).collect::<Vec<_>>())?;
                let entries = order
                    .iter()
                    .map(|&index| {
                        let (dest, source, elements) = copies[index];
                        [dest, source, elements as u64]
                    })
                    .collect::<Vec<_>>();
                let bytes = descriptor_bytes(&entries);
                let words = bytes.len() / std::mem::size_of::<f32>();
                if words > self.feedback_descriptor_capacity {
                    self.feedback_descriptors = self.allocate(words)?;
                    self.feedback_descriptor_capacity = words;
                }
                self.upload_descriptor_bytes(self.feedback_descriptors, &bytes)?;
                self.synchronize()?;
                check("cuStreamBeginCapture_v2", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.stream_capture_begin)(
                        self.stream,
                        CU_STREAM_CAPTURE_MODE_THREAD_LOCAL,
                    )
                })?;
                self.capturing = true;
                for (start, count, grid) in batches {
                    let mut descriptors = self.feedback_descriptors;
                    let mut first = start;
                    let mut args = [
                        (&mut descriptors as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                        (&mut first as *mut u32).cast::<c_void>(),
                    ];
                    check("cuLaunchKernel", unsafe {
                        (self.functions.launch)(
                            self.feedback_kernel,
                            grid,
                            count,
                            1,
                            256,
                            1,
                            1,
                            0,
                            self.stream,
                            args.as_mut_ptr(),
                            ptr::null_mut(),
                        )
                    })?;
                }
                let mut graph = ptr::null_mut();
                let ended = check("cuStreamEndCapture", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.stream_capture_end)(self.stream, &mut graph)
                });
                self.capturing = false;
                self.feedback_graph = graph;
                ended?;
                if self.feedback_graph.is_null() {
                    return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                        "feedback CUDA Graph capture returned null".into(),
                    ));
                }
                check("cuGraphInstantiateWithFlags", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.graph_instantiate)(
                        &mut self.feedback_graph_exec,
                        self.feedback_graph,
                        0,
                    )
                })?;
                self.feedback_plan.extend_from_slice(copies);
            }
            check("cuGraphLaunch", unsafe {
                (self.functions.graph_launch)(self.feedback_graph_exec, self.stream)
            })
        }

        // Keep distinct CUDA Graph caches for feedback and packed readback.
        // The same proven u32 load/store kernel executes in either graph;
        // swaps never escape this call, including on recoverable errors.
        fn launch_readback_pack(
            &mut self,
            copies: &[(DevicePtr, DevicePtr, usize)],
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_graph, &mut self.readback_graph);
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_graph_exec, &mut self.readback_graph_exec);
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_plan, &mut self.readback_plan);
            std::mem::swap(
                &mut self.feedback_descriptors,
                &mut self.readback_descriptors,
            );
            std::mem::swap(
                &mut self.feedback_descriptor_capacity,
                &mut self.readback_descriptor_capacity,
            );
            let result = self.launch_feedback_copies(copies);
            std::mem::swap(
                &mut self.feedback_descriptor_capacity,
                &mut self.readback_descriptor_capacity,
            );
            std::mem::swap(
                &mut self.feedback_descriptors,
                &mut self.readback_descriptors,
            );
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_plan, &mut self.readback_plan);
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_graph_exec, &mut self.readback_graph_exec);
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_graph, &mut self.readback_graph);
            result
        }

        // The same generic bit-copy kernel, but a third cache. Without it
        // alternating host uploads and readbacks rebuilds the transfer graph.
        fn launch_upload_scatter(
            &mut self,
            copies: &[(DevicePtr, DevicePtr, usize)],
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_graph, &mut self.upload_graph);
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_graph_exec, &mut self.upload_graph_exec);
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_plan, &mut self.upload_plan);
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_descriptors, &mut self.upload_descriptors);
            std::mem::swap(
                &mut self.feedback_descriptor_capacity,
                &mut self.upload_descriptor_capacity,
            );
            let result = self.launch_feedback_copies(copies);
            std::mem::swap(
                &mut self.feedback_descriptor_capacity,
                &mut self.upload_descriptor_capacity,
            );
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_descriptors, &mut self.upload_descriptors);
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_plan, &mut self.upload_plan);
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_graph_exec, &mut self.upload_graph_exec);
            std::mem::swap(&mut self.feedback_graph, &mut self.upload_graph);
            result
        }

        /// Opt-in CUDA event measurement of the *same* grouped D2D graph.
        /// This does not replay transfers a second time; it changes the
        /// caller's synchronization point and is unsuitable for throughput
        /// benchmarking. Events use the owned non-blocking stream only.
        pub fn launch_feedback_copies_device_timed(
            &mut self,
            copies: &[(DevicePtr, DevicePtr, usize)],
        ) -> Result<std::time::Duration, GpuError> {
            if copies.is_empty() {
                return Ok(std::time::Duration::ZERO);
            }
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            let mut start = ptr::null_mut();
            check("cuEventCreate", unsafe {
                (self.functions.event_create)(&mut start, CU_EVENT_DEFAULT)
            })?;
            let mut stop = ptr::null_mut();
            if let Err(err) = check("cuEventCreate", unsafe {
                (self.functions.event_create)(&mut stop, CU_EVENT_DEFAULT)
            }) {
                unsafe { (self.functions.event_destroy)(start) };
                return Err(err);
            }
            let result = (|| {
                check("cuEventRecord", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.event_record)(start, self.stream)
                })?;
                self.launch_feedback_copies(copies)?;
                check("cuEventRecord", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.event_record)(stop, self.stream)
                })?;
                check("cuEventSynchronize", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.event_sync)(stop)
                })?;
                let mut elapsed_ms = 0.0f32;
                check("cuEventElapsedTime", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.event_elapsed)(&mut elapsed_ms, start, stop)
                })?;
                Ok(std::time::Duration::from_secs_f64(
                    f64::from(elapsed_ms) / 1000.0,
                ))
            })();
            unsafe {
                (self.functions.event_destroy)(stop);
                (self.functions.event_destroy)(start);
            }
            result
        }

        fn copy_to_host_bytes(
            &mut self,
            out: *mut c_void,
            bytes: usize,
            address: DevicePtr,
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            let staging = self.staging_buffer(bytes)?;
            let pinned = staging.address;
            self.staging_pending.push(staging);
            // SAFETY: pinned staging remains live until synchronization completes.
            check("cuMemcpyDtoHAsync_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.device_to_host)(pinned, address, bytes, self.stream)
            })?;
            self.synchronize()?;
            // SAFETY: the async transfer completed and the caller supplied a
            // writable destination covering exactly `bytes`.
            unsafe { ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(pinned.cast::<u8>(), out.cast::<u8>(), bytes) };
            self.release_completed_staging();
            Ok(())
        }

        /// Queue F32 device-to-host copies into session-owned pinned staging
        /// on the same explicit non-blocking CUDA stream. Synchronize once,
        /// then copy the completed data into ordinary owned host vectors.
        /// Pending pinned buffers remain alive on any enqueue/sync failure,
        /// and are reclaimed only after a successful stream barrier.
        pub fn copy_f32_batch_to_host(
            &mut self,
            transfers: &[(DevicePtr, usize)],
        ) -> Result<Vec<Vec<f32>>, GpuError> {
            self.copy_f32_batch_to_host_profiled(transfers)
                .map(|(values, _)| values)
        }

        pub fn copy_f32_batch_to_host_profiled(
            &mut self,
            transfers: &[(DevicePtr, usize)],
        ) -> Result<(Vec<Vec<f32>>, CudaD2hTiming), GpuError> {
            if transfers.is_empty() {
                return Ok((Vec::new(), CudaD2hTiming::default()));
            }
            // Validate the complete batch before queuing any DMA.
            let byte_counts = transfers
                .iter()
                .map(|&(_, elements)| {
                    elements
                        .checked_mul(std::mem::size_of::<f32>())
                        .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements })
                })
                .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;
            let bytes = byte_counts.iter().try_fold(0usize, |sum, &count| {
                sum.checked_add(count)
                    .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: sum })
            })?;
            let enqueue_started = Instant::now();
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            let mut staged = Vec::with_capacity(transfers.len());
            for (&(address, elements), &bytes) in transfers.iter().zip(&byte_counts) {
                let pinned = self.staging_buffer(bytes)?;
                let pointer = pinned.address;
                self.staging_pending.push(pinned);
                check("cuMemcpyDtoHAsync_v2", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.device_to_host)(pointer, address, bytes, self.stream)
                })?;
                staged.push((pointer, elements));
            }
            let enqueue = enqueue_started.elapsed();
            let sync_started = Instant::now();
            self.synchronize()?;
            let synchronize = sync_started.elapsed();
            let copy_started = Instant::now();
            let mut outputs = Vec::with_capacity(staged.len());
            for (pointer, elements) in staged {
                let mut values = vec![0f32; elements];
                // SAFETY: the copy completed on this stream; staging is
                // pinned and remains owned by staging_pending until release.
                unsafe {
                    ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(pointer.cast::<f32>(), values.as_mut_ptr(), elements)
                };
                outputs.push(values);
            }
            self.release_completed_staging();
            Ok((
                outputs,
                CudaD2hTiming {
                    enqueue,
                    synchronize,
                    host_copy: copy_started.elapsed(),
                    transfers: transfers.len(),
                    bytes,
                },
            ))
        }

        /// Experimental packed readback: a CUDA Graph gathers disjoint
        /// F32 outputs bit-for-bit into one device allocation, then queues
        /// exactly one D2H DMA on the same non-blocking stream.
        /// This never launches a standalone kernel or reorders arithmetic.
        pub fn copy_f32_batch_to_host_packed_profiled(
            &mut self,
            transfers: &[(DevicePtr, usize)],
        ) -> Result<(Vec<Vec<f32>>, CudaD2hTiming), GpuError> {
            if transfers.is_empty() {
                return Ok((Vec::new(), CudaD2hTiming::default()));
            }
            let mut total_elements = 0usize;
            let mut spans = Vec::with_capacity(transfers.len());
            for &(source, elements) in transfers {
                self.require_allocation(source, elements)?;
                if elements > i32::MAX as usize {
                    return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements });
                }
                spans.push((source, total_elements, elements));
                total_elements = total_elements
                    .checked_add(elements)
                    .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements })?;
            }
            if total_elements == 0 {
                return Ok((vec![Vec::new(); transfers.len()], CudaD2hTiming::default()));
            }
            let bytes = total_elements
                .checked_mul(std::mem::size_of::<f32>())
                .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize {
                    elements: total_elements,
                })?;
            let enqueue_started = Instant::now();
            if total_elements > self.readback_device_capacity {
                self.readback_device_buffer = self.allocate(total_elements)?;
                self.readback_device_capacity = total_elements;
            }
            let mut copies = Vec::with_capacity(spans.len());
            for &(src, offset, elements) in &spans {
                if elements == 0 {
                    continue;
                }
                let offset_bytes = (offset * std::mem::size_of::<f32>()) as u64;
                let dst = self
                    .readback_device_buffer
                    .checked_add(offset_bytes)
                    .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: offset })?;
                copies.push((dst, src, elements));
            }
            // Pinned CUDA allocation also requires a current context.
            // Hold it across staging, graph packing, DMA and synchronization.
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            let pinned = self.staging_buffer(bytes)?;
            let pointer = pinned.address;
            self.staging_pending.push(pinned);
            self.launch_readback_pack(&copies)?;
            check("cuMemcpyDtoHAsync_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.device_to_host)(
                    pointer,
                    self.readback_device_buffer,
                    bytes,
                    self.stream,
                )
            })?;
            let enqueue = enqueue_started.elapsed();
            let sync_started = Instant::now();
            self.synchronize()?;
            let synchronize = sync_started.elapsed();
            let copy_started = Instant::now();
            let mut results = Vec::with_capacity(spans.len());
            for (_, offset, elements) in spans {
                let mut values = vec![0f32; elements];
                if elements > 0 {
                    // SAFETY: the graph and DMA have completed on this stream.
                    // The pinned allocation covers all packed tensor slices.
                    unsafe {
                        ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(
                            pointer.cast::<f32>().add(offset),
                            values.as_mut_ptr(),
                            elements,
                        )
                    };
                }
                results.push(values);
            }
            self.release_completed_staging();
            Ok((
                results,
                CudaD2hTiming {
                    enqueue,
                    synchronize,
                    host_copy: copy_started.elapsed(),
                    transfers: 1,
                    bytes,
                },
            ))
        }

        pub fn copy_to_host(
            &mut self,
            out: &mut [f32],
            address: DevicePtr,
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            self.copy_to_host_bytes(
                out.as_mut_ptr().cast::<c_void>(),
                std::mem::size_of_val(out),
                address,
            )
        }

        pub fn copy_indices_to_host(
            &mut self,
            out: &mut [i32],
            address: DevicePtr,
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            self.copy_to_host_bytes(
                out.as_mut_ptr().cast::<c_void>(),
                std::mem::size_of_val(out),
                address,
            )
        }

        // Reuse completed staging buffers instead of allocating/freeing pinned
        // memory on every update_inputs/read_output. The session owns both lists.
        fn release_completed_staging(&mut self) {
            self.staging_available.append(&mut self.staging_pending);
        }

        pub fn flush_input_copies(&mut self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            self.synchronize()?;
            self.release_completed_staging();
            Ok(())
        }

        /// Begin capturing only kernel launches to a CUDA Graph. No allocations,
        /// host copies, or default-stream commands are permitted during capture.
        pub fn begin_graph(&mut self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            if self.capturing || !self.graph.is_null() || !self.graph_exec.is_null() {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver("CUDA Graph already in progress".into()));
            }
            self.flush_input_copies()?;
            // Keep this session context current for the entire capture sequence.
            check("cuCtxPushCurrent_v2", unsafe {
                (self.functions.context_push)(self.context)
            })?;
            // SAFETY: an explicitly created nonblocking stream is current.
            let code = unsafe {
                (self.functions.stream_capture_begin)(
                    self.stream,
                    CU_STREAM_CAPTURE_MODE_THREAD_LOCAL,
                )
            };
            if let Err(err) = check("cuStreamBeginCapture", code) {
                let _ = self.pop_context();
                return Err(err);
            }
            self.capturing = true;
            Ok(())
        }

        /// Finish capture and instantiate an executable graph without launching it.
        pub fn finish_graph(&mut self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            if !self.capturing {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver("CUDA Graph was not started".into()));
            }
            let result = (|| {
                let mut graph = ptr::null_mut();
                // SAFETY: capture runs on the current thread and same CUDA stream.
                let code = unsafe { (self.functions.stream_capture_end)(self.stream, &mut graph) };
                self.capturing = false;
                self.graph = graph;
                check("cuStreamEndCapture", code)?;
                if self.graph.is_null() {
                    return Err(GpuError::Driver("CUDA Graph capture returned null".into()));
                }
                // SAFETY: all captured kernel parameters have been copied by CUDA.
                check("cuGraphInstantiateWithFlags", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.graph_instantiate)(&mut self.graph_exec, self.graph, 0)
                })
            })();
            let pop_result = self.pop_context();
            result?;
            pop_result
        }

        /// Replay an already instantiated graph on the owned non-blocking stream.
        pub fn launch_graph(&self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            self.launch_graph_current_context()
        }

        // For use inside a longer-lived context guard (CUDA-event benchmarks).
        fn launch_graph_current_context(&self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            if self.capturing || self.graph_exec.is_null() {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "CUDA Graph must be instantiated before replay".into(),
                ));
            }
            check("cuGraphLaunch", unsafe {
                (self.functions.graph_launch)(self.graph_exec, self.stream)
            })
        }

        /// Measure graph replay on the CUDA stream with device events.
        pub fn benchmark_graph(
            &self,
            warmup_launches: usize,
            measured_launches: usize,
        ) -> Result<f32, GpuError> {
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            for _ in 0..warmup_launches {
                self.launch_graph_current_context()?;
            }
            self.synchronize()?;

            let mut start = ptr::null_mut();
            check("cuEventCreate", unsafe {
                (self.functions.event_create)(&mut start, CU_EVENT_DEFAULT)
            })?;
            let mut stop = ptr::null_mut();
            if let Err(err) = check("cuEventCreate", unsafe {
                (self.functions.event_create)(&mut stop, CU_EVENT_DEFAULT)
            }) {
                unsafe { (self.functions.event_destroy)(start) };
                return Err(err);
            }

            let result = (|| {
                check("cuEventRecord", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.event_record)(start, self.stream)
                })?;
                for _ in 0..measured_launches {
                    self.launch_graph_current_context()?;
                }
                check("cuEventRecord", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.event_record)(stop, self.stream)
                })?;
                check("cuEventSynchronize", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.event_sync)(stop)
                })?;
                let mut milliseconds = 0.0f32;
                check("cuEventElapsedTime", unsafe {
                    (self.functions.event_elapsed)(&mut milliseconds, start, stop)
                })?;
                Ok(milliseconds)
            })();

            unsafe {
                (self.functions.event_destroy)(stop);
                (self.functions.event_destroy)(start);
            }
            result
        }

        /// Resolve the CUDA function before capture. Lazy lookup/JIT is not
        /// part of the captured stream's execution dependency graph.
        pub fn prepare_kernel(&mut self, name: &str) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            if self.capturing {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "kernel resolution during CUDA Graph capture is forbidden".into(),
                ));
            }
            if self.kernels.contains_key(name) {
                return Ok(());
            }
            let c_name = CString::new(name)
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::Driver("kernel name contains NUL".into()))?;
            let mut function = ptr::null_mut();
            // SAFETY: module is loaded and the C string is NUL terminated.
            check("cuModuleGetFunction", unsafe {
                (self.functions.module_function)(&mut function, self.module, c_name.as_ptr())
            })?;
            self.kernels.insert(name.to_owned(), function);
            Ok(())
        }

        pub fn launch(
            &self,
            name: &str,
            left: DevicePtr,
            right: DevicePtr,
            output: DevicePtr,
            length: usize,
            threads: u32,
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            if !self.capturing {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "direct kernel launch is forbidden; capture a CUDA Graph".into(),
                ));
            }
            let function = *self.kernels.get(name).ok_or_else(|| {
                GpuError::Driver(
                    "kernel function must be resolved before CUDA Graph capture".into(),
                )
            })?;
            let count = i32::try_from(length)
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: length })?;
            let grid = u32::try_from(length.div_ceil(threads as usize))
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: length })?;
            let mut lhs = left;
            let mut rhs = right;
            let mut dst = output;
            let mut n = count;
            let mut args = [
                (&mut lhs as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut rhs as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut dst as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut n as *mut i32).cast::<c_void>(),
            ];
            // SAFETY: each kernel argument points to correctly sized stable
            // storage matching the LLVM kernel signature. The launch itself
            // is asynchronous; synchronize before copying results.
            check("cuLaunchKernel", unsafe {
                (self.functions.launch)(
                    function,
                    grid,
                    1,
                    1,
                    threads,
                    1,
                    1,
                    0,
                    self.stream,
                    args.as_mut_ptr(),
                    ptr::null_mut(),
                )
            })
        }

        pub fn launch3(
            &self,
            name: &str,
            sources: [DevicePtr; 3],
            output: DevicePtr,
            length: usize,
            threads: u32,
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            if !self.capturing {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "direct kernel launch is forbidden; capture a CUDA Graph".into(),
                ));
            }
            let function = *self.kernels.get(name).ok_or_else(|| {
                GpuError::Driver(
                    "kernel function must be resolved before CUDA Graph capture".into(),
                )
            })?;
            let count = i32::try_from(length)
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: length })?;
            let grid = u32::try_from(length.div_ceil(threads as usize))
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: length })?;
            let [mut a, mut b, mut c] = sources;
            let mut dst = output;
            let mut n = count;
            let mut args = [
                (&mut a as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut b as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut c as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut dst as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut n as *mut i32).cast::<c_void>(),
            ];
            check("cuLaunchKernel", unsafe {
                (self.functions.launch)(
                    function,
                    grid,
                    1,
                    1,
                    threads,
                    1,
                    1,
                    0,
                    self.stream,
                    args.as_mut_ptr(),
                    ptr::null_mut(),
                )
            })
        }

        /// Four-source kernel capture. The sole launch is performed on the
        /// session-owned CU_STREAM_NON_BLOCKING while a CUDA Graph is captured.
        pub fn launch4(
            &self,
            name: &str,
            sources: [DevicePtr; 4],
            output: DevicePtr,
            length: usize,
            threads: u32,
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            if !self.capturing {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "direct kernel launch is forbidden; capture a CUDA Graph".into(),
                ));
            }
            let function = *self.kernels.get(name).ok_or_else(|| {
                GpuError::Driver(
                    "kernel function must be resolved before CUDA Graph capture".into(),
                )
            })?;
            let count = i32::try_from(length)
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: length })?;
            let grid = u32::try_from(length.div_ceil(threads as usize))
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: length })?;
            let [mut a, mut b, mut c, mut d] = sources;
            let mut dst = output;
            let mut n = count;
            let mut args = [
                (&mut a as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut b as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut c as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut d as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut dst as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut n as *mut i32).cast::<c_void>(),
            ];
            check("cuLaunchKernel", unsafe {
                (self.functions.launch)(
                    function,
                    grid,
                    1,
                    1,
                    threads,
                    1,
                    1,
                    0,
                    self.stream,
                    args.as_mut_ptr(),
                    ptr::null_mut(),
                )
            })
        }

        /// Capture a bounded two-output pointwise kernel on the owned
        /// non-blocking CUDA stream. Neither output aliases any source.
        pub fn launch4_dual(
            &self,
            name: &str,
            sources: [DevicePtr; 4],
            outputs: [DevicePtr; 2],
            length: usize,
            threads: u32,
        ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            if !self.capturing {
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "direct kernel launch is forbidden; capture a CUDA Graph".into(),
                ));
            }
            let function = *self.kernels.get(name).ok_or_else(|| {
                GpuError::Driver(
                    "kernel function must be resolved before CUDA Graph capture".into(),
                )
            })?;
            let count = i32::try_from(length)
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: length })?;
            let grid = u32::try_from(length.div_ceil(threads as usize))
                .map_err(|_| GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: length })?;
            let [mut a, mut b, mut c, mut d] = sources;
            let [mut extra, mut dst] = outputs;
            let mut n = count;
            let mut args = [
                (&mut a as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut b as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut c as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut d as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut extra as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut dst as *mut DevicePtr).cast::<c_void>(),
                (&mut n as *mut i32).cast::<c_void>(),
            ];
            check("cuLaunchKernel", unsafe {
                (self.functions.launch)(
                    function,
                    grid,
                    1,
                    1,
                    threads,
                    1,
                    1,
                    0,
                    self.stream,
                    args.as_mut_ptr(),
                    ptr::null_mut(),
                )
            })
        }

        pub fn synchronize(&self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
            let _context = self.enter_context()?;
            // SAFETY: stream belongs to this CUDA context; never synchronize legacy.
            check("cuStreamSynchronize", unsafe {
                (self.functions.stream_sync)(self.stream)
            })
        }
    }

    impl Drop for CudaSession {
        fn drop(&mut self) {
            // begin_graph intentionally keeps the context pushed until capture ends.
            let mut context_pushed = self.capturing;
            if !context_pushed && !self.context.is_null() {
                context_pushed = unsafe { (self.functions.context_push)(self.context) } == 0;
            }

            // The stream must complete before releasing graph/module/device/pinned
            // buffers. A failed capture is ended best-effort without replay.
            if self.capturing && !self.stream.is_null() {
                let mut graph = ptr::null_mut();
                // SAFETY: same CUDA stream, no concurrent host access.
                unsafe { (self.functions.stream_capture_end)(self.stream, &mut graph) };
                self.capturing = false;
                if !graph.is_null() {
                    unsafe { (self.functions.graph_destroy)(graph) };
                }
            }
            if !self.stream.is_null() {
                // SAFETY: session owns this stream.
                unsafe { (self.functions.stream_sync)(self.stream) };
            }
            if !self.guard_graph_exec.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.graph_exec_destroy)(self.guard_graph_exec) };
            }
            if !self.guard_graph.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.graph_destroy)(self.guard_graph) };
            }
            if !self.feedback_graph_exec.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.graph_exec_destroy)(self.feedback_graph_exec) };
            }
            if !self.feedback_graph.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.graph_destroy)(self.feedback_graph) };
            }
            if !self.readback_graph_exec.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.graph_exec_destroy)(self.readback_graph_exec) };
            }
            if !self.readback_graph.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.graph_destroy)(self.readback_graph) };
            }
            if !self.upload_graph_exec.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.graph_exec_destroy)(self.upload_graph_exec) };
            }
            if !self.upload_graph.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.graph_destroy)(self.upload_graph) };
            }
            if !self.graph_exec.is_null() {
                // SAFETY: the executable graph is owned by this session.
                unsafe { (self.functions.graph_exec_destroy)(self.graph_exec) };
            }
            if !self.graph.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.graph_destroy)(self.graph) };
            }
            for (address, _) in self.allocations.drain(..).rev() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.mem_free)(address) };
            }
            for host in self
                .staging_pending
                .drain(..)
                .chain(self.staging_available.drain(..))
            {
                unsafe { (self.functions.pinned_free)(host.address) };
            }
            if !self.guard_module.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.module_unload)(self.guard_module) };
            }
            if !self.feedback_module.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.module_unload)(self.feedback_module) };
            }
            if !self.module.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.module_unload)(self.module) };
            }
            if !self.stream.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.stream_destroy)(self.stream) };
            }
            if context_pushed {
                let mut popped = ptr::null_mut();
                unsafe { (self.functions.context_pop)(&mut popped) };
                debug_assert_eq!(popped, self.context);
            }
            // Release exactly one primary-context reference *after* destroying
            // every per-session CUDA object and popping the current context.
            if !self.context.is_null() {
                unsafe { (self.functions.primary_release)(self.device) };
            }
        }
    }
    #[cfg(test)]
    mod batching_tests {
        use super::{descriptor_bytes, transfer_buckets};

        #[test]
        fn buckets_preserve_every_copy_and_bound_wasted_threads() {
            let lengths = [1024, 1, 257, 2, 513, 128, 1025, 4];
            let (order, buckets) = transfer_buckets(&lengths).unwrap();
            assert_eq!(order.len(), lengths.len());
            let mut unique = order.clone();
            unique.sort_unstable();
            assert_eq!(unique, (0..lengths.len()).collect::<Vec<_>>());
            let mut covered = 0;
            for (start, count, blocks) in buckets {
                assert_eq!(start as usize, covered);
                let slice = &order[start as usize..(start + count) as usize];
                let ceiling = lengths[slice[0]].next_power_of_two();
                assert!(
                    slice
                        .iter()
                        .all(|&index| lengths[index].next_power_of_two() == ceiling)
                );
                assert_eq!(
                    blocks as usize,
                    lengths[*slice.last().unwrap()].div_ceil(256)
                );
                assert!(count <= 65_535);
                covered += count as usize;
            }
            assert_eq!(covered, lengths.len());
        }

        #[test]
        fn descriptors_keep_full_pointer_bits_and_exact_lengths() {
            let entries = [
                [0xfeed_beef_dead_cafe, 0x1234_5678_ffff_0000, 4],
                [0, 0x8000_0000_0000_0000, 1025],
            ];
            let bytes = descriptor_bytes(&entries);
            assert_eq!(bytes.len(), entries.len() * 24);
            let reconstructed = bytes
                .chunks_exact(8)
                .map(|b| u64::from_ne_bytes(b.try_into().unwrap()))
                .collect::<Vec<_>>();
            let expected = entries
                .iter()
                .flat_map(|e| e.iter().copied())
                .collect::<Vec<_>>();
            assert_eq!(reconstructed, expected);
        }
    }
}

